{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro","id":1197,"title":"Abrahamic Pantheon? [NECRO]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-02T12:06:28-07:00","id":1197,"title":"Abrahamic Pantheon? [NECRO]","content":"Discussion moved here from the Scion: Origin thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T12:27:32-07:00","id":1212,"title":"","content":"It wasn't even an argument in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal\">original thread</a>, just healthy discussion. At any rate<br /> <br /> I think there should be one. I think it would be cool.<br /> Some arguments are it doesn't have a Pantheon. It was brought up that Vodoun doesn't either. <br /> Other arguments are that it doesn't have the same feel, which I don't really understand","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T12:59:01-07:00","id":1240,"title":"","content":"Before I delve into the discussion, I must ask: what exactly do you mean when talking about the &quot;Abrahamic Pantheon&quot;? Which gods should it have according to you?<br /> <br /> There are some different ideas behind that name, and I would like to know what we're talking about this time.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 11-02-2013, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T13:02:27-07:00","id":1243,"title":"","content":"An Abrahamic Pantheon is tricky. On one hand it doesn't fit into the Pantheon system we have already, screws up the &quot;gods vs titans&quot; thing and of course skews things towards a judeo-christian morality mindset rather than the mythic tales of powerful heroes beating down monsters because they can.. However the current LACK of one is rather disturbing and the &quot;Ankhenaten&quot; theory rubs me the wrong way so bad that I demand a counter argument.<br /> <br /> The closest I ever got to a homebrew solution that didn't equally churn my stomach was based on the Catholic Saints. Real historical figures who lived and died, but through canonization achieved a form of godhood all there own. Of course it doesn't really &quot;address&quot; the issue of the Abrahamic faiths since in it, God isn't actually doing anything to help or hinder the war (yet) save to empower the Saints to act in his stead. But it's the best I've got.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I'M SORRY, I CAN'T HEAR YOU OVER THE SOUND OF HOW MANY MALFEAS CHARMS I HAVE!!!</b><i>~King Crazy Genius</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/345-kandagger","name":"Kandagger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T13:12:29-07:00","id":1252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=1240#post1240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before I delve into the discussion, I must ask: what exactly do you mean when talking about the &quot;Abrahamic Pantheon&quot;? Which gods should it have according to you?<br /> <br /> There are some different ideas behind that name, and I would like to know what we're talking about this time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I was the one who initially brought it up, I don't have any gritty details in mind or anything. It wouldn't needs &quot;Gods&quot;, Archangels could work just as well or Saints (as Scions that ascended) or important Biblical figures (Moses, Noah, Daniel, etc). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kandagger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=1243#post1243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Abrahamic Pantheon is tricky. On one hand it doesn't fit into the Pantheon system we have already, screws up the &quot;gods vs titans&quot; thing and of course skews things towards a judeo-christian morality mindset rather than the mythic tales of powerful heroes beating down monsters because they can.. However the current LACK of one is rather disturbing and the &quot;Ankhenaten&quot; theory rubs me the wrong way so bad that I demand a counter argument.<br /> <br /> The closest I ever got to a homebrew solution that didn't equally churn my stomach was based on the Catholic Saints. Real historical figures who lived and died, but through canonization achieved a form of godhood all there own. Of course it doesn't really &quot;address&quot; the issue of the Abrahamic faiths since in it, God isn't actually doing anything to help or hinder the war (yet) save to empower the Saints to act in his stead. But it's the best I've got.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, like what he said, Saints would work fine.<br /> <br /> But you bring up a good point about Titans, though I'm sure if we rolled ours sleeves up, dove in and got our hands dirty we could drum up a Titan for Judeo-Christian Pantheon","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T13:19:40-07:00","id":1255,"title":"","content":"Basically, the issue is that Scion says &quot;All Myths Are True&quot; and there's a conflict there. Monotheism specifcally says that All Myths Are NOT True. Only <b>their</b> myths are true. So there's a conflict between Abrahamic God and the polytheistic Gods like Odin, Thor, Ares, Shango. If Abrahamic God is right, then he's Legend Infinity. He's all powerful and all knowing. The other Gods are basically just pretenders, and so are the Titans.<br /> <br /> So there's a few soltuions, all of which compromise either a basic assumption of monotheism, or a basic assumption of the game.<br /> <br /> 1) God is really God. He is the ultimate power of the setting, all other Gods are wrong, liars, stupid or pretenders. This renders the entire setting moot, since God could solve everything with a blink of His eye. No conflict, no drama. Scion assumes active Gods, and if God is active and He is All Powerful, He ends the Titan War instantly. Also Titans don't exist, or are really demons, because God is the only God.<br /> <br /> 2) God is NOT really God. He's just an idiot and he's really on the same level as all the other deities. That causes issues because then God is by himself in his &quot;Pantheon&quot; of one. If you want to have other figures in there at Legend 12, suitable for standard Divine Parents, then you have to assume that figures like Jesus, Mary, Lucifer, Gabriel, etc, are <i><b>equal to God</b></i> and that's not following the mythology. Cept maybe Jesus, and that depends on if you believe Jesus <i>is</i> God or if he's the <i>son </i>of God.<br /> <br /> Either one has some pretty big issues. If you want really in-depth discussion, because this comes up a <b>lot</b>, here are some links to the foremost Scion Blog (one of like, two) and some very cogent thoughts on monotheism in Scion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://johnsscionresources.blogspot.com/2011/12/tell-me-all-your-thoughts-on-god.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://johnsscionresources.blogspot.com/2011/12/tell-me-all-your-thoughts-on-god.html\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://johnsscionresources.blogspot.com/2011/12/tell-me-all-your-thoughts-on-god.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://johnsscionresources.blogspot.com/2011/12/tell-me-all-your-thoughts-on-god.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://johnsscionresources.blogspot.com/2012/02/human-spirit.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://johnsscionresources.blogspot.com/2012/02/human-spirit.html\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://johnsscionresources.blogspot.com/2012/02/human-spirit.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://johnsscionresources.blogspot.com/2012/02/human-spirit.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://johnsscionresources.blogspot.com/search/label/monotheism\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://johnsscionresources.blogspot.com/search/label/monotheism\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://johnsscionresources.blogspot.com/search/label/monotheism\" target=\"_blank\"> http://johnsscionresources.blogspot.com/search/label/monotheism </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bBasically, I don't think monotheist religions work in a polytheistic game. I don't get a good feeling from the idea of playing a Scion of Jesus because that means Jesus had to come down from Heaven, have sex with a woman and then leave her by herself, carrying his child, to fight off pagan monsters. And the last time Angels had Scions... well, they were the Nephilim and there was a Flood related to that. Saints don't work for me because they <i>very clearly</i> are <i>not Gods</i>. At all. You have to entire re-define what a &quot;God&quot; is to make a Monotheistic Pantheon work and that causes cascading issues.<br /> <br /> If you want something <i>related</i> to the Abrahamic religions, use the ancient Semitic religions like Caananite, Babylonian or Arabian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T13:22:36-07:00","id":1258,"title":"","content":"I think there are extreme issues with the Abrahamic faiths that make it a thorny issue in Scion.<br /> <br /> The first is that, while there are worshippers of many of the pantheons detailed in Scion, the primary audience for the game is the US and Western Europe, who by and large tend to be members of one of the Abrahamic faiths. As such, doing them justice is going to be a challenge. Moreso because many people at the same table are likely to have strenuous arguments about whether Moses was a Scion or not, among other possibilities. It's going to be hard as hell to make the figures of these religions into something that will make everyone happy. People have split off and founded their own religions because of arguments like that. I care less about courting controversy here as I do about making sure that no one playing gets into friendship-destroying arguments with each other. That shit has the potential to get UGLY.<br /> <br /> Second is the fact that the nature of Abrahamic faiths is that there are no other gods aside from God/YHWH/Jehovah/Allah. All other gods are false gods, either folded in as Saints or made into demons. Many of the Elohim, the gods of the neighboring Caananite tribes, were made into demons by Christianity (Baal, Dagon, etc.). This view is incompatible with Scion's premise, that of mythical figures of different cultures banding together to fight old threats. It's like trying to fit an AC plug into a DC outlet<br /> <br /> Regarding the fact that Vodoun isn't a pantheon, I'd say that's why a number of us want to see the Loa revamped and brought more in sync with the Orishas, their Yoruba, West African roots rather than the New World, heavily-syncretized-with-Christianity Loa. That's something I hope happens in 2e, so that they seem more like a group of gods than of saints and whatnot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T14:00:59-07:00","id":1279,"title":"","content":"Try to look at it this way: The Abrahamic God is Fate (in Scion). He is the metaphysical string that ties all the world myths together and all are under his purview.<br /> <br /> This way He is powerful as in the Bible, but uncomprehensible by human and god minds. We can only see the effects of his works.<br /> <br /> If you accept this, then you can place the Angels, Archangels, Saint and others into the category of Creatures of Fate, the same that contains the World Serpent and the Feris Wolf as Fate Titans. Two sides of the same coin, but both necessary tools for God to place Humanity on the right path, even if it means to start anew.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the other hand, if you really want to be the Scion of (Arch)Angel X or Saint Y, I can't see any reason for why it wouldn't be possible in the game mechanics. It changes nothing in comparison to the other Scions, I just think the Abrahamic God and his followers work better as NPCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://s56.photobucket.com/user/Solkannar/media/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i56.photobucket.com/albums/g165/Solkannar/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":384,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","user":"Man in Black","date":". 11-02-2013, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","name":"Man in Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar384_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T14:12:42-07:00","id":1292,"title":"","content":"The idea of God=Fate doesn't really jive with what Monotheism says about him. As GriffinGuy pointed out, if you start messing with monotheism and treating it like it's equal with other religions, it becomes touchy for the core audience. I'm not saying that there aren't polytheists in the Scion audience, but just as a broad observation they seem to get less prickly about their religion than monotheists do. <br /> <br /> It's the issue of &quot;mythology&quot;. I've gotten into arguments with people when I use the term &quot;Christian mythology&quot; in comparative religion because they don't think anything Christian is mythological. It's real. Absolutely true and you can get into some hot water with folks for comparing Odin to God or Jesus to Moloch. It's two very incompatible world views and the monotheist side tends to be a lot stronger and more opinionated in modern, Western culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T14:22:27-07:00","id":1299,"title":"","content":"Hi Telgar, nice to see you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=1292#post1292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of God=Fate doesn't really jive with what Monotheism says about him. As GriffinGuy pointed out, if you start messing with monotheism and treating it like it's equal with other religions, it becomes touchy for the core audience. I'm not saying that there aren't polytheists in the Scion audience, but just as a broad observation they seem to get less prickly about their religion than monotheists do.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there are people that don't like the position a games places his world view, they can do what people always have: ignore it.<br /> <br /> Scion is a game about playing the child of a god with other children of gods, so unless they all play as children of God and deny the existence of other Gods and instead battle the Titan Devil they will have to get along.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=1292#post1292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the issue of &quot;mythology&quot;. I've gotten into arguments with people when I use the term &quot;Christian mythology&quot; in comparative religion because they don't think anything Christian is mythological. It's real. Absolutely true and you can get into some hot water with folks for comparing Odin to God or Jesus to Moloch. It's two very incompatible world views and the monotheist side tends to be a lot stronger and more opinionated in modern, Western culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>People are constantly wrong and those people you are talking about, definitely are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://s56.photobucket.com/user/Solkannar/media/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i56.photobucket.com/albums/g165/Solkannar/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","name":"Man in Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar384_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T14:23:43-07:00","id":1300,"title":"","content":"for me, this is really a question of the metaphysics of Scion, whoever you choose to run it. I tend to the &quot;humans create gods via belief&quot; view, but it's by no means the only one. In that view, the way I choose to handwave away the necessity of the Abrahamic faiths is that there are so many different conceptions that are supposed to apply to the same being (trinitarian vs unitarian, et cetera) that the actual being in question is not able to develop the coherent level of consciousness required to take active part in the World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T15:28:51-07:00","id":1332,"title":"","content":"Something brought up in discussions I've had about this came up that I feel should be brought up:<br /> <br /> Whenever you bring the Abrahamic faiths into something, it has a tendency to supercede everything else.<br /> <br /> This happens frequently in fiction (Sandman, Supernatural... Old World of Darkness) that when you have a big ol' melting pot of mythological stuff, and the Judeo-Christian-Islamic stuff is added, it overpowers the rest like a shot of Bailey's in a mixed drink (I may be mixing metaphors here). <br /> <br /> Then there's actual mythological syncretism like the Loa being Christian Saints or Brigid becoming a Saint, or St. Patrick summoning Cuchulain's ghost. If you add that in here, you are giving the Abrahamic stuff greater power and sway over everything else. This is not a precedent we should set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T17:13:30-07:00","id":1390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>griffinguy24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=1258#post1258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the fact that Vodoun isn't a pantheon, I'd say that's why a number of us want to see the Loa revamped and brought more in sync with the Orishas, their Yoruba, West African roots rather than the New World, heavily-syncretized-with-Christianity Loa. That's something I hope happens in 2e, so that they seem more like a group of gods than of saints and whatnot.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it's the same in the Yoruba mythology - the supreme God is Olorun/<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Ol\u00f3d\u00f9mar\u00e8<br /> <br /> EDIT: This is not to say I want the Loa/Orisha/what have you cute - far from it - but the 'no monotheism EVER' idea tends towards the European definition of pantheism, which doesn't hold up against others.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T17:25:11-07:00","id":1397,"title":"","content":"Mmmm. Yes, he was seen as a creator god, but not the <i>only</i> god. The Orishas were still very, very much seen as divine beings and gods. They were worshipped directly, not like the saints that you asked for intercession on your behalf with the <i>real</i> God.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T17:36:40-07:00","id":1403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=1397#post1397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mmmm. Yes, he was seen as a creator god, but not the <i>only</i> god. The Orishas were still very, very much seen as divine beings and gods. They were worshipped directly, not like the saints that you asked for intercession on your behalf with the <i>real</i> God.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Orisha are a fundamental part of the world, but Olurun is the only supreme God. Orisha reflect a part of the divine, and are left in charge of certain parts of the world but gain their power from Olurun.<br /> <br /> At least, that's how the Yoruba I know explain it to me - I'm Esan, personally.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, less of the 'was',, please. the religion of the Yoruba is still very much known and practised in its pre-colonial form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T17:50:55-07:00","id":1411,"title":"","content":"In fact, it's much easier for me to just post the link below for reference - it's an essay entitled &quot;Monotheism in Traditional Yoruba Religion&quot;, and it's far better articulated and sourced than I could hope to be. Here's the summary for the tl;dr crowd<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2379B5\"><b><a href=\"http://organizations.uncfsu.edu/ncrsa/journal/v03/johnsonoyinade_yoruba.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://organizations.uncfsu.edu/ncrs...ade_yoruba.htm</a></b></span><br /> <br /> -------------------<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Early researchers were biased and prejudicial in their analysis about the Yoruba concept of God. What we have learned by examining the concept of God by the Yoruba is that the Yoruba religion is monotheistic. From various names given to Olodumare, a clear picture of God emerges. He is seen as the Lord of the sky, the Creator of all mankind, the Giver of life and He is seen as invisible. Because of the invisibility of God, the Yoruba make no concerted efforts to erect a shrine of Him or any kind of &quot;physical representation&quot; (Opoku, p. 18). Although, the deities are revered, they are created by God to serve specific functions just as the angels are created to serve God.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T18:05:34-07:00","id":1415,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the tense.<br /> <br /> My impression is that the religion is much like other polytheistic religions, though yes, when you leave the Western cultures you have to start dealing with different basic assumptions about what things like &quot;godhood&quot; even mean. Olorun is a supreme creator deity, but there <i>are</i> other figures that are considered &quot;gods&quot;. You might define the Yoruba as henotheistic, but even that isn't quite accurate because the 'lesser' gods are still worshipped, not just acknowledged. Their entire purpose isn't just to communicate the prayers of mortals to Olorun, they actually respond to the prayers themselves, on their own behalf. Olorun set it all in motion, but he isn't the only one up there getting stuff done.<br /> <br /> Even in Greek polytheism, the most classical (heh) example of a polytheistic religion, there <i>is a creator</i>: Chaos. If he isn't anthropomorphic enough, there's Gaea. Zeus and the other Olympians aren't the original gods or even the most powerful figures. This theme is pretty consistent across polytheism, but it's glossed over because it makes things complicated. Religions are never, ever, ever simple things. Trying to simplify them is always going to be prickly, difficult and probably offensive.<br /> <br /> The difference between non-monotheist religions and monotheism is that traditional, Abrahamic-style monotheism does not acknowledge <i>any other divine figures</i>. At best, there are aspects to divinity if you believe in the Father/Son/Holy Ghost as a trinity of divinity. They're all still the same thing, just different aspects of it. There may still be existing sects that believe the Father, Son and Holy Ghost are distinct and separate divine beings on an equal level, but I'm not familiar with any. That would pretty much by definition no longer be 'monotheism', though. Angels, saints, etc, are <i>not gods</i>. They're not treated as gods. They're not worshipped as gods. They really <i>do</i> just carry messages to God. He really <i>is</i> the only one up there getting stuff done. You don't pray to St. Nick and expect <i>Saint Nick</i> to do something for you. You expect him to carry your message to God and have <i>God</i> do something.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't call the Yoruba monotheists, and I think that anthropologically that'd be a tough argument to make. Their religion is complex and includes a supreme creator deity, but it does include other deities created by that one. There are <i>parallels</i> to the idea of angels and saints, but Olorun isn't (as far as I know) considered as all-powerful as monotheists see their single God as being. He's got a different role, because they're working with a different framework. <br /> <br /> The <b>Loa</b> are a much stickier issue because they really are closer to non-divine messengers, since they've been far more heavily mixed with Christianity. But I still think there's a big jump from playing a Scion of Baron Samedi to playing a Scion of Jesus. Not least being that Christian mythology really just doesn't mesh with the idea of demigods. Even Jesus isn't really a demigod in modern Christianity. He's either an &quot;avatar&quot; of God or he <b>is</b>God.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T18:10:59-07:00","id":1417,"title":"","content":"Again, you've got an incredibly Eurocentric view of polytheism and monotheism based around <i>their</i> particular mythologies. Olurun is somethign wholly and utterly other and more powerful than the Orisha - in general the Yoruba religion is referred to as a 'diffused monotheism', with the monotheistic god, all powerful, omniscient god being aloof and unknowable.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I think in general that this is pretty much just pointing out the inadequacies of English theological language <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T18:28:41-07:00","id":1427,"title":"","content":"I admit, that's true. My understanding of the terms &quot;monotheism&quot;, &quot;henotheism&quot; and &quot;polytheism&quot; are based on the Western definitions of those concepts. It's also true, I admitted it earlier, that non-Western religions often do not fit neatly into those definitions because they aren't playing by Western rules. I'm not an expert religious anthropologist to get into exactly how to academically classify the Yoruba religion, but it's <i>not</i> monotheism under the traditional, common-parlance, Western definition. Abrahamic religions <i>are</i>. They do not play well with others. Having the Yoruba or even the Loa in the game doesn't mean that Abrahamic religion is going to mesh in well, because neither of those religions are monotheistic in the same sense that Abrahamic religions are.<br /> <br /> Think of Scion as an alkaline solution. It's a bad idea to add an acid to it. Monotheism is that acid. The pH value of Yoruba or Afro-Caribbean syncretic religions might be considerably closer to acidic, but they're not below 7. You can have all the ranges of basic materials you want in Scion, but things get unstable when you start mixing in acids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T18:38:02-07:00","id":1433,"title":"","content":"As a point, I have no problem with Abrahamic religions not being in Scion, it's just the term 'monotheistic' being thrown about as if it was onl the Abrahamic religions that grinds my gears a little (due to my cultural background and education).<br /> <br /> <i>Although</i>, that being said, having Old Testament style wholly alien angels turn up as events on the scale of supernatural Tsunamis (or Promethean's Qashmallim) could work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T22:20:41-07:00","id":1537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=1427#post1427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think of Scion as an alkaline solution. It's a bad idea to add an acid to it. Monotheism is that acid. The pH value of Yoruba or Afro-Caribbean syncretic religions might be considerably closer to acidic, but they're not below 7. You can have all the ranges of basic materials you want in Scion, but things get unstable when you start mixing in acids.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing to bear in mind is that Monotheism, specifically the Abrahamic faiths, isn't so much a question of can't be added as a question of where an individual group's comfort zone with it lies. It's not something that can be simply ignored in a world that is, at least in some sense, a mirror of modern earth. I feel as though the best option might be a sidebar specifically explaining &quot;no, we haven't explicitly said how the Abrahamic faiths could be used in Scion. That is up to you, as Storytellers and Players&quot;. Some groups may want to ignore it entirely, while some may want to go the Yahweh-As-Antagonist route, while still others may want to use angels/saints/whatever as a normal-style pantheon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T23:55:07-07:00","id":1564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=1415#post1415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There may still be existing sects that believe the Father, Son and Holy Ghost are distinct and separate divine beings on an equal level, but I'm not familiar with any. That would pretty much by definition no longer be 'monotheism', though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mormons fall into this category. The Father, Son and Holy Ghost are separate, but share the Godhead. That is, They (with capital T) form a divine council. And yes Wikipedia classifies it as tritheism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/210-siven","name":"Siven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T01:32:15-07:00","id":1597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=1411#post1411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, it's much easier for me to just post the link below for reference - it's an essay entitled &quot;Monotheism in Traditional Yoruba Religion&quot;, and it's far better articulated and sourced than I could hope to be. Here's the summary for the tl;dr crowd<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2379B5\"><b><a href=\"http://organizations.uncfsu.edu/ncrsa/journal/v03/johnsonoyinade_yoruba.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://organizations.uncfsu.edu/ncrs...ade_yoruba.htm</a></b></span></div> </div> </div> </div>This is definitely an interesting document. The majority of cited sources appear to be heavily Christianized, themselves, and much of the reference material is based around the Modern Yoruba religion. Because it is so modern, there is a fair bit of natural syncretization with modern monotheistic religions that have interacted with the Yoruba people over the centuries.<br /> <br /> \u200bOf course, it is going to be up to the individual storyteller about what time period they want to base any given 'pantheon' or organization of divinities. Some people prefer to take a snapshot from hundreds of years ago (to the best that we are able to research), while others are happy to use modern interpretations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T01:53:18-07:00","id":1604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guitarsniper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=1537#post1537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I feel as though the best option might be a sidebar specifically explaining &quot;no, we haven't explicitly said how the Abrahamic faiths could be used in Scion. That is up to you, as Storytellers and Players&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find I must concur with the Humon portraited one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T05:58:43-08:00","id":1694,"title":"","content":"I'd just like to say that, the assumption that pantheistic religions &quot;play well with one another&quot; is also wrong. Well before Christianity became powerful and well known, groups with different religions still fought over those religions. The Norse did not accept the concept that 'Roman gods might ALSO exist', no, ONLY the NORSE gods were REAL. The Roman gods were false. Likewise the Romans did not accept the existence of other gods SEPARATE from their gods, when they encountered a new religion the gods of that religion were EITHER &quot;Oh this god is totally Ares/Mars, you just have the wrong name because you are stupid barbarians, and look this one is Juno/Zeus. Man you guys are dumb&quot; OR &quot;This false god is a profane mockery kill them all centurion&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, the who Abrahamic &quot;There is no god but God&quot; thing isn't REALLY an obstacle to creating an Abrahamic Scion pantheon, rather it's just a story point that will cause contention between Abrahamic Heroes and NON-Abrahamic Heroes until both side pull their heads out of their bottoms.<br /> <br /> As for creating a Pantheon, I actually feel that there are Several viable options. For all of them, I would posit that the BEST choice would be to leave JHVH (God) out, and simply build an explanation that He is beyond/outside the normal order of the divine. I.E. For whatever inscrutable reason, He created these lesser deities, and THEIR purpose it to fight the Titans. And that fighting the Titans is part of His purpose (again, inscrutable) because being truly all powerful surely God could simply unmake the titans if he so chose. Basically the standard response to &quot;If god is both Benevolent and Omnipotent, wither Evil?&quot;<br /> 1&gt; A purely Catholic/Specific Orthodox Church pantheon consisting of Mary, Jesus, and the most prominent Saints. <br /> 2&gt; An Angelic Pantheon consisting of the Archangels and certain other named angels of lesser orders to fill out the roster. Angels appear in their classic khabalistic appearances, I.E. 7 wings, three heads one is a lion, etc.<br /> 3&gt; A Protestant specific Pantheon consisting of Jesus, the Archangels (in their modern depiction of cute mildly androgynous people with wings), and certain important religious figures added as a conceit on the concept that they were themselves Heroes who have since ascended, I.E. Martin Luther, others. Non-Mormon Heroes will be slightly bothered by the fact that Heroes empowered/descended from Moroni keep showing up...<br /> <br /> All my examples are Christian centric because, frankly, that's what I know, but I'm certain that if you're willing to use a slightly loose definition for 'god' you should be able to build a Jewish or Islamic group just as easily. <br /> <br /> As far as group specific Titans, the most obvious choice is to cast Lucifer, first of the Angels, once God's favorite, and ultimate betrayer, into the role. Lucifer was the 'prototype' for the angels, not a true angel. Much as the greek titans were the precursors of the greek gods, Lucifer would be the precursor for the archangels. The ranks of Abrahamic Titans could then be filled out with the other angels that followed Lucifer and fell during the war in heaven, and/or the various &quot;dukes of hell&quot; named throughout old mystical tradition texts - Belial, Ba'al, Asmodeas, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The only real obstacle to the inclusion of an Abrahamic Pantheon in a game of Scion is the preconceptions of the GM and Players that Christianity/Judaism/Islam are DIFFERENT from other religions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T07:14:21-08:00","id":1736,"title":"","content":"Must we use the Miltonean &quot;first among angels&quot; idea? It's not actually canon in pretty much any form of Christianity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T07:36:13-08:00","id":1752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TiwazTyrsfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=1694#post1694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd just like to say that, the assumption that pantheistic religions &quot;play well with one another&quot; is also wrong. Well before Christianity became powerful and well known, groups with different religions still fought over those religions. The Norse did not accept the concept that 'Roman gods might ALSO exist', no, ONLY the NORSE gods were REAL. The Roman gods were false. Likewise the Romans did not accept the existence of other gods SEPARATE from their gods, when they encountered a new religion the gods of that religion were EITHER &quot;Oh this god is totally Ares/Mars, you just have the wrong name because you are stupid barbarians, and look this one is Juno/Zeus. Man you guys are dumb&quot; OR &quot;This false god is a profane mockery kill them all centurion&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Citations? These claims are problematic for a number of reasons. For one, the Norse as we know them did not coexist in the same time period with pre-Christian Romans, so the first claim is impossible to deal with one way or another. However, the Norse did coexist with a number of other non-Christian cultures, and there is no evidence of their persecuting them on that count.<br /> <br /> As for the Romans' tendency to try to understand the gods of other cultures in terms of their own, that's simply a case of one culture viewing another through its own lens. If anything, it's the Romans trying to find some element of commonality with the other culture and not see them as utterly alien. But even then, the Greeks and Romans were totally used to there being localized cults of gods they had never heard of, so that didn't faze them at all. The very same phenomenon occurred throughout the Greco-Roman world, where pretty much every village would have gods that were unknown elsewhere. The concept of a fixed &quot;pantheon&quot; is, ironically, a monotheistic conceit. In fact, non-monotheistic cultures do not have a limit to the number of gods they recognize as existing. They just don't worship them all because it's impractical to do so. And of course they're gong to tend to favor the ones that are traditional to where they grew up, although that will not prevent them from appealing to foreign gods on occasion, if they think it will help them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only real obstacle to the inclusion of an Abrahamic Pantheon in a game of Scion is the preconceptions of the GM and Players that Christianity/Judaism/Islam are DIFFERENT from other religions. </div> </div> </div>Actually, the way monotheists understand the very concept of <i>divinity </i>is fundamentally different\u2014so much so, in fact, that scholars of ancient religion have pointed it out as a major stumbling block to proper understanding of how pre-Christian religions operated.<br /> <br /> In ancient terms, there is no essential definition of <i>god</i>. A being is a god if it receives worship according to the traditional rites afforded to gods in that culture. If it does not receive such worship, then it is not a god. It's as simple as that. A god can be a spirit, a dead person, a living person, an animal, a tree, an abstract concept, a river, a rock, or literally anything else that receives this kind of treatment.<br /> <br /> Abrahamic religions grant divine honors to only one being, so they are monotheistic. They may recognize the existence of other powerful spirits, and indeed all of the mainstream forms do, but those are either subservient to the one god or to be regarded as either irrelevant or actively malevolent. Angels are subordinate divine beings that are not worshiped as such, so they're not considered gods, even though they might be in a non-monotheistic context. Saints are a bit stickier, since they do receive reverence, but Christians who revere saints are very quick to point out that the worship they receive is different in kind from what one gives to the god, so they don't like to call it &quot;worship,&quot; even though that's what it looks like to an outsider.<br /> <br /> Neither Voodoo nor Zoroastrianism is monotheistic in any meaningful sense. Each may posit the existence of a supreme being, but lesser beings receive direct worship and divine honors in the manner of gods, and in fact that worship comprises the majority or even the entirety of religious activity for worshipers. Having a supreme god doesn't make a tradition monotheistic, especially if that supreme god is not the primary object of worship in the religion. There was a time when scholars wanted to view Zoroastrianism, for example, as monotheistic as a way of approaching it through the lens of Christianity, but that approach has since been discarded. Nor did Zoroastrians behave at all like monotheists when they conquered other peoples: on the contrary, the local gods were simply treated as <i>Yazatas</i>, and business continued as usual, with the King even being party to traditional rites where expected (e.g. Egypt).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":352,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","user":"Black Flag","date":". 11-03-2013, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T17:26:12-08:00","id":2201,"title":"","content":"One suggestion could be to let the abrahamic PSP deal with the &quot;god is mysterious&quot; and never really have god as an entity that actually has Scions. i.e. the gods of the abrahamic pantheon serve a higher power, or at least so they view it. The egyptians sort of do this with Ma'at (sp?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T17:36:50-08:00","id":2211,"title":"","content":"Ma'at is more of a philosophy, but she <i>is</i> a Titan Avatar too. She's not an all-powerful force beyond the system. And the same was true in Egyptian religion: Ma'at was a goddess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T19:35:42-08:00","id":2307,"title":"","content":"Every single ST and every single group in general is going to have a multitude of players that run all over the spectrum from devout to atheist. It is extremely wise to leave the idea of monotheism that the Abrahamic religions represens to the individual choice of a group/ST. Having run games with people who were devout believers and people who could give three cents about how I treated the Judeo-Christian faith system, I can safely say that it is not something that should ever have a blanket one-size-fits-all ruling. Someone who might be all right with the Saints in the pantheon might run up against someone who can't even conceive of anything beyond maybe God/Jesus/Holy Ghost.<br /> <br /> Use your judgement and understanding of the group and things will go a lot smoother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T21:43:00-08:00","id":2374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aynie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Every single ST and every single group in general is going to have a multitude of players that run all over the spectrum from devout to atheist. It is extremely wise to leave the idea of monotheism that the Abrahamic religions represens to the individual choice of a group/ST. Having run games with people who were devout believers and people who could give three cents about how I treated the Judeo-Christian faith system, I can safely say that it is not something that should ever have a blanket one-size-fits-all ruling. Someone who might be all right with the Saints in the pantheon might run up against someone who can't even conceive of anything beyond maybe God/Jesus/Holy Ghost.<br /> <br /> Use your judgement and understanding of the group and things will go a lot smoother.</div> </div> </div> </div>But as you once viciously snarled at me in the old forums, there are people who really do believe in a number of deities featured within Scion, and those belief systems are not always uniform either. So why should those gods be given any more of a pass?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","user":"The Revenge of TV Head","date":". 11-04-2013, 12:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T22:46:21-08:00","id":2411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=2374#post2374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But as you once viciously snarled at me in the old forums, there are people who really do believe in a number of deities featured within Scion, and those belief systems are not always uniform either. So why should those gods be given any more of a pass?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am only speaking from anecdotal experience here, but I have always noticed that regardless of the religion in question... regional minorities <b>TEND</b> to be a lot more forgiving and tolerant towards the beliefs of others.<br /> <br /> This is not to say that there is not a wealth of tolerance even from regional majorities, but regional majorities tend to express a lot of social pressure upon those regional minorities. This trend tends to happen regardless of who those regional majorities and minorities actually are (unless a specific doctrine encourages otherwise).<br /> <br /> We just happen to be in a situation where <b>MOST</b> of the pantheons represented in Scion are a regional minority.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T23:24:27-08:00","id":2430,"title":"","content":"Of course, according to that particular line of logic, I see absolutely no reason why the central divine figure of Sikhism can't be featured in Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T00:37:26-08:00","id":2462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=2430#post2430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, according to that particular line of logic, I see absolutely no reason why the central divine figure of Sikhism can't be featured in Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish you the best of luck with that. Ultimately what gets included in the Scion line will be based upon what is most popular in the sales region, balanced against what is going to make the fewest people angry. Also mythical accuracy of course, but the latter is just my personal preference. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T00:48:32-08:00","id":2466,"title":"","content":"Seeing as how we're dealing with a company that's the direct descendant (and essentially a continuation) of the company that produced <b>Demon: the Fallen</b>, I don't put much stock in the idea that they'd choose not to include something in <b>Scion</b> simply because &quot;the Abrahamic community would be offended&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T01:16:13-08:00","id":2474,"title":"","content":"Less &quot;The Abrahamic Community&quot; and more &quot;The people who are going to be playing our games&quot;. It's not 1970, a lot of christians actually play RPGs. Hell, I know of at least one RPG set in a fantasy world that's all about getting closer to God.<br /> <br /> And anyone who would have a problem with Sikhism being true in an &quot;All Myths are True&quot; setting is no one I'd want to play with anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T02:04:10-08:00","id":2482,"title":"","content":"<b>Demon: the Fallen</b> wasn't written in the 1970s. I agree that there are Christians who play RPGs; after all, I <i>am</i> one. If the <b>Scion</b>\u200b developers are steering clear of touching on Abrahamic themes for fear of offending Abrahamic roleplayers, I'll be disappointed: it implies that they think we need to be coddled.<br /> <br /> My only request is that they don't present Abrahamic elements in a primarily negative light (such as saying that Christians and Jews are unknowingly worshipping a malevolent Titan). In particular, I do <i>not</i>\u200b expect them to present an &quot;all-powerful 'Pantheon' of One&quot;; I'm willing to go along with something more akin to what <b>In Nomine</b> does: the angels (read: Abrahamic counterpart to gods) <i>know</i> that their Creator God exists; but they can't prove it, because He is no longer in contact with them. So they operate more or less like any other Pantheon would while they strive to find out where He went.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T04:45:11-08:00","id":2517,"title":"","content":"That is very similar to what the Yazata do. They approach the situation with Henotheism, claiming Ahura Mazda is the ultimate power in their pantheon but otherwise an unknown. It is the 'lesser' gods that operate under Ahura Mazda that form the body of the pantheon as a whole.<br /> <br /> So it is mechanically possible to stage the angels and archangels as 'Gods', but it goes back to begging the question of whether they acknowledge the existence of other 'Gods'. That's the real crux of the issue. If all myths are true, and their myths say that none of the other myths are true, then how do you resolve the paradox?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T04:50:46-08:00","id":2521,"title":"","content":"Nanomachines, son.<br /> <br /> Is it so hard to have someone bring it up to Yaweh and just have him reply with &quot;Well why did you chucklefucks think the first rule I ever made was: Fuck those other gods, if there were no other gods? I mean. Seriously.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T05:14:04-08:00","id":2531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=2521#post2521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nanomachines, son.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Is it so hard to have someone bring it up to Yaweh and just have him reply with &quot;Well why did you chucklefucks think the first rule I ever made was: Fuck those other gods, if there were no other gods? I mean. Seriously.&quot;</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Apparently so! It has certainly been one of the predominant theological questions that have been floating around for centuries. Did he mean 'no other gods before me' because there were none? Or because he was advocating Henotheism? (rhetorical question).<br /> <br /> Entire denominations have sprung up over similar issues over the years. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T06:45:46-08:00","id":2566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=2374#post2374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But as you once viciously snarled at me in the old forums, there are people who really do believe in a number of deities featured within Scion, and those belief systems are not always uniform either. So why should those gods be given any more of a pass?</div> </div> </div> </div>I snarled at many a person when they decided to treat the beliefs of anyone with less than a minimum of respect. I know a few folks who still follow the belief system of the Hellenistic faith and they adore Scion. Is it a game, ultimately? Sure. But you can respect the cultures and belief-systems within that game by trying to remain as accurate to the myths as possible; which is what I try to do.<br /> <br /> Keeping accurate to the ideals of the Abrahamic religions might step on toes and cause drama if candor isn't done pre-game. I should know, it's happened personally in a game I ran. I didn't double-check with a player pre-game and when they discovered that in the Scion Universe that the Abrahamic religion was all a front for one particular Canaanite god who managed to slip by the rule to disappear --- not a happy post-game session. Another player of mine in a different game was extremely offended that the Archangels were worshipped on the same level as other gods because, to them, that was a huge no.<br /> <br /> A third game, no one cared, and we've got a band of new demigod Scions actively using the Christian faith to build a new pantheon with Yahweh at the lead.<br /> <br /> It is something that cannot be stretched to a one-size-fits all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T06:58:21-08:00","id":2571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=2566#post2566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keeping accurate to the ideals of the Abrahamic religions</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a healthy suspension of disbelief is needed for Scion, after all there probably <i>isn't</i> a Titan-God war going on and it's a healthy assumption that various Gods/Goddesses are <i>not</i> siring children.<br /> <br /> Not to mention anecdotal evidence isn't really strong to argue with, your players might have been offended but I'm a Methodist and I wouldn't be offended if they were included. Sure, I was a little (re: the smallest possible modicum of upset) that the Christian Faith was portrayed as worshiping a Titan in Scion 1e, but that didn't stop me from still loving the material. <br /> <br /> <br /> Like Dataweaver said, I think it implies our faith needs to be coddled if they steer clear of including a Pantheon and as many said God/Yahweh doesn't even need to be in the Pantheon to alleviate all sorts of &quot;But he's the strongest!&quot; etc. He can just be entirely absent--and in his absence---Archangels have begun to fight the war against the Titans. Perhaps in the setting Abrahamic faith changed their beliefs to the Archangels in God's absence. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T07:04:58-08:00","id":2576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=2517#post2517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it is mechanically possible to stage the angels and archangels as 'Gods', but it goes back to begging the question of whether they acknowledge the existence of other 'Gods'. That's the real crux of the issue. If all myths are true, and their myths say that none of the other myths are true, then how do you resolve the paradox?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's trivial. Angels don't consider themselves to be gods, even when they're statistically equivalent to the beings in other Pantheons who call themselves \u201cgods\u201d. So why would they consider, say, the Aesir or the Akatsukami to be \u201cgods\u201d? Put another way: they don't deny that multiple Pantheons exist; they merely deny that said Pantheons are honest-to-goodness <i>gods</i>. They consider the other Pantheons to be beings like them who have delusions of grandeur, and who don't properly understand their place in the grand scheme of things. It wouldn't be the first time that Pantheons have had a difference of opinion.<br /> <br /> And yes, it's also entirely reasonable to play it as the Abrahamic Pantheon advocating for henotheism instead of monotheism; I'd be OK with that, too. Frankly, I can think of several other Pantheons that could benefit from a henotheistic makeover: the Loa, Vedas, and Celestial Bureaucracy come to mind quite readily. It's a much more flexible framework, because it has <i>room</i> for each Pantheon to have a \u201cHigher God\u201d, but doesn't <i>require</i> it of any Pantheon. <br /> <br /> Finally, let's say for the sake of argument that it's a necessary feature of the Abrahamic faiths that they deny that other supernatural forces exist <i>at all</i>. Why would that have any bearing on the existence of the other Pantheons? \u201call myths are true\u201d means that positive statements about something\u2019s existence are true, not that negative statements about something\u2019s nonexistence are true. It affirms things; it does not deny them. <br /> <br /> So we've got a Pantheistic solution, a Henotheistic solution, and even a Monotheistic solution. And that's without getting into the possibilities of \u201cYahweh is the last surviving member of the ancient Canaanite Pantheon\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T07:23:38-08:00","id":2599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=2576#post2576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's trivial.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm afraid it is not as trivial as all that (hence why this conversation has spanned countless pages before and will continue to spawn them in the future). In fact, I showed your suggestions to a few very devout associates of mine and they were quite offended.<br /> <br /> So many eggs broken in making this omelette apparently.<br /> <br /> There are also some genuine mechanical issues with each of your approaches. Granted, some these are issues that may not be remotely present in the 2nd Edition of Scion.<br /> <br /> If angels do not consider themselves to be gods, then are they mechanically gods? If so, then there is the mechanical acknowledgement that they are deluded gods. If not, can they make scions? If not, can they make entities of equivalent power that are reskinned and reflavored scions? Or are they just potentially benevolent Titanspawn?<br /> <br /> What happens when Odin looks an Archangel right in the face and uses God's Honest to tell the truth? &quot;I am a god.&quot; Do all the Archangels have some relic or PSP that grants them immunity to such absolute truths? If so, that could heavily inform the setting that they need a protection against such truths. If not, and the absolute truth fails? Then the rest of gods are not really gods?<br /> <br /> I could seriously go on with similar questions and examples for about another thirty paragraphcs, but I hope you can see where it is going. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 11-04-2013, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T08:40:29-08:00","id":2647,"title":"","content":"The forum ate my reply. Short version: what offended them? The notion that God isn't talking to the angels, the notion that angels don\u2019t consider high-Legend beings to be gods, the notion that supernatural beings who call themselves \u201cgods\u201d exist in the first place, or something else? On the bit about whether angels are in fact the same sort of beings as those who call themselves \u201cgods\u201d, saying that they are only makes them delusional if the so-called gods <i>really are</i> gods; and <i>that\u2019s</i> a question that should ultimately be left up to the Storyteller to answer \u2014 or to avoid, as he sees fit. And if they <i>are</i> a different kind of being than the self-styled gods, that doesn't mean that they're Titanspawn: there are Immortals who are neither god nor titan; and it would be a simple matter to extend Immortals all the way up to Legend 12.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T09:17:17-08:00","id":2672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=2647#post2647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The forum ate my reply.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry the forum ate your post <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Specifically? They thought it was a bit blasphemous to suggest that the angels actually cannot hear the word of god, or that the faithful cannot hear the word of god. Also that there was anyone or anything that could rival the angels in power (save perhaps other fallen angels). I did warn you that they were pretty devout.<br /> <br /> Now, I notice you say that it is the kind of question that should ultimately be left up to the Storyteller to answer -- or to avoid. I think you and I are in complete agreement. I happily leave that question up to be judged on a case by case basis from one group to the next.<br /> <br /> But it probably should not be written out as an actual pantheon to be used in the core Scion books. Maybe as a supplement named Monotheism that goes into the various versions of monotheism and how to handle those settings, or integrate them into a regular Scion game?<br /> <br /> <b>I might buy that. But I don't want it in Core.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T10:42:15-08:00","id":2761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=2647#post2647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> On the bit about whether angels are in fact the same sort of beings as those who call themselves \u201cgods\u201d, saying that they are only makes them delusional if the so-called gods <i>really are</i> gods; and <i>that\u2019s</i> a question that should ultimately be left up to the Storyteller to answer \u2014 or to avoid, as he sees fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm confused on this part of your reply. Are you suggesting that if the Abrahamic pantheons are included in core, then the question of if the other pantheons are actually gods is a ST-by-ST basis? Because the entire premise of the game-line itself is the Gods are real, that their myths are real, and divinity is something that you can pass down to a kid and that kid can become a God.<br /> <br /> That should not be a case-by-case basis idea and is exactly why the Abrahamic pantheons should be not included within the core-game itself because once they're in there, the question of true divinity and what qualifies as a god becomes really muddled really fast.<br /> <br /> If that's not what you were implying, then I apologize and we can blame a overly-large dosage of Dayquil and cough drops for my interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T11:03:35-08:00","id":2780,"title":"","content":"The one thing that's clear is that if you add Monotheism to the equation (sorry, OtherGuy, but I'm going with a traditional, Western definition of monotheism) then things get confusing and fast. You have to make compromises and shuffle things around and it opens a lot of questions about &quot;what is a God&quot; and &quot;are Gods real?&quot; and just.. all sorts of messy, icky questions. Without monotheism, that doesn't come up nearly as much.<br /> <br /> So what's the benefit vs cost ratio? What benefit do you get from adding the ability to play a Scion of Jesus in a band with Scions of Thor, Morrigan, Susano-O and Ra? Is that benefit worth all the issues, anger, questions and compromises that have to be made to allow it? Considering my own experiences here in the American South, I would say that it isn't worth it. Getting Christianity involved in a game of &quot;Mythology&quot; is a FAST way to get into a bunch of very heated arguments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T11:58:20-08:00","id":2815,"title":"","content":"Here, I think, is the crux of the argument: would the addition of an Abrahamic pantheon, with all that it entails, add more to the gameline as a whole than whatever else the developers who would otherwise have been making this Abrahamic pantheon could have been working on. If the developers who were writing up Michael and Gabriel and Jesus and whatnot, and causing potential controversy and issues for players could instead have been making, for example, an uncontroversial and still awesome polynesian pantheon that wouldn't otherwise have been included, go with the ridiculous jade-wielding seafarers. please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T15:47:01-08:00","id":2960,"title":"","content":"I really do think any instances of using Abrahamic faiths as a pantheon should be done as a side supplement, if at all, largely because I'd rather the game line not become completely <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/HijackedByJesus\" target=\"_blank\">hijacked by Jesus</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T15:53:48-08:00","id":2966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=2672#post2672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Specifically? They thought it was a bit blasphemous to suggest that the angels actually cannot hear the word of god, or that the faithful cannot hear the word of god. Also that there was anyone or anything that could rival the angels in power (save perhaps other fallen angels). I did warn you that they were pretty devout.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that they'd have a problem with angels not having a significant edge over everyone else, I suspect that they'd have at least as much of a problem with the notion that God doesn't have <i>any</i> influence in the setting. If your primary goal is to not offend them, your only option is to give them angels that are more powerful than the gods. Which is why I don't think that the principle of least offense makes any sense; the decision of how to handle the Abrahamic faiths should be primarily based on other factors, such as which option provides the most interesting story options.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=2672#post2672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it probably should not be written out as an actual pantheon to be used in the core Scion books. Maybe as a supplement named Monotheism that goes into the various versions of monotheism and how to handle those settings, or integrate them into a regular Scion game?</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. To clarify, I'm not arguing for it to be included in the core book; I'd be fine with the Abrahamic faiths being handled in a supplement designed to be purchased by those interested in the subject and ignored by those who aren't. I'd also be OK with the Abrahamic faiths being addressed in a supplement dedicated to, say, religions originating in the Middle East. What I'd want in the core book would be a paragraph or so that outlines the basics on how <b>Scion</b> intends to handle them, on which an appropriate supplement would then expand.<br /> <br /> More generally though, I'd like the notion of the \u201cHigher God\u201d (a being who is to the gods of a given Pantheon as those gods are to men \u2014 say, something that's roughly analogous to a Greater Titan in much the same way that lesser Titans are roughly analogous to gods) to be included in the core book \u2014 not so much for the purpose of implementing Abrahamic faiths as for handling <i>any</i> mythology that has one Divine Being (or even two or three) who operates on a whole different level than the rest of the Pantheon. I've mentioned the Loa before in this context; in their case, much of the issue comes from the fact that Voudoun and Satiera (sp?) are hybrids of Christian and native African mythologies. But you also get the issue with the likes of Hindu mythology (where you have three \u201chead gods\u201d, and everyone else is a manifestation of one of those three) and what little I know of the Chinese mythology on which the Celestial Bureaucracy is based. And as OtherGuy pointed out, the notion of the Pantheon as described in the existing edition of <b>Scion</b> is primarily a European thing; even regions as close as Africa include mythologies that don't fit neatly into that paradigm. And at the other end of the scale \u2014 and for similar reasons \u2014 I'd like to see the notion of Hero-level characters who don\u2019t have Divine heritage, but who acquired Legend through other means (e.g., the patronage, as opposed to parentage, of a Higher God).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T06:27:56-08:00","id":3434,"title":"","content":"If it were me, I'd do it like this:<br /> <br /> God is God and the head of the Pantheon. The other pantheons ignore His existence, but the faithful can hear Him just fine. But since he rarely takes corporeal form or directly intercedes, no one outside of the pantheon is sure if He's a myth or how powerful He really is. (In turn, it's setting mystery left to the ST.)<br /> <br /> Place Jesus and Muhammed as the functioning &quot;heads&quot; of the pantheon. (Not the actual, as that is God.) As the most famous prophets of their respective religions, their Legend has simply grown above the rest of the pantheon, but below God. I don't know enough about Judaism to posit an acceptable candidate here. (One of the Archangels? Enoch the patriarch?) In any case, they aren't gods or worshiped directly, just really, really revered.<br /> <br /> Then from there, cascade Mary, Joseph, Angels, Saints and other important personages based on their relative importance. Their Legend is more of a reflection their legends and less on divine ichor. Again, not gods in any sense (save mechanically for Scion rules purposes.) They just happen to be really revered for the Holy beings they are. The other pantheons call everyone from God on down, &quot;gods,&quot; but the Abrahamic pantheon as a whole is offended by the characterization, assuming they pay attention in the first place.<br /> <br /> The only &quot;true&quot; God in the pantheon is God. The only being in the pantheon that ever Sired a child proper is God, in the form of Jesus. (Which fits into Scion just fine.) Or possibly Jesus is not the son of God, just a really important prophet. It's ultimately irrelevant, because Jesus is still a well known Legend 10+ being. Anyone who asks anyone in the pantheon for the truth gets the axiom &quot;We're all the children of God&quot; in reply. The other Legendary beings in the pantheon adopted their Scions. That in turn gave rise to the Saints.<br /> <br /> Why some of the Legendary beings in the Abrahamic Pantheon didin't need to be directly Sired by God is a setting mystery. Were they Scions adopted from other Pantheons? Does God touch mortal beings, infuse them with divine ichor directly, and guide the other beings in the pantheon to take care of the nascent Scion? Or were they actual divine Scions of God, but the lesser members of the pantheon &quot;adopt&quot; as necessary? It could be a complete mystery.<br /> <br /> Or make it their Pantheon Purview. Much like the Aesir give their divine ichor to empower people and creatures, perhaps Legendary beings of the Abrahamic Pantheon can pass on God's touch (and therefore divine ichor) much more directly. This could be reflected in holy sites, relics, and the like. Maybe they take their own Legend and imbue <i>that</i>.<br /> <br /> As for their Titan-spawn, we have the fallen angels, demons, and the like. The &quot;gods&quot; that Christianity co-opted as demons, could actually be an early Titan spawn tactic designed to turn the other pantheons against the nascent Abrahamic Pantheon. That is to say, certain Titan spawn (or Titan Avatars) masqueraded as the other pantheons' gods and messed with the the younger pantheon. It didn't work and they were eventually found to be Titan spawn/Avatars, but it still made for difficult relations between pantheons.<br /> <br /> Just some thoughts.<br /> <br /> -Ariketh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/753-ariketh","name":"Ariketh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T08:37:05-08:00","id":3522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ariketh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=3434#post3434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Place Jesus and Muhammed as the functioning &quot;heads&quot; of the pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is going to sound intensely blasphemous, but I really do not intend it to be so. I do not think the likes of Jesus or Muhammed would rank higher than Legend 4 or Legend 5 at the absolute most. I certainly think they may have had some serious divine power watching over them and helping them accomplish their goals, but either as Scions or Avatars their personal accomplishments do not rank very high on the legend scale by the mechanics of the game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T08:56:05-08:00","id":3537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=3522#post3522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is going to sound intensely blasphemous, but I really do not intend it to be so. I do not think the likes of Jesus or Muhammed would rank higher than Legend 4 or Legend 5 at the absolute most. I certainly think they may have had some serious divine power watching over them and helping them accomplish their goals, but either as Scions or Avatars their personal accomplishments do not rank very high on the legend scale by the mechanics of the game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Haha, not blasphemous at all. This isn't a church and we're having an open discussion environment, you bring up good points.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's why, I think anyway, the hypothetical &quot;Pantheon&quot; would just be a choir of Archangels that are fighting the Titans in the absence of their creator, God<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T10:16:20-08:00","id":3590,"title":"","content":"Wasn't there a Canaanite fan pantheon that was all written out and nice and edited? It's the origin religion so does that count as an abrahamic pantheon?<br /> <br /> Aside from that, if I were to create one more like what the abrahamic religions look like today, I would have, as others have stated, it pretty much comprised of angels. In fact I'd prolly make them all angels even each of the trinity, kind of in the same vain as how they are laid out in the His Dark Materials trilogy.<br /> <br /> It shouldn't be all to hard really, each named angel has a purview in abrahamic lore. They have a &quot;heaven&quot; type place for the gods (they call themselves angels instead of gods with the exception of a handful of them (the trinity and maybe a few others)<br /> <br /> For titans I can see a few different Ideas: Either demons/fallen angels are the titans (and there fore hate the gods for the same reason that other titans do) or the titans could be only demons with &quot;fallen&quot; angels just as another faction of gods similar to the technically two yet not Scandinavian pantheons. I'd prolly lean more in favor of the second one because that would allow for more intricacy of plot in that two factions who usually don't get along, sometimes might work together. Kind of like having loki as a god and how he and his scions even provide a good amount of drama.<br /> <br /> the lore even has tales of the offspring of the gods (read angels). I don't know, the more I think about it the more I actually want to create it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T10:32:04-08:00","id":3603,"title":"","content":"Christian epics like the Milton/Jeruselam duology by William Blake, Finnegans Wake by James Joyce, and Paradise Lost by Milton seem like excellent places to draw from for a nominally Christian pantheon. What do others think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thinking as I do that the Creator of this World is a very Cruel Being &amp; being a Worshipper of Christ, I cannot help saying: &quot;the Son, O how unlike the Father!&quot; First God Almighty comes with a Thump on the Head. Then Jesus Christ comes with a balm to heal it. - William Blake, Christian mystic and visionary","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/774-pilgrim","name":"Pilgrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar774_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T14:10:57-08:00","id":3751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pilgrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=3603#post3603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Christian epics like the Milton/Jeruselam duology by William Blake, Finnegans Wake by James Joyce, and Paradise Lost by Milton seem like excellent places to draw from for a nominally Christian pantheon. What do others think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just going to sit here and be disappointed on behalf of one Dante Alighieri.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T14:28:20-08:00","id":3762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guitarsniper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=3751#post3751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just going to sit here and be disappointed on behalf of one Dante Alighieri.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, if Dante knew of this thread and the whole discussion behind it, he would write a new canto just to put us in the Inferno so we can get what we deserve. I wonder what kind of punishment is reserved for roleplayers... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T16:25:15-08:00","id":3838,"title":"","content":"Are the devs still going with the idea of presenting multiple possible settings in Scion: Hero? If they go that route, it seems like they could have their cake and eat it to, on this question. Have one setting with an Abrahamic pantheon (one that will presumably be published in another supplement) and the rest without.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/794-el-pinko-grande","name":"el pinko grande","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar794_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T17:13:58-08:00","id":3877,"title":"","content":"I seriously hope they do NOT include the Abrahamic faith as a pantheon. It's bad enough that many myths have been bastardized by the monotheists, but to include it in the end means to include the view point of the &quot;faithful&quot;. The monotheists have a long history of intolerance to differing beliefs, even within their own faiths. The end results are people pissed/offended/etc. because they don't feel G-D is almighty enough, too almighty, inaccurately portrayed, too heavy handed, to separation of church and game.<br /> <br /> Please, please, please, by the gods, do not make Scion the Sunday Schooling. Just my two cents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/783-xsv-violence","name":"Xsv-Violence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar783_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T17:21:41-08:00","id":3881,"title":"","content":"Monotheists arent the only group to oppress people.... That kind of as arguement doesn't belong here","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T19:58:06-08:00","id":3961,"title":"","content":"Intolerance and oppression are not the same thing, even though they tend to go hand in hand. Monotheism is largely opposed to polytheism, in a bad way, in such a degree it's quite simple to construe it like a Titan. This doesn't sit well with many whom consider their supreme being the good guy. To accurately portray the &quot;myth&quot; correctly means to have a whole lot of conflict with the pantheons. If not portrayed the greatest, sole divine being, can, and will be construed as an attack on their belief. So if one doesn't portray them as an opposing, force of creation (greater Titan), what than? As a pantheon? Even though it isn't one? Do we mix the ideas up, like an over done Hollywood tripe and portray Hades as a Satan like figure?<br /> <br /> Other reasons to largely ignore it is just look at Ahketaten. The Titan based on an actual Egyptian Monotheist religion. The Titan stirred up it's own controversy for it's similarities to the Abrahamic faith, which it ironically had enough similarities in real life to be construed as the founding root of the faiths by the likes of Freud. The point I am making here is that this had some not happy with it's &quot;similarities&quot;, imagine going with an actual portrayal. On the other side of it, there are those whom do not want anything to do with it. <br /> <br /> If you portray it factually you might please those of faith, and irritate those that don't by watering down the myths they love, much like how we tire of how they do the myths on film. If you don't portray it factual, you entertain some, but irritate the faithful whom tire of &quot;attacks&quot; on their beliefs.<br /> <br /> This is the intolerance to which I speak, the easy to offend and be offended. <br /> <br /> If you don't actually take a stance, most people don't care, and the ones that really want it in their game can write their own version of Abrahams &quot;pantheon&quot;. I personally think a set of guidelines for writing up pantheons we want that aren't the main ones are the best way to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/783-xsv-violence","name":"Xsv-Violence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar783_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T20:36:40-08:00","id":3973,"title":"","content":"Eh. I still say that Onyx Path shouldn\u2019t be making design decisions based off of who will be offended, but rather on what will make for the most interesting story possibilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T21:09:08-08:00","id":3987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=3973#post3973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. I still say that Onyx Path shouldn\u2019t be making design decisions based off of who will be offended, but rather on what will make for the most interesting story possibilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>SMT sure as hell doesn't care and it tends to have an extremely high fanbase. As for an Abrahamic pantheon, anything can work and anything can be interesting it just depends on how much effort is put and the angles responsible as well as the friction between PCs. They have to be done in a way the doesn't cause too many issues. I don't think you can do anything without offending someone though. It's just life .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T21:10:12-08:00","id":3989,"title":"","content":"Thank You Data. Too many stories are cheapened because someone wasn't willing to take the risk to offend. We trade greatness for normality way too much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T21:33:08-08:00","id":4008,"title":"","content":"You know, if this were just a little bit different, it would be awesome.<br /> <br /> If you had Yahweh as one part of a pantheon of gods from the Levant area, alongside Baal and Dagon and Moloch and all the other Caananite/Phonecians (that later JudeoChristians literally demonized) and made it that he's no more or less powerful than his peers, but his Scions/Avatars/Followers/whathaveyou managed to get REALLY LUCKY in founding a religion that stuck, I'd find THAT an incredibly compelling mythological take on it. <br /> <br /> Certainly moreso than the archangel and saints stuff that's, honestly, been done to death","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T21:58:59-08:00","id":4031,"title":"","content":"Certainly, if a Caananite Pantheon ever gets published, it should address its relationship to the Abrahamic faiths. I saw one fan writeup of such a Pantheon where Yahweh was missing, with lots of theories about what happened to him but nothing conclusive, and the implication that he might be the god that was Fatebound by the Order of Divinity (or whatever the group in <b>Companion</b> was called).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T22:57:48-08:00","id":4085,"title":"","content":"Canaanite Pantheon would be cool, including Yahweh. That would be a pantheon, fitting with the polytheistic theme. It's a far cry different from the monotheistic faiths, it's not the all supreme being creator that is the omnipotent alpha and omega that is supreme above all (Titans included) that contradicts the entire premise of Scion. <br /> <br /> I am not against offending someone, I personally would link Ahketaten to Yahweh as apposed to strikingly similar. From a business standpoint though, I think a pragmaticly neutral approach makes more sense as there is little to gain from literal interpretation or reinterpretation. <br /> <br /> My viewpoint is simply this...<br /> <br /> How does it improve the game to butcher the myth of other cultures to fit the myths of abraham? Or to butcher the myths of Abraham to fit the myths of the other myths?<br /> <br /> How does it improve the game to take a myth with so many passionate interpretations, from faith and lack thereof, and define it?<br /> <br /> How will adding it improve the genre, feel, and spirit of the game?<br /> <br /> How will adding it improve the experience of the myth, when we have to already sift through the Monotheist rewrites of the existing myths?<br /> <br /> How is adding it not trying to fit a square peg in a round hole?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/783-xsv-violence","name":"Xsv-Violence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar783_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T23:11:40-08:00","id":4098,"title":"","content":"Have you seen <i>anyone</i> asking for a supreme being creator who is the omnipotent alpha and omega and that is supreme above all (Titans included) to be added to <b>Scion</b>? I haven\u2019t. Frankly, characterizing requests to include something about Abrahamic faiths in <b>Scion</b> in such an extreme way is a strawman argument, and I wish you\u2019d stop it.<br /> <br /> As for your other questions, they\u2019re about as fair as \u201chave you stopped beating your wife?\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-06-2013, 02:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T00:05:35-08:00","id":4123,"title":"","content":"But all suggestions of an Abrahamic Pantheon carry that supreme-above-all-others baggage. If you handwave away the presence/existence/activity of God, that's going entirely against the main tenant of Abrahamic religions: that God IS present, He IS active and He IS Supreme. You have to compromise monotheism to make it fit with polytheism, or you have to compromise the setting of the game itself to incorporate unadulterated monotheism.<br /> <br /> They just don't play well together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T00:12:21-08:00","id":4126,"title":"","content":"Then compromise a bit on the \u201csupreme power\u201d thing. It\u2019s not like other mythologies haven\u2019t been compromised to varying extents to get them to fit into <b>Scion</b>\u2019s premise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T06:36:44-08:00","id":4261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=4123#post4123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But all suggestions of an Abrahamic Pantheon carry that supreme-above-all-others baggage. If you handwave away the presence/existence/activity of God, that's going entirely against the main tenant of Abrahamic religions: that God IS present, He IS active and He IS Supreme. You have to compromise monotheism to make it fit with polytheism, or you have to compromise the setting of the game itself to incorporate unadulterated monotheism.<br /> <br /> They just don't play well together.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't carry any baggage, you guys are the only ones that are even insinuating God would be the be-all-end-all-other-Gods-are-suckas-compared-to-him. As Dataweaver said, it doesn't even matter that things would need to be compromised and frankly I don't see why you're dragging your heels so much so to speak","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T07:06:49-08:00","id":4278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=4123#post4123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But all suggestions of an Abrahamic Pantheon carry that supreme-above-all-others baggage. If you handwave away the presence/existence/activity of God, that's going entirely against the main tenant of Abrahamic religions: that God IS present, He IS active and He IS Supreme. You have to compromise monotheism to make it fit with polytheism, or you have to compromise the setting of the game itself to incorporate unadulterated monotheism.<br /> <br /> They just don't play well together.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe we discussed this once but Shiva doesn't have the ability to destroy the universe and neither does Brahma's solipsism trigger the end of it either by waking up in Scion. There are a lot of deities who aren't nearly as powerful as their own myths would imply. You are assuming that half the restrictions that apply to other gods that have such myth tied to them wouldn't apply to an Abrahamic Pantheon when that doesn't make any sense. It would all have to conform together like it currently does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T07:18:16-08:00","id":4286,"title":"","content":"The &quot;some people might be offended&quot; argument seems weak to me, because that didn't stop them from including the Abrahamic faith as a Titan sham and nobody seemed to get up in arms as far as I'm aware","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":245,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","user":"Egg","date":". 11-06-2013, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T07:22:24-08:00","id":4291,"title":"","content":"If I recall correctly, Thor with his hammer is kinda off-scale when it comes to the level of destruction he can dish out.<br /> And if &quot;current worship in this reality&quot; has any influence in a person's gaming experience, Norse deities aren't really worshipped much today when compared to the big three which are flourishing; Christian, Islam, and Hindu.<br /> And even though the Scion game doesn't mention it, a few Hindu deities have mystic weapons that are easily on a par with Thor's hammer.<br /> I don't want to think what an Abrahamic deity-weapon could be.<br /> <br /> *shrugs* Reading the back and forth, Abrahamic deities probably aren't doable, unless one sticks to Semitic and Sumerian deities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T07:26:52-08:00","id":4293,"title":"","content":"XSM-violence, I think you're being pretty intolerant yourself. It's a fair point that many monotheistic believers are intolerant, but it's no different than what you are doing right here, by labeling the faithful in a mostly liberal and open-minded demographic as being intolerant and unable to accept the limitations of Scion to portray Allah, Yahweh, or Jesus. No one is asking for an all-powerful super-being that breaks Scion. No one is asking people to compromise mythology to serve their inclusion in a game. I'm even Christian and I really don't have an interest in playing as a Scion of Jesus in the standard setting. I want to play a variant setting based on the apocalyptic prophecies of Daniel and Revelations if I was to have rules for an Abrahamic pantheon.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thinking as I do that the Creator of this World is a very Cruel Being &amp; being a Worshipper of Christ, I cannot help saying: &quot;the Son, O how unlike the Father!&quot; First God Almighty comes with a Thump on the Head. Then Jesus Christ comes with a balm to heal it. - William Blake, Christian mystic and visionary","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/774-pilgrim","name":"Pilgrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar774_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T07:30:59-08:00","id":4297,"title":"","content":"And Arabic ones, unless you consider Allah to be a Semitic or Sumerian deity. <br /> <br /> Last I checked, gods aren\u2019t empowered by worship in <b>Scion</b>. That may change in 2e; but at least for now, being one of the most worshipped Pantheons in the modern world doesn\u2019t make the Vedas notably more powerful than the other Pantheons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T07:43:18-08:00","id":4307,"title":"","content":"I thought some Gods had a knack which allowed them to gain Legend Points or something when they heard a prayer or something? I haven't really played Scion in a while but that's what I thought.<br /> <br /> Also. I'm pretty sure Allah is supposed to be Yahweh. If the developers actually did do an Abrahamic Pantheon, I could see different conceptions of God being counted as different &quot;Gods&quot; for the purposes of the pantheon. El Shaddai is pretty different from Yahweh and Jesus for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thinking as I do that the Creator of this World is a very Cruel Being &amp; being a Worshipper of Christ, I cannot help saying: &quot;the Son, O how unlike the Father!&quot; First God Almighty comes with a Thump on the Head. Then Jesus Christ comes with a balm to heal it. - William Blake, Christian mystic and visionary","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/774-pilgrim","name":"Pilgrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar774_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T07:57:03-08:00","id":4314,"title":"","content":"being a new comer to this forum....would anyone mind seeing the &quot;Elohim&quot; I created? it might be a good idea for the story of them and some of their abilities and stuff...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/622-showzilla","name":"showzilla","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T07:59:20-08:00","id":4316,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://johnsscionresources.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">John\u2019s Scion Resources</a>, referenced earlier in this thread, has some interesting insights concerning the likes of Allah, El, Yahweh, and others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T08:11:14-08:00","id":4327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pilgrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=4293#post4293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I want to play a variant setting based on the apocalyptic prophecies of Daniel and Revelations if I was to have rules for an Abrahamic pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forgive me but, if that's the case, and we all agree that creating a &quot;first among equals&quot; pantheon won't do any good to the line, would not be easier to do it as a fanmade project? Or, and I really hope you don't get me wrong here, play another game?<br /> <br /> I'm saying that in the most diplomatic way possible. Lots of people want the Abrahamic pantheon in Scion. Not Semitic, not Sumerian nor Canaanite: they want the Abrahamic (and Arabic) ones. On the other side, lots of other people would hate to have it portrayed in the game. I honestly cannot discern if, on both sides, this is more a case of vocal groups expressing their ideas and thus they should not really have an impact on the line development (again, in a way or the other), but I think we can agree that the Abrahamic pantheon, if written as asked, is going to be different from the others. I mean, a quick example, angels, saints and prophets as gods? I'm not saying that's wrong, but it's different from all the other pantheons and for a reason that can be resumed as &quot;just because&quot;. As for the Loa (and the possibility of a Yoruba pantheon), the devs said they are going to be quite different in 2E, so we'll have to wait.<br /> <br /> I suggest the &quot;fanmade&quot; option for the simple reason that if you have to distance yourself too much from the rules of the setting and make exceptions just to shoehorn the Abrahamic in the &quot;canon&quot; game, I can't see why that would be a good idea. Not to mention that there are a lot of other interesting pantheons out there that would prove to be a lot easier and painless to add to Scion for the writers and developers. For those of you who suggest having the Abrahamic pantheon in a separate supplement, in a separate setting, in a separate context, I don't think the relatively limited resources of the line (what? I love Scion but let's be fair, guys) should be used to throw a bone to a part of the fanbase.<br /> <br /> And I'm saying this as the guy who wrote the longest unofficial pantheon on the old forum, so I can get what people are feeling when they say they have cool ideas and plot hooks in mind. I still think that an Abrahamic pantheon would cause more problems than it's worth. Semitic and Sumerian pantheons? Not nearly as much (if at all).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 11-06-2013, 11:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T08:13:28-08:00","id":4329,"title":"","content":"I personally think that an abrahamic pantheon would not only be doable but relatively easy with how much deity like beings are in the religious lore. Most of it taken from fiction like Dante and Milton. Many of the named angels could easily be re branded &quot;god&quot; instead and many works depict the angelic host as being familial anyway so it will be very much like many of the other pantheons. <br /> <br /> Personal opinion here, but I really don't care that the abrahamic religions are largely monotheistic. The world of Scion is really not the world that we live in so it doesn't have to be. All that I really care about is the intriguing story potential of say: the scion of Michael and the Scion of Raziel who find each other and other scions of other pantheons. Raziel and Michael want nothing more than both of their children to go along and be good friends but in actuality they really can't stand each other. I can think of other combinations and interesting plans and cool story hooks.<br /> <br /> And in the end, the story is really all that matters to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T08:58:30-08:00","id":4377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=4327#post4327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but I think we can agree that the Abrahamic pantheon, if written as asked, is going to be different from the others. I mean, a quick example, angels, saints and prophets as gods? I'm not saying that's wrong, but it's different from all the other pantheons and for a reason that can be resumed as &quot;just because&quot;. As for the Loa (and the possibility of a Yoruba pantheon), the devs said they are going to be quite different in 2E, so we'll have to wait.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find the juxtaposition of these two statements to be an interesting one. On the one hand, an Abrahamic Pantheon would be \u201cdifferent from the others\u201d \u2014 because we all know exactly what \u201cthe others\u201d are going to be like in the second edition. On the other hand, the Loa are going to be \u201cquite different\u201d, in as-yet unspecified ways\u2026<br /> <br /> My point is that we don\u2019t know enough about the second edition to know if an Abrahamic Pantheon could be made to work in it or not. A lot of assumptions have been getting tossed around here, both in terms of what an Abrahamic Pantheon would \u201cnecessarily\u201d entail and in terms of what the second edition of <b>Scion</b> is going to be like. I\u2019ve made some suggestions for how <b>Scion</b>'s basic framework could be opened up a bit to allow for more flexibility in representing <i>numerous</i>\u200b mythologies, changes that would have the fringe benefit of making it easier to incorporate Abrahamic mythology into the setting if you\u2019re so inclined; for all we know at this stage, the development team may have had similar thoughts. Or not; it\u2019s too early to say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T09:26:29-08:00","id":4405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=4377#post4377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find the juxtaposition of these two statements to be an interesting one. On the one hand, an Abrahamic Pantheon would be \u201cdifferent from the others\u201d \u2014 because we all know exactly what \u201cthe others\u201d are going to be like in the second edition. On the other hand, the Loa are going to be \u201cquite different\u201d, in as-yet unspecified ways\u2026<br /> <br /> My point is that we don\u2019t know enough about the second edition to know if an Abrahamic Pantheon could be made to work in it or not. A lot of assumptions have been getting tossed around here, both in terms of what an Abrahamic Pantheon would \u201cnecessarily\u201d entail and in terms of what the second edition of <b>Scion</b> is going to be like. I\u2019ve made some suggestions for how <b>Scion</b>'s basic framework could be opened up a bit to allow for more flexibility in representing <i>numerous</i>\u200b mythologies, changes that would have the fringe benefit of making it easier to incorporate Abrahamic mythology into the setting if you\u2019re so inclined; for all we know at this stage, the development team may have had similar thoughts. Or not; it\u2019s too early to say.</div> </div> </div> </div>The juxtaposition was more a case of &quot;I have to put a sentence about the Loa somewhere&quot; than a Freudian slip of sorts but, given that the devs went out to say that the Loa are going to be different (not much, but still) and said even less about other pantheons, I think that for now it's fair to think they are not going to be changed as much as the Loa (or the Yoruba. Or whatever else they're going to be in 2E). You'll notice I haven't said anything about how we &quot;exactly&quot; know something about the game, and how my previous post was not as arrogant as you've depicted it but, hey, feel free ignore the rest of my answer to make some sarcasm...<br /> <br /> I have not said that doing an Abrahamic pantheon would necessarily entail something. I'm saying that, <i>if</i> that the game does not change too much <i>and </i>the hypothetical Abrahamic pantheon is written along the line of what the fanbase is asking for, it's going to be problematic. We know the devs are discussing its inclusion, and they have said that, even among them, that's been a complex topic. Now, I have no way to predict how 2E will be (and I've never said that), nor what they exactly meant with that, but at least we can discuss in a general way, basing oursevelves on what we've got. I know 2E may be completely different, but there's no point in having a discussion if we can't ignore the fact that, for now, the Second Edition is a &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Schr\u00f6dinger's Edition&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, that said, to return to my central point: <i>provided </i>that 2E's setting and the pantheons are not too much different from those of the first one, would not be easier and better for the game to avoid the Abrahamic pantheon (again, not Semitic or Sumerian, but the kind of pantheon most people are asking for in this thread) and write it ourself?</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 11-06-2013, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T09:38:17-08:00","id":4416,"title":"","content":"I think a pantheon based upon the God of Christians, Islam, and Jews would ruin the flavor I think that Scion has.<br /> <br /> Sure, I can see the angels in Christianity, and Judaism, and the Jinn (as well as angels) in Islam. But I don't think I want to hear about a grudge match between a scion of Ra and a scion of Michael. Which I suppose in that interpretation both would be referred to as Nephilim or Elioud..or even better, Bene Elohim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T09:42:40-08:00","id":4420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, and I really hope you don't get me wrong here, play another game?</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason why I'd want to use the Scion rules is that they are simple and easy(compared to other systems) while maintaining the sort of feel that I appreciate about the core game. I personally would want something along the lines of taking the system of Scion and using it in other similar but different settings. To me, the idea of the anagelic hosts of heaven waging a massive war against the spawn of Satan isn't that different from the core assumptions of massive mythic forces such as waging war against each other. A setting hack like the Mirrors book for NWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thinking as I do that the Creator of this World is a very Cruel Being &amp; being a Worshipper of Christ, I cannot help saying: &quot;the Son, O how unlike the Father!&quot; First God Almighty comes with a Thump on the Head. Then Jesus Christ comes with a balm to heal it. - William Blake, Christian mystic and visionary","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/774-pilgrim","name":"Pilgrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar774_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T09:55:57-08:00","id":4430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pilgrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=4420#post4420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A setting hack like the Mirrors book for NWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some sort of &quot;Book of the Pantheons and Stuff we would have loved to do but don't really fit into the setting*&quot;? I can get behind this. I don't think it should be among the first priorities of the gameline, but still.<br /> <br /> Hell, I would even buy that. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *If the setting is not too much different from that of 1st Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 11-06-2013, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T10:02:19-08:00","id":4434,"title":"","content":"That strikes me funny...seeing the angels led by the seven virtues; Humility, Charity, Kindness, Patience, Chastity, Temperance, and Diligence fighting against the demonic forces led by the seven sins; Wrath, Greed, Sloth, Lust, Pride, Envy, and Gluttony. And seeing the likes of Odin and Zeus in the background collecting wagers...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T11:55:06-08:00","id":4497,"title":"","content":"if you're writing an Abrahamic Pantheon, you've got to wonder: which God is your God? the vengeful one of the old testament, the redemptive of the new? is it a unitarian deity? a trinitarian? there are a whole bunch of questions that'd need to be addressed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T11:59:10-08:00","id":4498,"title":"","content":"If I were to write it I would not include God at all","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T12:36:17-08:00","id":4520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=4498#post4498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were to write it I would not include God at all</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't Yahweh the entire point of an Abrahamic pantheon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T13:01:05-08:00","id":4537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guitarsniper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=4520#post4520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't Yahweh the entire point of an Abrahamic pantheon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to me anyway.<br /> <br /> I just think the Angels, various other celestial beings (Thrones, etc), and the Abrahamic Mythology are neat and would be interesting to explore in the world of Scion.<br /> <br /> Horses with scorpion tails!<br /> Behemoths!<br /> Giant sea leviathans!<br /> Cockatrice!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T13:15:02-08:00","id":4550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=4098#post4098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you seen <i>anyone</i> asking for a supreme being creator who is the omnipotent alpha and omega and that is supreme above all (Titans included) to be added to <b>Scion</b>? I haven\u2019t. Frankly, characterizing requests to include something about Abrahamic faiths in <b>Scion</b> in such an extreme way is a strawman argument, and I wish you\u2019d stop it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry you feel I am putting up a strawman. The point is, which seems to be missed, is that to present the &quot;myth&quot; you either have to water it down or rewrite it (then what is the point as it is no longer the myth) or you have to do that treatment to all the other myths in the game. Is that my opinion? Sure. <br /> <br /> I'm also of the opinion that Yahweh has more in common with a Titan, largely due to the myths. He is distant, a force of nature, and largely acts through proxies, acts of god, and symbolism. It's pretty hard to have a pantheon of one, though Avatars representing the different personas as a Titan can represent the differing religious perspectives. Since Titans aren't necessarily evil, there is a lot of ground to work with here. <br /> <br /> That's all my opinion, and I haven't argued for that, though maybe one should... Which would then leave the question does either interpretation enhance the game for the majority of players? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=4098#post4098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for your other questions, they\u2019re about as fair as \u201chave you stopped beating your wife?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>How does asking you &quot;How does adding it improve the genre, feel, and spirit of the game?&quot; equate to &quot;have you stopped beating your wife?&quot;<br /> <br /> Let me rephrase it for you, &quot;How does adding it improve the genre, feel, spirit of the game, for <b><i>the majority who will play the game</i></b>?&quot; <br /> <br /> Do we 1) add it as a Titan opposing the Canaanite Pantheon or as a member? 2) water it down to fit the other myths? 3) just not add it except as a house rule as done with 1e so that we can play to each our own?<br /> <br /> I personally like Option 1, though I have been advocating option 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/783-xsv-violence","name":"Xsv-Violence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar783_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T13:22:44-08:00","id":4558,"title":"","content":"WE ALREADY WATERDOWN A LOT OF MYTHS. This is fucking bullshit. The Aztecs believe they created the universe and destroyed it five times. The Hindu's believe their major deities consistently destroy and bring it back. If I looked into other Pantheons I would find this happens more often than not. There are a lot of Myths that have been watered down to make it fit into scion. What honestly makes this something special? Why do you think it can't be watered down when it's already happened?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T13:36:09-08:00","id":4566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=4558#post4558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WE ALREADY WATERDOWN A LOT OF MYTHS. This is fucking bullshit. The Aztecs believe they created the universe and destroyed it five times. The Hindu's believe their major deities consistently destroy and bring it back. If I looked into other Pantheons I would find this happens more often than not. There are a lot of Myths that have been watered down to make it fit into scion. What honestly makes this something special? Why do you think it can't be watered down when it's already happened?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been ignoring this thread since I really don't think anything asides from a bitter argument can develop from this debate, with no side ever actually winning. But, I really need to step in here and just say that I have never played in a game where any of those myths were watered down. I have never heard of a game where those things are watered down. And I do not believe I ever remember these things being watered down in RAW.<br /> <br /> All of those myths are true. This is the fifth world for the Aztecs. They've broken it four times in the past and have changed who is the Sun over the eras. At the same time, for the Hindu Gods, all of reality is an illusion and the world is in a constant cycle of destruction and restoration. (An incredibly easy way to include this in a game is to have the Titan War be one of these destructions.) Every ST can rule how all of these things are true in different ways. Maybe the creation myths all just revolve around &quot;The World&quot; in the idea of the known world for that culture. So each Pantheon or Creator Figure just made their culture's area. Maybe the prior worlds the Aztecs have broken were Terra Incognita, or they just keep remaking their own part of the world.<br /> <br /> It, of course, is a ST's option to water those things down if they wish. But that is an individual's choice. They are not watered down in any of the games I have played, and not, as far as I can remember, in core.<br /> <br /> While this conversation is getting out of hand, because it always has every time we have had it, devolving into throwing caps around and declaring this to be &quot;fucking bullshit&quot; is a bit much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T13:41:56-08:00","id":4568,"title":"","content":"As per the Core RAW. There is literally no Pantheon capable of reproducing their creation and rebirth cycles moreover they all contradict each other. I'm just mad at the fact that we are talking about one religion's myth being toned down when they all have. Unless we go with your point of view in which they haven't been toned down. Christianity isn't the only religion with all powerful figures. It's just annoying me that we keeping going on to a point that has no bearing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 11-06-2013, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T14:19:44-08:00","id":4588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=4568#post4568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As per the Core RAW. There is literally no Pantheon capable of reproducing their creation and rebirth cycles moreover they all contradict each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Creation myths mostly use Avatars. Avatars have no limits on how powerful they are as long as they stay inside their area of focus. Most pantheons are entirely capable of preforming their creation myths because of this, with the only immediate exceptions to this that pop to mind being the Tuatha de Dannan who don't have one and just show up one day, and the Aesir since creating a world from a corpse is a bit different then the standard. Although the Babylonians do the same actually on second thought.<br /> <br /> The Greek creation myths function with use of Purview Avatars, the Egyptian, and Aztec. I am sure I could give more examples, but those are the only ones I am totally sure of off the top of my head. <br /> <br /> I don't quite want to get into the contradiction stuff because that would end up with me having to argue about the whole Monotheism situation. But, the way I generally see it is that they are all right because the myths never say that, &quot;We are right and they are wrong.&quot;. The Aztecs codexes don't say that the Cree creation myth is wrong, the Hindu Gods don't say the Chinese creation myth is wrong. In the Theogony we never have Hesiod saying, &quot;This is how the world was made, and those bloody people up north who can't say anything but 'barbarbar' are wrong.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T14:28:09-08:00","id":4592,"title":"","content":"Avatars are kind of a gray area in my opinion because we don't know how powerful they are which leaves them up to the ST which means an ST can go either way.<br /> <br /> Religions tend not toexplicitly say it but they imply the idea that they are incompatible with other religions. I mean I guess you can argue that because they don't say it that there is an explicit statement that it's cohesive but I can't honestly believe that one religion wouldn't place it's beliefs above others. Personally, I'm of the mind that these are myths. That most of these events didn't take place or were skewed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T14:43:06-08:00","id":4605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=4592#post4592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Avatars are kind of a gray area in my opinion because we don't know how powerful they are which leaves them up to the ST which means an ST can go either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, Scion: God explains the power of Avatars as so. &quot;[The Deity's] power over that Purview increases from quantifiable traits and game mechanics to narrative effects that can change the course of a whole cycle in one fell swoop. Each [Purview] Avatar has a write-up of suggested ways it can affect the action of the story. Becoming the Avatar of a Purview also allows the character to use any Boon of that Purview free of charge, without any dice roll and to an extent limited only by imagination&quot; (Scion: God, pg 80.)<br /> <br /> A God, Goddess, NPC or PC, who assumes a Purview Avatar can do anything they can imagine as long as it relates to the Purview. They can use entirely un-written Boons. Becoming The Reaper and giving eternal life to an entire species. Or use written Boons, such as using Create Earth with an infinite number of successes. And then Shaping with an infinite number of successes. And so on and so forth. The power of Avatars is very plainly stared RAW as &quot;limited only by imagination.&quot;, that is not a grey area in the slightest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=4592#post4592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Religions tend not toexplicitly say it but they imply the idea that they are incompatible with other religions. I mean I guess you can argue that because they don't say it that there is an explicit statement that it's cohesive but I can't honestly believe that one religion wouldn't place it's beliefs above others. Personally, I'm of the mind that these are myths. That most of these events didn't take place or were skewed.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an entirely acceptable personal stance to take on how things function in your games. But, that is not how it functions rules as written. All myths are true RAW. Despite the issues that such a thing presents when you have a countless number of Sun-beings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T14:47:28-08:00","id":4611,"title":"","content":"Really? I haven't honestly seen a definitive answer for All Myths Are Real in Scion. If you could point me too it'd have no problem disagreeing. It doesn't actually change my original point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T14:59:23-08:00","id":4620,"title":"","content":"Well, to be honest, the Supreme status is not the only issue. Nor the only reason I make for using the term watering down.<br /> <br /> It's the lack of a pantheon, one has to essentially make one up. Angels aren't gods, but his created minions (they usually don't have free will), even if they are powerful. Also according to the myth, the offspring of Angel and Man is abomination and largely the reason for flooding the earth. Jesus would be the only technical Scion, the rest are simply chosen Heroes and prophets. Unlike most of the other myths, Yahweh is largely impersonal, and elemental in nature (burning bush, radiant light, etc). Quite frankly these are some of the very reasons I think Yahweh is more like a Titan (Justice or Light) than a god (as defined by Scion and Myth) and just some of the things one must rewrite to fit the theme in the game if one want a &quot;pantheon&quot;.<br /> <br /> If you rewrite the Myth (meaning all the basics), whats the flippin point of including it? Either way, it really doesn't matter as it all breaks down to these points of view...<br /> <br /> I want to be a Scion of Yahweh and his host of Angels...<br /> <br /> I don't think it fits the theme, and I don't want this in the Core or Game...<br /> <br /> I think it fits to have him as part of the Canaanite Pantheon, possibly as a Titan, but not as a pantheon of one...<br /> <br /> I think this is a highly polarized topic, probably best to leave it out...<br /> <br /> I don't care, can we move on already...<br /> <br /> I doubt this forum will come to an accord on this, judging by the prior threads on this topic. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/783-xsv-violence","name":"Xsv-Violence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar783_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T15:03:29-08:00","id":4623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=4611#post4611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? I haven't honestly seen a definitive answer for All Myths Are Real in Scion. If you could point me too it'd have no problem disagreeing. It doesn't actually change my original point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, your presentations of evidence to support your original point haven't swayed me, and my counter points have not swayed you, and if pointing you to more would just have me disagreed with, unless that is a typo there, I don't believe there is any reason for us to continue this back and forth. Neither of us will convince the other to chance their convictions on the matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T15:06:27-08:00","id":4624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=4623#post4623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, your presentations of evidence to support your original point haven't swayed me, and my counter points have not swayed you, and if pointing you to more would just have me disagreed with, unless that is a typo there, I don't believe there is any reason for us to continue this back and forth. Neither of us will convince the other to chance their convictions on the matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>You said All Myths Being Real was written in the gameline. At least from what I could infer you did. I just want to know what book it's in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T15:09:36-08:00","id":4629,"title":"","content":"Seriously, all these arguments have been made at least a dozen times, and mostly by the same people saying the same things. It's an <b><i>extremely</i></b> contentious issue <i>among the player base</i>. I think including a &quot;Pantheon&quot; of Angels or Saints would be a big mistake for Scion with a remarkably small benefit. <br /> <br /> Because, honestly, when you read about a game of ancient mythology come to life in the modern era, do you think of playing the son of the Metatron? I sure don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T15:12:33-08:00","id":4634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=4624#post4624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You said All Myths Being Real was written in the gameline. At least from what I could infer you did. I just want to know what book it's in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I believe I misunderstood the &quot;If you could point me too it'd have no problem disagreeing&quot; line then. Terribly sorry. I believe the section that talks about it is in Scion: God when it is detailing cosmology. I believe it is in reference to the proliferation of Sun figures who are all technically the Sun, even though there is only one.<br /> <br /> My copy of God is a physical copy, so searching through the entire thing would take a great deal of time. Especially if I am wrong about the location and it's somewhere with the Titans. If the Purview Avatar section hadn't been labeled with big bold letters, and in an obvious place, I wouldn't have bothered to put in the direct quotations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 11-06-2013, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T15:23:39-08:00","id":4646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=4629#post4629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, all these arguments have been made at least a dozen times, and mostly by the same people saying the same things. It's an <b><i>extremely</i></b> contentious issue <i>among the player base</i>. I think including a &quot;Pantheon&quot; of Angels or Saints would be a big mistake for Scion with a remarkably small benefit.<br /> <br /> Because, honestly, when you read about a game of ancient mythology come to life in the modern era, do you think of playing the son of the Metatron? I sure don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>The option would be interesting but you'd have to use Canaanites.<br /> <br /> Also, don't try to use the quote button more than one person it'll eat up your post. Apparently the forums can't support more than one quote. But I'll check God out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T15:58:29-08:00","id":4682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=4646#post4646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The option would be interesting but you'd have to use Canaanites.<br /> <br /> Also, don't try to use the quote button more than one person it'll eat up your post. Apparently the forums can't support more than one quote. But I'll check God out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking at how contentious this topic is maybe I was wrong. I guess people other than me feel more strongly how the abrahamic pantheon is represented in the medium. <br /> <br /> Still, seeing as how OPP designs their stuff to be more of a toolbox then a thing that STs and players should take from wholesale, what does designing and adding a pantheon such as this do that would make it a bad thing to add? From where I'm standing, worst case scenario is the ST and Players don't use it. And it seems that at least half of the posters on this topic would be interested no matter how it's represented so I don't really see any real downsides.<br /> <br /> Although I guess it's not a big deal if they don't include it, someone could just make it them selves. Pantheons seem pretty easy to create.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T16:05:41-08:00","id":4686,"title":"","content":"Honestly, my issue has nothing to do with the Abrahamic Pantheon specifically but the idea that it can't be made and made well. I'm always of the mind that if it's interesting you can create it especially in a setting like Scion. There are so many Myths and so many Pantheons it wouldn't be impossible nor would it be all that difficult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T16:11:26-08:00","id":4688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xsv-Violence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=4620#post4620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt this forum will come to an accord on this, judging by the prior threads on this topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that this is the first thread on this topic on the new forums; so it serves the purpose of establishing what everyone\u2019s positions are. Once it has done that, the lack of consensus means that there\u2019s little point in continuing. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=4646#post4646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The option would be interesting but you'd have to use Canaanites.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fine by me. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=4646#post4646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, don't try to use the quote button more than one person it'll eat up your post. Apparently the forums can't support more than one quote. But I'll check God out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nitpick: multi-quoting is working fine for me. You need to select the posts you wish to quote, then hit the \u201cPost Reply (x)\u201d button in the upper left-hand corner of the screen. What the new forums don't support are nested quotes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T16:46:06-08:00","id":4717,"title":"","content":"I would stand behind the Canaanite Pantheon, though I don't know a whole lot about it other than a couple of the gods namely, Yahweh, Molech, and Baal.<br /> <br /> So what about tying Yahweh to Logos?<br /> <br /> Logos, the primordial embodiment of order and justice, was never imprisoned. Her avatars Themis, Syn and Ma\u2019at accepted limitations. - Scion - God<br /> <br /> It would nicely explain why Yahweh departed the pantheon, his strong following/presence in the world, his nature, etc. Just a thought...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/783-xsv-violence","name":"Xsv-Violence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar783_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T16:46:42-08:00","id":4718,"title":"","content":"From <a href=\"http://www.bidstrup.com/bible.htm\" target=\"_blank\">this essay</a> <i><br /> <br /> Yet influences from the east must have been, because we have evidence of worship of their gods and goddesses.<br /> The heiarchy of gods and goddesses who included Baal, the god of storms, who made the land fertile, and Lotan, the seven-headed dragon, known to Old Testament readers as Leviathan. There is Yam Nahar, the god of the seas and rivers, and other pantheons and heiarchies of gods and goddesses. <b>Reigning over them all was El, the king of the gods</b>, ruler of the pantheon. Remember the name, we'll encounter it again.<br /> <br /> Prior to the Babylonian exile, we know that the Israelites followed a wide variety of cults, most of which were polytheistic, and the cult of Yahweh was a relatively minor cult among the Israelites during this period that has been greatly revised over time. We know, for example, that the narrative of the Yahweh included a wife. Her name was Asherah, though in related cults she had different names, including Astarte and Istar. She was a powerful, important, even indispensible part of the cult, mostly related to fertility. We know that she figured prominently throughout the pre-Roman period, as she appears frequently in inscriptions and on figurines prior to the Assyrian expulsion and to a lesser extent afterwards. She remained a major figure in the Old Testament narratives, though as time went on, she was gradually edited out by subsequent copyists and editors, disappearing almost completely from the Old Testament narrative by about the 8th Century, though traces of this cult figure remain even today in the Old Testament. ...<br /> <br /> We now know this Mesopotamian god as &quot;El-ohim,&quot; and our author &quot;E,&quot; one of the earliest scriptorialists writing about this time, first has <b>El introducing himself to Abraham as &quot;El Shaddai&quot; (El of the Mountain)</b>. He also appears as El Elyon, or El of Bethel in other, non-canonized scripture, and his name is also preserved in such Hebrew names as Isra-El and Ishma-El. The word Elohim was originally a plural of El. To the south, from Bethel to the Valley of Beersheba, a similar transformation is taking place. In this climatically and geologically harsher place, a place with a much smaller and less settled population with greater geographical isolation, the Canaanite god Yahweh is being transformed by a culturally similar people of the land of Judah. The unknown author known to scholars simply as &quot;J&quot; has his god being familiar with and comfortable with Abraham, and he casually appears to Abraham in Genesis 18, introducing himself as Yahweh. But &quot;J's&quot; contemporary, author &quot;E&quot; in the north can't have God being so casual, and first appears as a voice, commanding Abraham to leave his people in Mesopotamia and settle in Canaan. Yahweh, in his transformation from a pagan Canaanite god to the god of the Jews, becomes a cruel and vindictive god in the hands of author &quot;J.&quot; He commands Abraham to sacrifice his first born son, an act which is not at all surprising given the nature of the pagan religions of the time. Many of these pagan religions (and remember that Yahweh got his start as a Canannite pagan god) considered the first-born to be the seed of a god. Because of this, they were often sacrificed to the god who presumably sired them. Yet Elohim in the north continues to be a much more subtle god, who directs the affairs of men by revelation of the voice, hidden from the view of mere mortals. There is a tension among these peoples, both of whom identify themselves as culturally descendants of Abraham, Isaac and Jacob. One people, perhaps, but two gods. </i><br /> <br /> Hmm.. <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Deities_in_the_Hebrew_Bible\" target=\"_blank\">Deities in the Hebrew Bible</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","user":"Shadowflame","date":". 11-06-2013, 11:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T16:53:58-08:00","id":4723,"title":"","content":"Is there some reason why I can't edit my post?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T17:24:30-08:00","id":4738,"title":"","content":"You will find an excellent Canaanite Pantheon located here: <a href=\"http://www.gothambynight.com/scion/downloads.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.gothambynight.com/scion/downloads.htm</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T17:25:08-08:00","id":4739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xsv-Violence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=4717#post4717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would stand behind the Canaanite Pantheon, though I don't know a whole lot about it other than a couple of the gods namely, Yahweh, Molech, and Baal.<br /> <br /> So what about tying Yahweh to Logos?<br /> <br /> Logos, the primordial embodiment of order and justice, was never imprisoned. Her avatars Themis, Syn and Ma\u2019at accepted limitations. - Scion - God<br /> <br /> It would nicely explain why Yahweh departed the pantheon, his strong following/presence in the world, his nature, etc. Just a thought...</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually really like this idea, a lot more than the Yahweh=Akhetaten of the original gameline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T18:22:11-08:00","id":4766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=4738#post4738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You will find an excellent Canaanite Pantheon located here: <a href=\"http://www.gothambynight.com/scion/downloads.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.gothambynight.com/scion/downloads.htm</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Don\u2019t forget the Arabian Pantheon, found on the same page. Between the Elohim and the Alihah, the bases for Judaism and Islam are covered. <br /> <br /> Note that in both cases, they\u2019re covered through the Pantheons\u2019 respective Titans. El is an Avatar of the Greater Titan of Order (and it\u2019s suggested that Yahweh might be an alias for El) while Allah is the sole Avatar of the Greater Titan of Unity. I could easily see both being served by minions who resemble angels, much like Aten is. <br /> <br /> The main Abrahamic faith not covered here is Christianity, which has founding teachings that are at odds with the legalism that El is described as embodying. I could see treating Yeshua as a Scion of El \u2014 strike that: El\u2019s <i>only</i> Scion \u2014 who ended up parting ways with his father over a difference of opinion about the virtues of legalism. Technically, he would be an Elohim; but despite being at odds with El, he\u2019s shown no interest in associating with others of that Pantheon: he still considers himself El\u2019s son first and foremost, and is hopeful that they can eventually reconcile. <br /> <br /> There are a couple other lesser-known Abrahamic faiths: Samaritanism, which is a nearly-dead cousin to Judaism; and another whose name I can\u2019t remember, which is younger than Islam. I don\u2019t know enough about the latter to say anything about how they\u2019d fit into this. <br /> <br /> I could get behind something like this as <b>Scion</b>\u2019s official take on the Abrahamic faiths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T18:27:10-08:00","id":4768,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Are you thinkin</span>g<span style=\"font-family:arial\"> of <span style=\"color:#000000\">Bah\u00e1'\u00ed?</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T18:27:35-08:00","id":4769,"title":"","content":"Thank you! I appreciate the links.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/783-xsv-violence","name":"Xsv-Violence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar783_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T18:42:00-08:00","id":4780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=4768#post4768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Are you thinking of <span style=\"color:#000000\">Bah\u00e1'\u00ed?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, that\u2019s the one.<br /> <br /> After some really light research (i.e., I read the Wikipedia page), I could perhaps see the Bah\u00e1\u2019\u00ed faith being related to the Alihah in a manner similar to how I suggested that Christianity might be related to the Elohim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-06-2013, 10:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T19:21:23-08:00","id":4792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xsv-Violence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=4769#post4769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you! I appreciate the links.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the same site, there are also web pages for ten <a href=\"http://www.gothambynight.com/scion/pantheons.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Pantheons</a>: eight replacements for existing Pantheons, and two new ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T04:02:40-08:00","id":4944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=4792#post4792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the same site, there are also web pages for ten <a href=\"http://www.gothambynight.com/scion/pantheons.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Pantheons</a>: eight replacements for existing Pantheons, and two new ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also cannot stress just how awesome these websites are. They are run by two people who put mythological accuracy as their single highest priority, and do more research on the topic than many Doctrates I happen to know. Thanks to popular demand and the high production values on their website, they are even being consulted for the 2nd Edition of Scion.<br /> <br /> Because of an NDA, we have no idea how they are actually involved, but we can all hope they will be ensuring mythological accuracy for the new edition.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T06:34:06-08:00","id":5025,"title":"","content":"It's an impressive website.<br /> <br /> But I'd be leery of making claims of accuracy when it's for a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T06:38:53-08:00","id":5029,"title":"","content":"The claim is that it\u2019s well-researched, which it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T06:50:55-08:00","id":5034,"title":"","content":"Well-researched...<i>for a game</i>.<br /> *shrugs*<br /> I prefer these little disclaimers...It's the same one that a lot of games put out.<br /> I've no desire to go indepth since going through the site is kinda fun to read over and a lot of work seems to have went into it, which I can only applaud.<br /> (and someone finally gives respect to Veles..*sniffs* I need a hankie..)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T09:01:50-08:00","id":5109,"title":"","content":"Gotham By Night's work is incredibly accurate, not just for a game. They put a monumental amount of time and energy into their work with the goal of utter accuracy. In this case, there need be no disclaimer for them that all of this is 'for a game'. You should go look at their Blog Shadowflame and look at their extensive explanations of ancient cultures views on different things, ranging from homosexuality, to each other (assuming there was contact).<br /> <br /> Their work is more accurate than many textbooks I have read, and while I can understand putting the 'for a game' disclaimer onto many a website, I would really advise you check out this one, especially their blog, and their lists of source material for all of their Pantheon protects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T09:28:09-08:00","id":5139,"title":"","content":"Well, as I already posted I won't rip it apart. (I'm aware of what's used for sources. Translations always goes back and forth. Simply settling upon one translation and then re-translating it for the sake of a game...?)<br /> But if anyone is a student and they cite material used for a game for his/her homework, I'm pretty sure that s/he will get the grade that s/he deserves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T09:34:45-08:00","id":5146,"title":"","content":"Well yes, they are not a published journal. They are far more accurate than many other works though. They blow most Irish mythology resources I have come across, with the exception of an Oxford Reference dictionary of Irish Myth, which only wins by numbers and ease to use, out of the water.<br /> <br /> I do not understand your complaints though in the slightest though. The medium in no way has any effect on the accuracy of a material, and the complaint about translations makes little sense. If you would like to expand on that, you are welcome to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T09:40:04-08:00","id":5152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=5139#post5139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if anyone is a student and they cite material used for a game for his/her homework, I'm pretty sure that s/he will get the grade that s/he deserves.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is mostly a failing of the teachers not thinking outside of the box when it is time to hand out grades. Unfortunately, I have neither pity nor patience for teachers who grade based on what they expect to see instead of what actually exists. It's an harsh lesson of life that such teachers exist, but I wish any student of mythology the best of luck in avoiding them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T10:05:11-08:00","id":5185,"title":"","content":"The failing here is when genuine research is replaced by blog material that's used for entertainment.<br /> <br /> As an example, The Egyptian Book of the Dead has been translated more than a few times. And it's still considered to be a work in progress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T10:35:22-08:00","id":5211,"title":"","content":"Yes, people should go to primary documents for research, and secondary sources should not be the entirety of their research. But, I still do not understand your argument against Gotham By Night's works and their accuracy. They are not accurate just because they are a blog? That is preposterous. The medium has little to no sway in the accuracy. If Lady Gregory had done equivalent research for all of her works, and had them in a blog, they would still be accurate, and good sources.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, this is derailing the intended conversation in this thread, so I suppose the argument should be cut back. But, if you are going to rail against GBN, please come to the table with some real evidence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T10:44:40-08:00","id":5221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=5211#post5211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately, this is derailing the intended conversation in this thread, so I suppose the argument should be cut back. But, if you are going to rail against GBN, please come to the table with some real evidence.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. If Shadowflame wishes to continue his defense that the blogs are not well researched because they are blogs, or that the blogs are not well researched because the motivation for writing them was love of a game, or another reason he has not yet presented, then we should start a new thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T10:45:35-08:00","id":5222,"title":"","content":"I'm confused by this discussion. The research by GBN is top-notch and their product reflects that. Their product is not a scholarly resource, nor intended to serve as one. Why does the nature of their product lessen the level of their own scholastic ability? There doesn't need to be a warning label attached to books, films or anything else fictional that says &quot;WARNING: Research Used To Create This Was Only Intended To Be Used For Fictional Purposes!&quot;<br /> <br /> So yes, their research was top-notch &quot;for a game&quot;... but what else would you expect? That's what they're writing for. Are you implying it isn't up to scholarly standards? Having written my own share of academic papers as an art historian, I can assure you that their research <i>is</i> up to scholarly standards. They did more research on their Pantheons than I did on my undergraduate thesis. So what's the deal? I don't think anyone was suggesting using GBN's material as scholarly references. <br /> <br /> I'm seriously befuddled, Shadowflame. What's wrong with saying that a blog run by two people with degrees in mythology-related fields is an excellent resource for learning about mythology? They are not, and never have, suggested that anyone take what they say as an academic source. They are happy to provide people with works cited lists, and do so in all their released documents. I'm a professor and if one of my students came to me saying they were reading art or art history blogs for entertainment, I'd be incredibly happy. Encouraging interest and discussion is never bad.<br /> <br /> What defines &quot;genuine research&quot; and why is it being replaced?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T13:54:29-08:00","id":5387,"title":"","content":"I have only one quibble with GBN. I believe that their research is top-notch but, because it is summary information in many cases, designed for ease of use in a game setting, it is somewhat short in many cases. I would like it if they included a sources list, so that I could go to the primary or secondary documents they were using if I wanted to get more in-depth information on a topic. Moreover, there are a lot of books on mythology out there, and it seems like the GBN folks have some pretty good idea of what are good sources and what aren't. And as an academic, though I'll be the first to admit, not one specializing in anything remotely related to mythology, I'd love to be able to dig a bit deeper into the literature without having to wade through quite as much crap as I would have if I had started entirely on my own.<br /> <br /> TLDR: GBN is pretty great, I wish they'd list sources so that I could go and look at them myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T16:45:01-08:00","id":5554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guitarsniper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=5387#post5387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TLDR: GBN is pretty great, I wish they'd list sources so that I could go and look at them myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>The pantheon PDFs all have bibliographies on the last page, and a few of their blog posts have lists of sources (occasionally those are in comments, so it's not readily available).<br /> <br /> Their question box is a good resource, and Anne's a library student, so I'm certain you could ask for sources to consult (or avoid) you'll get a good answer.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T16:51:06-08:00","id":5561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>griffinguy24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=5554#post5554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The pantheon PDFs all have bibliographies on the last page, and a few of their blog posts have lists of sources (occasionally those are in comments, so it's not readily available).<br /> <br /> Their question box is a good resource, and Anne's a library student, so I'm certain you could ask for sources to consult (or avoid) you'll get a good answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>didn't know about the PDF bibliographies, I've been mostly using the HTML versions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T17:59:26-08:00","id":5623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=5211#post5211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, people should go to primary documents for research, and secondary sources should not be the entirety of their research. But, I still do not understand your argument against Gotham By Night's works and their accuracy. They are not accurate just because they are a blog? That is preposterous. The medium has little to no sway in the accuracy. If Lady Gregory had done equivalent research for all of her works, and had them in a blog, they would still be accurate, and good sources.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, this is derailing the intended conversation in this thread, so I suppose the argument should be cut back. But, if you are going to rail against GBN, please come to the table with some real evidence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't said anything negative or mentioned anything about accuracy or that they weren't well-researched (for a game). Just the opposite really. (and I love the sacred-texts links)<br /> But were I to continue in that line, I'd prefer a forum dedicated to archaeology/anthropology rather than a game forum. After all, putting an argument in an academic setting isn't at all easy when all you have to crow about is a blog. Especially if you expect the professionals to take you seriously. (&quot;Well ok mister smith, why did you prefer Budge's interpretation over MacMurray's for the Book of the Dead? Because it fit a game better? WTF?&quot;)<br /> <br /> As this thread is supposed to be about the Abrahamic beliefs, I think we've gone as far as we could beating this horse to death.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T20:42:26-08:00","id":5708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=5139#post5139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, as I already posted I won't rip it apart. (I'm aware of what's used for sources. Translations always goes back and forth. Simply settling upon one translation and then re-translating it for the sake of a game...?)<br /> But if anyone is a student and they cite material used for a game for his/her homework, I'm pretty sure that s/he will get the grade that s/he deserves.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is beating a dead horse but I had to comment on this.<br /> <br /> I am using GBN's blog and research done by Anna as an accredited second-hand source for a research paper I'm doing in my mythology class concerning morality and cultural values as seen through the lens of their myths. I've already cleared it with not only my professor, andthe head of the Humanities department. When both of them said that the blog would be adequate enough to use as a second-hand source (so long as I did the best I could to verify with first-hand sources and it was hard, but I followed up on enough to make it work), and I walk away with a solid A on my paper ... yeah. I say I got the grade I deserved from using the amazing research Anne puts in.<br /> <br /> Unless you've actually read the blog and followed through to the sources used for their explanations (which more often than not have <i>nothing</i> to do with the gameline itself, please don't speak ill about it. Anne's awesome. End of story.<br /> <br /> Edit: They're so well-established as a source of research and accuracy concerning various mythologies and ancient tales to the point where they've been signed on to do Scion 2.0. They're not just a blog for the Scion game itself. And I cannot stress <i>enough </i>second-hand source. Even though Anne's clearly done her homework and put the time in, it's still very wise to follow her citations which I did. GBN's blog is a stepping stone into scholary sources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","user":"Aynie","date":". 11-07-2013, 11:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T21:12:34-08:00","id":6598,"title":"","content":"Just how many arguments on the Scion Forums break out because of people's differing ideas of legitimacy in given subjects?<br /> <br /> It might just be me here, but it seems like something that gets argued a lot. And gets downright out of hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T21:39:03-08:00","id":6617,"title":"","content":"That's just called society, dude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T22:17:38-08:00","id":6632,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://www.greenberg-art.com/.Illustrations/.Humorous/qq1sgPassingTheBuck.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T22:27:41-08:00","id":6634,"title":"","content":"Considering that the forums haven\u2019t been up for a week, I\u2019d say that one contentious thread \u2014 where people have gotten testy, but remained civil throughout \u2014 is pretty good. And if this <i>is</i> something that comes up repeatedly, I\u2019d say that it\u2019s a good idea to get it addressed early on, so that new threads that bring it up can be pointed to this one.<br /> <br /> Finally, it has not gotten out of hand, and is showing no signs of doing so. Overall, I\u2019m satisfied with the way this topic has turned out. Indeed, there has been as much arguing on the derailment about John\u2019s Scion research as there has been on the nominal topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-09-2013, 01:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T06:42:35-08:00","id":6786,"title":"","content":"*shrugs* I tend to let an argument lay after realizing that it's going around and around and not progressing. I know this irks the hell out of some that have some sort of personal axe to grind...<br /> <br /> For those into adding angels to their game, I would look into this:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Dictionary-Angels-Including-Fallen/dp/002907052X\" target=\"_blank\">Dictionary of Angels</a><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://ecx.images-amazon.com/images/I/51pam3AZy9L._SX258_PJlook-inside-v2,TopRight,1,0_SH20_BO1,204,203,200_.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> From one critic: <i>Davidson's introduction itself is worth the money and so is the fabulous Bibliography.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","user":"Shadowflame","date":". 11-09-2013, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T07:50:59-08:00","id":6821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=6598#post6598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And gets downright out of hand.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=6634#post6634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, it has not gotten out of hand, and is showing no signs of doing so.<br /> Overall, I\u2019m satisfied with the way this topic has turned out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to agree with Dataweaver completely. This is an issue that has come up many times before, so it is no surprise that it came up again on the new forums. Almost everyone has been open minded and civil with their posts. Considering that changing someone's mind over the internet is always a Sisyphean task, this has turned up nothing but peaches and cream so far. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T10:44:10-08:00","id":6915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=6786#post6786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For those into adding angels to their game, I would look into this:</div> </div> </div> </div>That website is one of the things I was thinking about when thinking about adding a pantheon like it.<br /> <br /> Most Pantheons get about 10-15 gods right?<br /> Just looking up some things, the pantheon could be simply the arcangels from all three religions as the gods of the pantheon. for the most part I can find about 16 names online like: Michael, Raphael, Gabriel, Lucifer, uriel, chamuel, Jophiel, Raziel, Raguel, Ariel Azrael, Camael, Castiel, Haniel, Jeremiel, Metatron, Sandalphon.<br /> <br /> Ok that's more than needed but I figure that angels that have been in the lore would work wonderfully as the established gods of the abrahamic pantheon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T14:35:59-08:00","id":7034,"title":"","content":"As I read, Metatron and Sandalphon became big guns, with Metatron 2nd only to God in rank. Indeed, were I making up a pantheon, I'd probably put Metatron at the top since I'd be uncomfortable trying to run with a singular God.<br /> Kind of interesting how those particular two had human origins. (Metatron = Enoch; Sandalphon = Elijah...elevated scions to godly status?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T15:09:17-08:00","id":7058,"title":"","content":"Certainly, if I were to do an Abrahamic Pantheon I would seriously consider an option in the upper tiers of its PSP to transform a devout mortal into a Scion. The Elohim on John\u2019s Scion Resources come close to this already (it\u2019s all about empowering devout followers); and El would arguably have it, too. <br /> <br /> That Dictionary of Angels that Shadowflame pointed to? I wouldn\u2019t use that to build a Pantheon; I\u2019d use it to define El\u2019s \u201cTitanspawn\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T15:53:36-08:00","id":7071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=7034#post7034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I read, Metatron and Sandalphon became big guns, with Metatron 2nd only to God in rank. Indeed, were I making up a pantheon, I'd probably put Metatron at the top since I'd be uncomfortable trying to run with a singular God.<br /> Kind of interesting how those particular two had human origins. (Metatron = Enoch; Sandalphon = Elijah...elevated scions to godly status?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea I would probably make them all gods to really fit with the scion themes and be consistant. <br /> <br /> Imagine though, what if Elijah and Enoch were already Scions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T22:05:13-08:00","id":7188,"title":"","content":"Hmn. I wonder if those advocating the Abrahamic pantheon have considered using the Gnostic Demiurge as their Titan. A flawed creator-figure who believes it is the supreme being and sole source of life and divinity in the universe, opposed by Aeons, individual emanations of divinity that promote spiritual enlightenment. Seems an easy fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/938-bigbad","name":"BigBad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T01:57:22-08:00","id":7241,"title":"","content":"I had indeed considered that possibility when composing my suggestion. To the extent that El is typical of Titanic Avatars, he does indeed bear some resemblance to the Gnostic Demiurge; and Yeshua as his estranged son mimics the perceived divide between an apparently cruel Old Testament God vs. a more benevolent New Testament God. <br /> <br /> Conversely, the Elohims\u2019 Titan is one of the few Titans described that isn\u2019t characterized as being outright evil. So if you want to play El in a more positive light, it\u2019s easily enough done. And I intentionally avoided presenting the El/Yeshua relationship as being hostile \u2014 whereas the El/Elohim relationship <i>does</i> tend to be hostile. And since El and Yeshua are on good terms despite their differences, what hostility the Elohim have toward El carries over to Yeshua. <br /> <br /> (The basis for my opinion is this: <b>Scion</b> is a game, not reality; and regardless of how much it strives for authenticity in its research, it nevertheless is about <i>myths</i>. Thus, it says nothing one way or the other about the truth of my religious beliefs.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T07:00:37-08:00","id":7319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigBad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=7188#post7188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmn. I wonder if those advocating the Abrahamic pantheon have considered using the Gnostic Demiurge as their Titan. A flawed creator-figure who believes it is the supreme being and sole source of life and divinity in the universe, opposed by Aeons, individual emanations of divinity that promote spiritual enlightenment. Seems an easy fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not bad at all.<br /> With Sophia (re: Pistis Sophia) as a major goddess figure and Simon Magnus can be seen as a scion...somewhere there.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d2/Lion-faced_deity.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <a href=\"https://&#91;url=http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demiurge#Yaldabaoth\" target=\"_blank\">Yaldabaoth</a>?<br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>A lion-faced deity found on a Gnostic gem in <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bernard_de_Montfaucon\" target=\"_blank\">Bernard de Montfaucon</a>\u2019s <i>L\u2019antiquit\u00e9 expliqu\u00e9e et repr\u00e9sent\u00e9e en figures</i> may be a depiction of the Demiurge</i></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T04:31:41-08:00","id":10321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=2672#post2672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They thought it was a bit blasphemous to suggest that the angels actually cannot hear the word of god, or that the faithful cannot hear the word of god. Also that there was anyone or anything that could rival the angels in power (save perhaps other fallen angels). I did warn you that they were pretty devout.<br /> <br /> Now, I notice you say that it is the kind of question that should ultimately be left up to the Storyteller to answer -- or to avoid. I think you and I are in complete agreement. I happily leave that question up to be judged on a case by case basis from one group to the next.<br /> <br /> But it probably should not be written out as an actual pantheon to be used in the core Scion books. Maybe as a supplement named Monotheism that goes into the various versions of monotheism and how to handle those settings, or integrate them into a regular Scion game?<br /> <br /> <b>I might buy that. But I don't want it in Core.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with most of the statements above, but it seems like the objections about not being able to hear the word of god could be overcome through some sort of PSP. Ideally, it would grant the angels an edge on the other Legend 9+ powers at the expense of part of their free will, making them faultless messengers of their god as they are often depicted.<br /> <br /> Probably the angels would regard the gods as fallen angels. Whether this is actually true should be left to the storyteller, or not resolved at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T09:04:35-08:00","id":10465,"title":"","content":"Ancient Israelites were Henotheists, not Monotheists. There's no more contradiction between its mythos as exists between Odin carving the world out of Ymir's body vs. Tefnut and Shu giving birth to Nut and Geb.<br /> <br /> At my table, the Elohim refer to other gods as &quot;Grigori&quot; and Scions as &quot;Nephilim&quot;. They do not conceive Scions of their own, but will adopt Scions who renounce their pagan idols to serve YHWH (their non-manifest supreme Deity)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T09:07:49-08:00","id":10471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=1255#post1255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, the issue is that Scion says &quot;All Myths Are True&quot; and there's a conflict there. Monotheism specifcally says that All Myths Are NOT True. Only <b>their</b> myths are true. So there's a conflict between Abrahamic God and the polytheistic Gods like Odin, Thor, Ares, Shango. If Abrahamic God is right, then he's Legend Infinity. He's all powerful and all knowing. The other Gods are basically just pretenders, and so are the Titans.<br /> <br /> So there's a few soltuions, all of which compromise either a basic assumption of monotheism, or a basic assumption of the game.<br /> <br /> 1) God is really God. He is the ultimate power of the setting, all other Gods are wrong, liars, stupid or pretenders. This renders the entire setting moot, since God could solve everything with a blink of His eye. No conflict, no drama. Scion assumes active Gods, and if God is active and He is All Powerful, He ends the Titan War instantly. Also Titans don't exist, or are really demons, because God is the only God.<br /> <br /> 2) God is NOT really God. He's just an idiot and he's really on the same level as all the other deities. That causes issues because then God is by himself in his &quot;Pantheon&quot; of one. If you want to have other figures in there at Legend 12, suitable for standard Divine Parents, then you have to assume that figures like Jesus, Mary, Lucifer, Gabriel, etc, are <i><b>equal to God</b></i> and that's not following the mythology. Cept maybe Jesus, and that depends on if you believe Jesus <i>is</i> God or if he's the <i>son </i>of God.<br /> <br /> Either one has some pretty big issues. If you want really in-depth discussion, because this comes up a <b>lot</b>, here are some links to the foremost Scion Blog (one of like, two) and some very cogent thoughts on monotheism in Scion.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you apply in-setting ambiguity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T09:17:54-08:00","id":10482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=10321#post10321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether this is actually true should be left to the storyteller, or not resolved at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=10471#post10471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Or you apply in-setting ambiguity.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That kind of 'leave it to the storyteller' ambiguity is one of the better reasons not to include monotheism in the core books. Maybe a nice section chatting about the possibilities at most; never a fully stated out pantheon.</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T11:33:22-08:00","id":10602,"title":"","content":"I don't actually see a problem with canonical-uncertainty (which doesn't inherently mean &quot;leave it to the Storyteller to decide&quot; as the assumed default with canonical-uncertainty is that it remains uncertain, not that the Storyteller imposes an answer [though they always have that option of course]).<br /> <br /> That said, I agree it shouldn't be in the Core. It would eat up space from Pantheons more &quot;on-theme&quot;. I wouldn't have a problem with it appearing in a supplement with either canonical-uncertainty OR as simply being a Henotheistic pantheon.<br /> <br /> If anyone's unaware, henotheists acknowledge the existence of other gods but exclusively worship their One God. All evidence indicates the actual Ancient Israelites were henotheists (when they weren't occasionally falling off the wagon and throwing some extra idols in the Temple as well) up until the Babylonian Captivity, when the concept of YHWH evolved to be omnipresent and precluded other divinities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T12:14:47-08:00","id":10661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=10602#post10602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If anyone's unaware, henotheists acknowledge the existence of other gods but exclusively worship their One God. All evidence indicates the actual Ancient Israelites were henotheists (when they weren't occasionally falling off the wagon and throwing some extra idols in the Temple as well) up until the Babylonian Captivity, when the concept of YHWH evolved to be omnipresent and precluded other divinities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect that most people here have no problem with henotheism. For the most part, it easily fits into essential rubric of 'All Myths Are True&quot; without causing too many speed bumps.<br /> <br /> But I don't think very many people are advocating the use of those ancient henotheistic roots. Especially not the surprising number of people who disbelieve in those henotheistic roots regardless of possible evidence.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T23:09:22-08:00","id":11079,"title":"","content":"It's pretty hard to deny the roots when it's baldly stated in the Ten Commandments. If no other gods exist, no prohibition on their worship is necessary. In fact, God goes on a whole tangent (the 'I am a jealous god' bit, Exodus 20:5) about why you shouldn't worship other gods and it's all about his inability to share and his willingness to curse transgressors, not the pointlessness of worshiping entities that do not exist. If it was already a tenet of the faith at the time that no other gods than YHWH existed, it seems like the sort of point you'd want to bring up in a discussion on idolatry and heresy.<br /> <br /> &quot;Do not bow down and worship them because you look a bit silly, and it doesn't accomplish anything. And it irritates me, so if you do insist on it, I'll curse you. And your kids, because why not. And maybe their kids. I dunno, depends on how I'm feeling that day. Maybe I'll get on a roll and go to the fourth generation.&quot; --Not an actual bible quote, don't PM me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/938-bigbad","name":"BigBad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T23:32:03-08:00","id":11088,"title":"","content":"I've written papers on the historical evolution of Christianity in high school and undergrad. I have been told to my face that I was wrong about every single bit, because Christianity never had to evolve from earlier forms of its religion, since there <b>are</b> no earlier forms. God has been there since the beginning, straight up telling people how things worked. There are no other Gods, never have been and never will be. That commandment is against <i>false</i> gods, not evidence of a henotheistic past to the religion.<br /> <br /> Calling the study of angels, demons and miracles &quot;Christian Mythology&quot; got my high school research project rejected until I appealed it, and even then it was strongly 'suggested' that I use a different phrase to describe such things. Seriously, this is not stuff that I would want to work into an RPG based on ancient mythology, because it is <i>messy </i>and <i>angry</i>. When you go to the book store, there's a section on &quot;Theology&quot; for monotheism and a section on &quot;Mythology&quot; for everyone else. You might get lucky and find some Hindu or Buddhist material in the &quot;Theology&quot; section, but don't count on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T01:43:20-08:00","id":11117,"title":"","content":"...how does one argue that there are no earlier forms of Christianity while taking into account even such relatively recent events as the Protestant Reformation? I mean, it is demonstrably and incontestably true that the form of Christianity practiced by, say, Southern Baptists is wildly different from the form practiced by Romans in the early Church. And that's completely ignoring things like the Apocrypha, the Nag Hammadi library and its revelations on Gnostic Christianity, the existence of approximately five bajillion separate Christian denominations with many going back a thousand years or more, etc. If God is supposed to be watchdogging the dogma, he's not really doing a good job.<br /> <br /> But I digress. I happen to agree with the exclusion of modern monotheistic faiths from the gameline. It just doesn't jive well with the game's feel, and there's not really enough named entities with distinct personalities to fill out an entire pantheon anyway. Ninety percent would just be guesswork and making stuff up. I mean, if you really want Jesus in your game, just have Dionysus show up. He's kind of like the stoner precursor to Jesus, as far as his Mystery Cult goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/938-bigbad","name":"BigBad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T01:54:29-08:00","id":11120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigBad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=11117#post11117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...how does one argue that there are no earlier forms of Christianity while taking into account even such relatively recent events as the Protestant Reformation?</div> </div> </div> </div>With emotion and conviction, unfortunately.<br /> <br /> <b>Telgar has the right of it.</b> No amount of evidence is going to convince the staggering number of people who believe otherwise. Genuine wars have been fought, and real people like you and me have been outright murdered for suggesting otherwise. And not just a few people here and there, but full lynchings, burnings, and worse. We're only recently getting to a point where tolerance is becoming the majority.<br /> <br /> I think everyone here is wonderfully tolerant and well above the average when it comes to the importance of scholarly merit in an argument. But this is not a hypothetical situation. I've actually been knocked to the ground and repeatedly kicked for pointing out evidence to the contrary.<br /> <br /> How does this all relate to Scion? Mostly, I want Scion to sell well. This includes being easy to play, fun, and not making a large demographic uncomfortable when I try to teach them the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 11-15-2013, 05:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T02:57:15-08:00","id":11135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigBad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=11079#post11079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty hard to deny the roots when it's baldly stated in the Ten Commandments. If no other gods exist, no prohibition on their worship is necessary. In fact, God goes on a whole tangent (the 'I am a jealous god' bit, Exodus 20:5)[...]<br /> &quot;Do not bow down and worship them because you look a bit silly, and it doesn't accomplish anything. And it irritates me, so if you do insist on it, I'll curse you. And your kids, because why not. And maybe their kids. I dunno, depends on how I'm feeling that day. Maybe I'll get on a roll and go to the fourth generation.&quot; --Not an actual bible quote, don't PM me.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was a common error of translation.<br /> <br /> &quot; I am a ZELOUSE God&quot;.<br /> From Hebraic, the Commandment is &quot; Dont have another God that stand (countrary) to me&quot;.<br /> Just for say.<br /> <br /> For the sake of thread, read Psalm 81(82) <a href=\"http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Psalm%2082&amp;version=ESV\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/...82&amp;version=ESV</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 11-15-2013, 06:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T07:56:53-08:00","id":11281,"title":"","content":"I'd like to keep monotheism out of it and go with a supplement later myself. I don't mind the henotheistic roots of monotheistic religions, but then I'm a henotheistic Christian myself, so there you do. Monotheism tends to take things over, and while I'd like it addressed, I don't want it taking up space from my precious other pantheons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/911-phoebuslore","name":"phoebuslore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar911_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T12:57:49-08:00","id":11512,"title":"","content":"The important thing to me with respect to the Abrahamic faiths is to include angels and holy men who are potential protagonists. I don\u2019t need the angels to be monotheists; I\u2019m fine with them primarily being henotheists, with the more pious of them leaning toward monolatry (just as any Pantheon that has Piety as a Virtue has a tendency to consider themselves to be superior to everyone else). I don\u2019t even need them to be a Pantheon; but then, I\u2019ve never been a fan of restricting <b>Scion</b>\u2019s protagonists to <i>just</i> scions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T17:53:15-08:00","id":11734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=11135#post11135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This was a common error of translation.<br /> <br /> &quot; I am a ZELOUSE God&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Debatable - the primary use of &quot;qanna&quot; was with regard to marital relations and implied jealousy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T14:48:31-08:00","id":12981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=2374#post2374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But as you once viciously snarled at me in the old forums, there are people who really do believe in a number of deities featured within Scion, and those belief systems are not always uniform either. So why should those gods be given any more of a pass?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a practicing Asatru who is in a long-term relationship with an Evangelical Christian, I may be uniquely qualified to explain.<br /> <br /> Because the nature and identity of the Norse Gods is covered in two texts with a bare handful of apocryphal works intruding upon what might be taken as, our admittedly fallible, canon there's no sense that the nature and identity of these deities needs protecting from the apocrypha and misconception. It really doesn't matter that most of my friends identify Thor with the Marvel character. Nor does it impact my life on any particular level that most people don't realize the days of the week are named after Norse deities. Frankly, when you tell people you believe in Valhalla, glorious death in battle, and Ragnarok, most people admit that it seems like a pretty cool idea of an afterlife. My significant other just nodded and said &quot;That's not really different from Revelations,&quot; which is where the problem begins for Christians.<br /> <br /> Revelations is an amusing Cliff's notes take on Ragnarok to most Asatru. These &quot;appropriations&quot; littered the apocryphal texts of Christianity in its infancy. Until they began to be included in Bibles compiled by Emperors and Kings several hundred years later (around the time Islam was codified, incidentally). This creates a problem for most Evangelical (e.g. Bible) Christians, who have to reconcile their faith with the original stories sacred to other faiths. This is made even more morally hazardous because of the belief is that the Bible is divinely inspired (or written by God). If the material in it is plagiarized that bodes ill for the infallibility of the god of Abraham.<br /> <br /> Which is the point people have been trying to make. As Monotheistic faiths, Abrahamic practice requires that there be no other gods, no idols worshiped, and no more prophets. That's Judaism, Christianity, and Islam. Collectively, that's about one-third of the world's population you're going to offend by including an Abrahamic pantheon in a game of urban fantasy, because you cannot reach an end result that is going to satisfy all three faith groups, much less the hundreds of sects within those major faith groups.<br /> <br /> You simply can't squeeze an Abrahamic pantheon in without making it virtually unrecognizable. I'd humbly suggest you consider, instead, a hard look at a Sumerian pantheon, as that's the religion Judaism was derived from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T15:35:04-08:00","id":13003,"title":"","content":"Naw, Caananite is way closer than Sumerian. But you're quite right about the issues involved with fundamentalist followers of the Abrahamic religions and attempts to view their religion in the same anthropological and historical light as ones <i>they personally</i> do not believe in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T16:36:36-08:00","id":13046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=13003#post13003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Naw, Caananite is way closer than Sumerian. But you're quite right about the issues involved with fundamentalist followers of the Abrahamic religions and attempts to view their religion in the same anthropological and historical light as ones <i>they personally</i> do not believe in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I picked Sumerian because it is dissimilar enough that it can't be recognized by most people as related to modern Abrahamic religions. Plus it has lots of really cool iconography and symbolism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T17:11:08-08:00","id":13066,"title":"","content":"Well, Abraham supposedly led his tribe from the city of Ur. A big city for that time with gods in all their glory likely left an impression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T16:50:33-08:00","id":14371,"title":"","content":"True; but the book of Genesis ends with the Israeli patriarchs settling down in Egypt; and the story of Exodus picks up several generations later. Arguably, Egyptian religious beliefs had at least as much of an influence on the proto-Israelites as the Sumerians did. I agree with Telgar that if you\u2019re going to tie Abrahamic religions to one ancient Pantheon, the most logical choice would be the Canaanite Elohim. <br /> <br /> Of course, there was also the Babylonian Captivity, followed by their time as subjects of the Roman Empire, which was where Christianity was born. And Islam arose in the Arabian peninsula. That\u2019s four or five Pantheons that were involved in the formation of the various Abrahamic religions (I\u2019m not sure what connection, if any, exists between Babylonian and Sumerian mythologies: I believe that they\u2019re either the same, or they\u2019re like the Greeks and the Romans; and the possibility that they may have been suitably distinct to count as separate Pantheons is why I said \u201c\u2026or five\u2026\u201d).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T20:12:55-08:00","id":14478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=14371#post14371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, there was also the Babylonian Captivity, followed by their time as subjects of the Roman Empire, which was where Christianity was born. And Islam arose in the Arabian peninsula. That\u2019s four or five Pantheons that were involved in the formation of the various Abrahamic religions (I\u2019m not sure what connection, if any, exists between Babylonian and Sumerian mythologies: I believe that they\u2019re either the same, or they\u2019re like the Greeks and the Romans; and the possibility that they may have been suitably distinct to count as separate Pantheons is why I said \u201c\u2026or five\u2026\u201d).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sumerian and Babylonian are close enough that they have deity overlap, so yes, similar to Greco-Roman mythology, down to provincialism in patron deity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T20:31:51-08:00","id":14491,"title":"","content":"Dude's right, Assyrian, Akkadian, Babylonian and Sumerian are all <i>super</i> similar religions. Caananite is far more distinct, but the big four Mesopotamian cultures are all pretty close together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T06:50:06-08:00","id":41681,"title":"","content":"Well, historically Palestine was bounced back and forth between Mesopotamia and Egypt like a provincial football, so it's not surprise that Hebrew culture shows strong influences from both. But at heart the Hebrews were originally Canaanites (i.e. Phoenicians), as far as culture and language goes. It's just that the cult of Yahweh became extremely powerful and eventually edged out everybody else.<br /> <br /> For a bronze-age (i.e. pre-Hebrew and pre-Greek) look at Canaanite myth, see the writings we've recovered from Ugarit. The Sons of El would make a fine pantheon for Scion, albeit one with clear Mesopotamian influence (as all cultures in the Near East). For example, Baal Haddad is Addad in Babylon, although he's much more important to the Canaanites.<br /> <br /> What seems to have happened in iron-age Hebrew culture is that Yahweh, patron god of Jerusalem, came to be identified with El and eventually absorbed or subordinated the rest of the family, whereas he's named as one of the sons of El in Ugarit. That sort of genealogical shenanigans is actually very common in the myths of the region, as each city attempted to show how their patron god was king of the others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T07:01:40-08:00","id":41686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=14491#post14491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude's right, Assyrian, Akkadian, Babylonian and Sumerian are all <i>super</i> similar religions. Caananite is far more distinct, but the big four Mesopotamian cultures are all pretty close together.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're all functionally the same religion, in the same sense that Greco-Roman religion existed on a single continuum. Individual cities had rites and traditions specific to them, as was the case in any ancient culture, but the basic forms and assumptions were shared in common throughout the region.<br /> <br /> In Mesopotamia it's largely because Sumerian and Akkadian cultures (including the latter's Assyrian and Babylonian variants) existed side-by-side in the same land for many centuries. Each city was multi-ethnic, so it's not as if you have a Sumerian-only city or an Akkadian-only city by the historical period. It was basically just a question of which language you spoke at home.<br /> <br /> The Sumerian culture was the oldest in the region, and the basic religious and mythic framework was originally Sumerian, but the Semitic-speaking Akkadians became Sumerianized pretty early on, to the point where they made the culture their own and added to it, eventually absorbing and overshadowing it altogether, to the point where Sumerian was primarily a ceremonial language. Trying to disentangle them and identify something as essentially one or the other is futile, just as trying to identify an &quot;essentially Roman&quot; culture apart from Greek influence is pointless (and characteristic of a rather nasty period in early 20th-century scholarship that was tied up with ethnic essentialism and race theory).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T14:17:31-08:00","id":42475,"title":"","content":"First, I am glad that someone mentioned the El connection, since many of the Host have the El suffix. So reading all these pages makes me think of three things that could work:<br /> <br /> 1. Using the Cannanite pantheon in Scion would work well in explaining the advent of monotheism as an attempt from El to have a backup faith source, in case the pantheon dies off. Hell, even the introduction of Baal and others may gain the attention (and perhaps respect) of Satanists who believe in the characters differently.<br /> <br /> 2. Abrahamism (Christianity, Judaism, Islam) can be considered antagonists. I'm saying this is because if a Scion spouts the glory of their divine parent and their pantheon to a fundamentalist, said fundamentalist would first try to prove the Scion wrong, then when proven wrong would accost the Scion as being a pagan heretic up to the point where he and his friends would try to lynch mob him.<br /> <br /> 3. As for this one, I read Cracked's book: The De-Textbook. Under the info about vikings, it said that the Prose Edda was actually written 300 years AFTER the Norse became Christianized. Two pieces of evidence that they noted in the book was how Odin's attaining of wisdom was eerily similar to the crucifixion of Jesus Christ and that Ragnarok was a Christian add in for Armagedeon. Go on and read the book. So the third thought is that the Aesir created Christianity to mitigate the eventual fate at Ragnarok.<br /> <br /> Also in my opinion, I probably wouldn't like the Yoruba pantheon in there because it would cheapen the African pantheon that we already have (the Loa). It'll be like someone making a RPG about messiahs and have Mormonism as a religion separate from Christianity. I did read somewhere that Africans worshipped a montheistic god called Yoruba, but I wondered where was the Yoruban religion when black slavery happened. As far as I know, the slaves that were sent to the Caribbean and the States worshipped the Loa, which they hid under the guise of Christian saints.<br /> <br /> Where was the Orishans?<br /> <br /> As altenatives, I would like to see the Sumerian pantheon. I saw a special on the History Channel about Dragons in ancient myth, and they said that the first time a dragon was mentioned in the Western hemisphere was in the Sumerian mythology where the Dragon Goddess (I forget her name) killed an evil dragon to form the land. If you add her to the Sumerian pantheon, I would be so happy, because I LOVE dragons and being the Scion of one would be awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T14:30:19-08:00","id":42484,"title":"","content":"Oops, saw the Orisha bloodline and saw Shango in there. So new thought. Adding the Orisha in there would cheapen the Loa because the entire religion changed in the time since its creation to the time of black slavery. In short: The Orisha IS the Loa and vice-versa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T17:20:05-08:00","id":42573,"title":"","content":"In &quot;Bloodline of the Holy Grail&quot; Laurence Gardner claims that Ahkenaten was Moses. I hate that idea, but someone might want to use it.<br /> <br /> In &quot;Whisper of Stone&quot; Tess Dawson says that Baal Haddad was known as the foreigner. I like the idea that fairy tales in which the king gives half his kingdom and the princess to a young man who does a service for him are retellings of the story between El (the king), Baal Haddad (the young man) and Arhat the impetuous daughter (the princess). Yahweh then is the prince who looses half his patrimony to his brother-in-law, hence the animosity between the two. As Harold Boom says in &quot;Jesus and Yaweh the Names Divine&quot; Yahweh of the Bible is human all to human.<br /> <br /> There is also the Japanese shrine that equates Yahweh and Susano-o.<br /> <br /> In &quot;Jesus the Magician&quot; it says that in the Hellinistic world non-jews identified the god of Israel with Set. Some scholars have identified Yahweh with a minor Egyptian moon god named Yao,(also known as Iao).<br /> <br /> I personally favor the idea that the Canannite Pantheon; including Yahweh, created Christianity to compete with the mystery religions of the greeks and eqyptians, but the project got highjacked the romans through St. Paul and things got out of hand. All the schisms in the missionary faiths of Buddism, Christianity, and Islam are the works of different pantheons influencing things from behind the scenes. Thus the Mormons, Baptists, Jehovah's Witnesses, and even the Scientologists are creations of the Manitous, which is why the French government tried to ban all four of them. The Celtic and Greek gods(or Gaulish Pantheon if you've got the book) didn't want the Manito growing more popular than their proxies.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1869,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","user":"moonwolf8","date":". 01-05-2014, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T17:23:39-08:00","id":42580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=42484#post42484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oops, saw the Orisha bloodline and saw Shango in there. So new thought. Adding the Orisha in there would cheapen the Loa because the entire religion changed in the time since its creation to the time of black slavery. In short: The Orisha IS the Loa and vice-versa.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not understanding your logic. How would adding the Orisha cheapen the Loa when they ARE the Loa (except for Damballah)? And they're hardly the only religion that's done a total 180 in the course of its history.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">As altenatives, I would like to see the Sumerian pantheon. I saw a special on the History Channel about Dragons in ancient myth, and they said that the first time a dragon was mentioned in the Western hemisphere was in the Sumerian mythology where the Dragon Goddess (I forget her name) killed an evil dragon to form the land. If you add her to the Sumerian pantheon, I would be so happy, because I LOVE dragons and being the Scion of one would be awesome.</span></span> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> I think you have the story slightly confused. The God Marduk created the World from the body of Tiamat. And while Tiamat is definitely the original Mother of Dragons, I don't think she herself is ever described as a dragon, though someone better acquainted with Mesopotamian iconography could give you a more conclusive answer. Also, Tiamat is prime Titan material, so being her Scion is a remote possibility at best.</span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T19:50:31-08:00","id":42646,"title":"","content":"Sounds like this could be reposted:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=4718#post4718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From <a href=\"http://www.bidstrup.com/bible.htm\" target=\"_blank\">this essay</a> <i><br /> <br /> Yet influences from the east must have been, because we have evidence of worship of their gods and goddesses.<br /> The heiarchy of gods and goddesses who included Baal, the god of storms, who made the land fertile, and Lotan, the seven-headed dragon, known to Old Testament readers as Leviathan. There is Yam Nahar, the god of the seas and rivers, and other pantheons and heiarchies of gods and goddesses. <b>Reigning over them all was El, the king of the gods</b>, ruler of the pantheon. Remember the name, we'll encounter it again.<br /> <br /> Prior to the Babylonian exile, we know that the Israelites followed a wide variety of cults, most of which were polytheistic, and the cult of Yahweh was a relatively minor cult among the Israelites during this period that has been greatly revised over time. We know, for example, that the narrative of the Yahweh included a wife. Her name was Asherah, though in related cults she had different names, including Astarte and Istar. She was a powerful, important, even indispensible part of the cult, mostly related to fertility. We know that she figured prominently throughout the pre-Roman period, as she appears frequently in inscriptions and on figurines prior to the Assyrian expulsion and to a lesser extent afterwards. She remained a major figure in the Old Testament narratives, though as time went on, she was gradually edited out by subsequent copyists and editors, disappearing almost completely from the Old Testament narrative by about the 8th Century, though traces of this cult figure remain even today in the Old Testament. ...<br /> <br /> We now know this Mesopotamian god as &quot;El-ohim,&quot; and our author &quot;E,&quot; one of the earliest scriptorialists writing about this time, first has <b>El introducing himself to Abraham as &quot;El Shaddai&quot; (El of the Mountain)</b>. He also appears as El Elyon, or El of Bethel in other, non-canonized scripture, and his name is also preserved in such Hebrew names as Isra-El and Ishma-El. The word Elohim was originally a plural of El. To the south, from Bethel to the Valley of Beersheba, a similar transformation is taking place. In this climatically and geologically harsher place, a place with a much smaller and less settled population with greater geographical isolation, the Canaanite god Yahweh is being transformed by a culturally similar people of the land of Judah. The unknown author known to scholars simply as &quot;J&quot; has his god being familiar with and comfortable with Abraham, and he casually appears to Abraham in Genesis 18, introducing himself as Yahweh. But &quot;J's&quot; contemporary, author &quot;E&quot; in the north can't have God being so casual, and first appears as a voice, commanding Abraham to leave his people in Mesopotamia and settle in Canaan. Yahweh, in his transformation from a pagan Canaanite god to the god of the Jews, becomes a cruel and vindictive god in the hands of author &quot;J.&quot; He commands Abraham to sacrifice his first born son, an act which is not at all surprising given the nature of the pagan religions of the time. Many of these pagan religions (and remember that Yahweh got his start as a Canannite pagan god) considered the first-born to be the seed of a god. Because of this, they were often sacrificed to the god who presumably sired them. Yet Elohim in the north continues to be a much more subtle god, who directs the affairs of men by revelation of the voice, hidden from the view of mere mortals. There is a tension among these peoples, both of whom identify themselves as culturally descendants of Abraham, Isaac and Jacob. One people, perhaps, but two gods. </i><br /> <br /> Hmm.. <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Deities_in_the_Hebrew_Bible\" target=\"_blank\">Deities in the Hebrew Bible</a></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T08:08:29-08:00","id":42887,"title":"","content":"All good stuff. Just bear in mind that <b>Scion</b> is a game about \u201cmyths made real\u201d, not a documentary on \u201cthe truth behind the myths\u201d: we don\u2019t insist on a rigorous examination of, say, nordic history and what the realities were that gave rise to the myths about the Aesir; we take Norse mythology at face value as much as we can manage, compromising only to the extent needed to build a setting where the Aesir coexist with other Pantheons. IMHO, the same should be done with the Abrahamic faiths: don\u2019t go in saying \u201cit\u2019s all a lie\u201d; go in saying \u201chow much of this can we declare to be true without undermining everyone else?\u201d<br /> <br /> The catch, of course, is inherent in that last part. Is Judaism mutually exclusive with the Caananite Elohim, with the \u201ctruth\u201d in <b>Scion</b> being that a bunch of Canaanites who had been driven out of Egypt invented mythological figures such as Abraham, Moses, and King David who had never actually existed, and that an Elohim named Yahweh condoned this mythmaking for his own benefit? Or is there a way to \u201cthread the needle\u201d and say that in the world of <b>Scion</b>, Abraham, Moses, and David were real people; their stories were real; and the God of the Israelites was at odds with the Gods of the Canaanites?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T08:51:21-08:00","id":42905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=42887#post42887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The catch, of course, is inherent in that last part. Is Judaism mutually exclusive with the Caananite Elohim, with the \u201ctruth\u201d in <b>Scion</b> being that a bunch of Canaanites who had been driven out of Egypt invented mythological figures such as Abraham, Moses, and King David who had never actually existed, and that an Elohim named Yahweh condoned this mythmaking for his own benefit?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this would be intense, I vote for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T10:23:37-08:00","id":42969,"title":"","content":"Why would it be intense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T10:46:36-08:00","id":43000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=42969#post42969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would it be intense?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it <i>would</i> be implying that the holy men of some fairly widely-practised religions are hoaxes and the God of said religions is an ego-maniacal opportunist who abandoned his Pantheon to the dregs of history and set himself up as a solo act on the basis of false pretences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T11:21:13-08:00","id":43023,"title":"","content":"Not exactly the first time it's happened. <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atenism\" target=\"_blank\">Atenism</a><br /> <br /> And for the sake of reference: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canaanite_religion#Pantheon\" target=\"_blank\">Canaanite (Levantine) Deities</a>; and of course the much favored <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Mesopotamian_deities\" target=\"_blank\">Mesopotamian Deities</a><br /> <br /> And <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panbabylonism\" target=\"_blank\">Panbabylonism</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T12:57:51-08:00","id":43075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=43000#post43000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it <i>would</i> be implying that the holy men of some fairly widely-practised religions are hoaxes and the God of said religions is an ego-maniacal opportunist who abandoned his Pantheon to the dregs of history and set himself up as a solo act on the basis of false pretences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly; but in a game where every other significant religious mythology is assumed to be essentially true except where absolutely necessary to provide a coherent multi-myth setting, why is declaring a religious mythology to be essentially false considered to be a good thing?<br /> <br /> IIRC, the Yazatas book talks about how the Hindu Gods were seen by the Persians as demons. To me, declaring that the Abrahamic faiths are lies perpetrated by Canaanite renegades is akin to saying that the Devas don\u2019t exist, and that the Hindu people unknowingly worship Zoroastrian demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-05-2014, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T13:16:43-08:00","id":43090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=43075#post43075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certainly; but in a game where every other significant religious mythology is assumed to be essentially true except where absolutely necessary to provide a coherent multi-myth setting, why is declaring a religious mythology to be essentially false considered to be a good thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said that it was a good thing. I only agreed with Egg's evaluation, that such a decision would be <i>intensely</i> received. And gave my reasoning as to <i>why</i> I think it would be intensely received.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T16:22:47-08:00","id":43200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=43075#post43075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IIRC, the Yazatas book talks about how the Hindu Gods were seen by the Persians as demons. To me, declaring that the Abrahamic faiths are lies perpetrated by Canaanite renegades is akin to saying that the Devas don\u2019t exist, and that the Hindu people unknowingly worship Zoroastrian demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how I run it in all of my games. According to any of the Yazata asked, the Hindu people are currently under the influence of demons and must be rescued or purged. The fact that they're such a widespread religion only infuriates the righteous gods.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the Deva see and believe the same of their opposite counterparts! It makes for tense relationships between the two that spill over into Scion bands and mundane politics.<br /> <br /> It's the same as Aztec Gods needing blood to be sacrificed so the world can continue and the Egyptians needing Ra to defeat Apep every night so the sun can rise again. Two different &quot;truths&quot; can co-exist because it's Scion. When Apollo died in the current game I run, Sunlight effectively ceased to exist over anywhere the Greeks held domination. Most of the recreated Roman Empire (and America and England due to conquest) now exist in perpetual twilight until they find someone else to take Helios' light once again. Everywhere that the Greeks don't have sway though, is perfectly fine to have bright days.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-05T21:50:14-08:00","id":43348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=43200#post43200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When Apollo died in the current game I run, Sunlight effectively ceased to exist over anywhere the Greeks held domination. Most of the recreated Roman Empire (and America and England due to conquest) now exist in perpetual twilight until they find someone else to take Helios' light once again. Everywhere that the Greeks don't have sway though, is perfectly fine to have bright days.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody picked a nit about Helios (a Titan) being the one actually responsible for making the sun rise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T00:16:37-08:00","id":43380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=43075#post43075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC, the Yazatas book talks about how the Hindu Gods were seen by the Persians as demons. To me, declaring that the Abrahamic faiths are lies perpetrated by Canaanite renegades is akin to saying that the Devas don\u2019t exist, and that the Hindu people unknowingly worship Zoroastrian demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not seeing how that implies that the Hindu Gods don't exist. The Yazata very much believe they exist. They just happen to also believe that they are servants of the Titans. And vice versa. A no. of the Yazata are referred to as Asuras in Hinduism, including great Mithra and Ahura Mazda himself. Similarly, Indra and Shiva are counted amongst the greatest of deevs in Persian mythology. The Yazata believe that the Deva, with their talk of how the sacred elements of Nature are really just illusions, are servants of the Titan of Lies Ahriman, and the Deva believe that the Yazata, with their talk of rejection of asceticism, are servants of Titan of Illusions Mayasura.<br /> <br /> Of course, Fate has a sense of humour. Which is probably why the largest concentration of Zoroastrians today, happens to be in India. I'm pretty sure both the Pantheons are foaming at the mouth at that little twist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T06:11:31-08:00","id":43465,"title":"","content":"The current approach, where the Devas and Yazatas are both Pantheons of Gods and where the demonization of each by the other is strictly a matter of propaganda, is a good, valid way to handle things. What I\u2019m talking about, though, is a hypothetical situation: what if <b>Scion</b> were to declare that the official position of the game was that the Yazatas were a Pantheon of Gods while the Devas were \u201cmerely\u201d demonic Titanspawn? That official declaration that the Devas are <i>not</i> gods wouldn\u2019t fly with the fans. <br /> <br /> But that\u2019s <i>exactly</i> the sort of thing that\u2019s being suggested here: either ignore the Abrahamic faiths outright (which implicitly declares them to be essentially false) or present them primarily as a human invention \u2014 a massive game of make-believe that\u2019s backed by a handful of opportunistic gods \u2014 which, again, declares them to be essentially false. Why not declare them to be essentially true, save only for that troublesome \u201cstrong monotheism\u201d thing that could be downgraded to henotheism to accommodate other gods? Why the hostility to this particular set of religion-based mythologies, when nearly every other religion-based mythology is endorsed? Not necessarily as a Pantheon, mind you (although Abrahamic mythology includes the notion of Nephilim, which could be equated with Scions if you equate angels with gods); but also not as inherently malevolent Titanspawn (the operating term being \u201cmalevolent\u201d).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T06:56:00-08:00","id":43486,"title":"","content":"<br /> That's the big problem with trying to integrate the Abrahamic religions; the uncomfortable fact that there is the core belief that all other pantheons would be referred to as at the least as pagan, or at the worst &quot;Satanic&quot; and that's assuming any measure of roleplaying it with some degree of real-life historicity. And experience with other deities would be simply denied as either delusional or the devil tempting the player with heretical thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T07:24:36-08:00","id":43495,"title":"","content":"I never said the Yazata and Deva consider each other Titan<i>spawn</i>, only <i>servants of the Titans</i>. The older texts of both religions declare that the other are Gods, just Gods who are allied with Titans. After all, Loki doesn't magically become Titanspawn when he sides with the Fire Giants during Ragnarok. He's still a God, just one working for Muspelheim now.<br /> <br /> As for the idea of including the Abrahamic Pantheons in Scion, I really couldn't care less as long as it was it's own supplement so I can ignore it.<br /> <br /> As for why I'm don't like the idea, well, firstly, I do not find the concept of a Pantheon with a single God (can it even be called a Pantheon at that point?) very interesting. There are also public relations to be considered. Is not the First Commandment 'Thou shalt have no other Gods before me'? Try getting into an alliance with the Japanese Gods while not showing deference to Amaterasu. She, at least, would only tell the messenger to politely leave. Zeus would probably thunderbolt him on the spot. And I really don't want to think of what Marduk would do. The Abrahamic God would essentially be left all alone to face the Wrath of the Titans.<br /> <br /> There is also the matter of the already extant Gods. Yahweh, I note, has already been discussed in detail. But what about Allah? How do you reconcile the God of Islam with the already extant Creator God of Arabian Mythology?<br /> <br /> As I said, so long as it is its own optional supplement, I don't really care. But I don't think it fits Scion's overall aesthetic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T07:29:34-08:00","id":43498,"title":"","content":"As far as the First Commandment? Technically, it says &quot;Thou shalt have no other gods BEFORE me.&quot; Technically, that could be interpreted as &quot;There are other gods, and it's okay to show them some respect, but you are NOT to honor them as being equal to or greater than I am. Sure, bow before Amaterasu in order to gain her favor. Maybe even attend a festival or two in her honor. MAYBE even offer her a quick prayer or offering now and then. But she is a LESSER GOD and you will always put ME first in your heart.&quot;<br /> <br /> Just a thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T10:13:18-08:00","id":43591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=43348#post43348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody picked a nit about Helios (a Titan) being the one actually responsible for making the sun rise?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unique game setting. Helios was spared the fate of being thrown into Tartarus but was never again trusted with the role of travelling across the heavens without divine escort. Apollo became this escort which is why (in game universe) he developed connections to the sun in later myths. So someone else needs to take up the mantle of escorting Helios across the heavens. Enter one of the PCs.<br /> <br /> Imagine the scenario being similar to Huitzilopochtli and Tonatiuh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T13:01:10-08:00","id":43675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=43348#post43348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody picked a nit about Helios (a Titan) being the one actually responsible for making the sun rise?</div> </div> </div> </div>The sunlight still being there but extremely dim is due to Helios still around but yes, Iry is correct. Helios was detached from being the true embodiment of the sun and no longer rode the heavens every day (which Apollo took up). The sun isn't GONE-gone, it's just an eternal twilight until the Greeks get their act together and either put Helios back in the sky or find another sun god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T13:12:57-08:00","id":43680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=43495#post43495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never said the Yazata and Deva consider each other Titan<i>spawn</i>, only <i>servants of the Titans</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I never said that you called them Titanspawn; just that there's ample support in Zoroastrian mythology to cast the Hindu deities as such if one chose to do so. Well, that and that I grateful that <b>Scion</b> didn't take this route, and that I hope they avoid doing this sort of thing with respect to Abrahamic myths. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=43495#post43495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for why I'm don't like the idea, well, firstly, I do not find the concept of a Pantheon with a single God (can it even be called a Pantheon at that point?) very interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has already been addressed: I'm not asking for a Pantheon; I'm asking for the Abrahamic mythologies to be treated in a manner that isn't dismissive of them, just like every other religion-based mythology in <b>Scion</b>. <br /> <br /> And if I was asking for a Pantheon, the same fuzziness of terminology that translates Japan's &quot;little gods&quot; into Scion's lingo could be used to build a Pantheon of angels \u2014 thus my mention of Nephilim (children of angels and humans) as possible counterparts to Scions if an Abrahamic Pantheon were to be included. Jews and musims have occasionally accused Christians of being polytheists due to their belief in the Trinity. Mormonism shows another way that the Abrahamic mythology could be cast in a vaguely polytheistic form. There are ways to do it, as long as you're willing to make a few compromises in the spirit of consistency with the game's premises. <br /> <br /> And to head it off at the pass: I'm not saying that the connections between the Abrahamic mythologies and the likes of Canaanite, Sumerian, Egyptian, Greek, and Arabian mythologies should be ignored; just that they shouldn't be presented as &quot;the Abrahamic faiths are a human invention supported by renegade Canaanite, Sumerian, Egyptian, Greek, and/or Arabian gods&quot;. The Devas' Titan includes Danu, who is enough like the Danu of the Tuatha that the Devas are wary around the Irish Gods; in a similar way, the Abrahamic God doesn't have to be the Canaanite El or Yahweh or the Arabian Allah; but said Pantheons could easily associate them and react accordingly. Ultimately, what I'm hearing you say is &quot;the clunkiest possible interpretation of Abrahamic mythology wouldn't work in <b>Scion</b>&quot;, paired with the assumption that said interpretation is the <i>only possible way to do it</i>. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1975-new-clan-weaknesses?p=4345#post4345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are also public relations to be considered. Is not the First Commandment 'Thou shalt have no other Gods before me'? Try getting into an alliance with the Japanese Gods while not showing deference to Amaterasu. She, at least, would only tell the messenger to politely leave. Zeus would probably thunderbolt him on the spot. And I really don't want to think of what Marduk would do. The Abrahamic God would essentially be left all alone to face the Wrath of the Titans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, &quot;clunkiest possible interpretation&quot;. This has already been addressed in part by unnatural1. I would add that an Abrahamic Pantheon would include Piety among its Virtues; IMHO, that would adequately cover the First Commandment issue. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=43495#post43495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is also the matter of the already extant Gods. Yahweh, I note, has already been discussed in detail. But what about Allah? How do you reconcile the God of Islam with the already extant Creator God of Arabian Mythology?</div> </div> </div> </div>Please enlighten me as to what difficulties you see here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T14:48:45-08:00","id":43732,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allah_as_Moon-god\" target=\"_blank\">Allah as Moon God</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T14:57:54-08:00","id":43739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if I was asking for a Pantheon, the same fuzziness of terminology that translates Japan's &quot;little gods&quot; into Scion's lingo could be used to build a Pantheon of angels \u2014 thus my mention of Nephilim (children of angels and humans) as possible counterparts to Scions if an Abrahamic Pantheon were to be included. Jews and musims have occasionally accused Christians of being polytheists due to their belief in the Trinity. Mormonism shows another way that the Abrahamic mythology could be cast in a vaguely polytheistic form. There are ways to do it, as long as you're willing to make a few compromises in the spirit of consistency with the game's premises. </div> </div> </div>It has been a long time since I read the Scion books, so feel free to correct me if I'm wrong, but aren't the 'little gods' of Japan lesser immortals? The only mechanical Gods are the supreme spirits of Shintoism, the greatest of Kami. Similarly I'd imagine angels fall into the lesser immortal category (albeit, very powerful ones). I am not knowledgeable about Mormonism so I cannot comment on that, but the concept of treating the Holy Trinity as separate beings is interesting. It strikes me as not unlike the treatment of Parvati and Kali as separate beings. Tell me, in this interpretation, would Jesus Christ be a Scion of the Son, a Scion of the Father, or the Son Himself using the Avatar Birthright?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And to head it off at the pass: I'm not saying that the connections between the Abrahamic mythologies and the likes of Canaanite, Sumerian, Egyptian, Greek, and Arabian mythologies should be ignored; just that they shouldn't be presented as &quot;the Abrahamic faiths are a human invention supported by renegade Canaanite, Sumerian, Egyptian, Greek, and/or Arabian gods&quot;. The Devas' Titan includes Danu, who is enough like the Danu of the Tuatha that the Devas are wary around the Irish Gods; in a similar way, the Abrahamic God doesn't have to be the Canaanite El or Yahweh or the Arabian Allah; but said Pantheons could easily associate them and react accordingly. Ultimately, what I'm hearing you say is &quot;the clunkiest possible interpretation of Abrahamic mythology wouldn't work in <b>Scion</b>&quot;, paired with the assumption that said interpretation is the <i>only possible way to do it</i>. </div> </div> </div>Then what would your explanation be? Are the younger Gods deliberately copying the older, or is the matter one of coincidence that in the same areas that the Canaanite El and Yahweh and the Arabian Allah once flourished rises a God who just happens to be very similar to these three?<br /> <br /> For that matter, is He that similar to all three? The Islamic Allah tends to get lumped together with the Judeo-Christian God as the Abrahamic God, but He does have some notable personality quirks (notably, the intense dislike of paparazzi) that, along with other things like the presence of Iblis (who is a Jinn as opposed to a fallen angel) instead of Lucifer, sometimes makes me wonder if that isn't oversimplifying things (like the Native-American Pantheon idea). Anyway, discussion for another day.<br /> <br /> Overall, I chose the 'clunkiest possible' interpretation because that appeared to me to be the one closest in spirit to the cultures whose mythology is being adapted. From your counter-arguments it appears that you are willing to do away with the most fundamental tenet of Abrahamic religion, that a follower of God does not bow before any other deity. If you feel that such a supplement would enhance the setting, fine. As I stated above (twice), I have no problem with it. It just seems to me to be the equivalent of the Aztec Gods stopping blood sacrifice because some of their allies disliked it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T15:26:34-08:00","id":43748,"title":"","content":"With regard to &quot;A follower of God does not bow before any other deity&quot; I have to ask if you read my post on that matter on the previous page?<br /> <br /> In the world of Scion, where there ARE other gods, it's easy to interpret the First Commandment as &quot;You can bow before other gods, but you cannot honor them more than you honor ME.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Thou shalt have no other gods before me&quot; doesn't actually say &quot;There ARE no other gods.&quot; It only says that no other god is to be held above or beside The One True God.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T15:37:01-08:00","id":43756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=43680#post43680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately, what I'm hearing you say is &quot;the clunkiest possible interpretation of Abrahamic mythology wouldn't work in <b>Scion</b>&quot;, paired with the assumption that said interpretation is the <i>only possible way to do it</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That clunky interpretation happens to be the most common one that covers how a large majority of current followers of the Abrahamic faiths perceive their religion. Yes, you CAN rip, tear and mangle their religion until it fits into Scion. That won't make anyone happy. You can toss in a Pantheon of Saints or Angels easy as pie, if you just handwave away all the many, many cosmological questions and issues raised by that. The Yazata are already skirting very close to that line, especially trying to take into account modern forms of their religion.<br /> <br /> The sheer level of contention on how such a pantheon could be included in Scion without either massive changes to Scion's fundamental narrative (I know you already strongly favor such changes, which I disagree with) or massive changes to the Abrahamic religions being portrayed is a sign that it would not be simple. There would be a great many people unhappy no matter how it was done. Why do it when instead they could write up the Polynesians or the Hittites or the Cherokee and <i>raise none of these issues at all</i>? There are tons of games for playing angels and demons, nephilim and saints, templars and holy priests. <br /> <br /> I'm not saying there couldn't be a Scion book about massively different settings, including one where Monotheism vs Polytheism is a major theme and the rules of the universe are very different. That could be a thing. It doesn't need to be a <i>central</i> thing. It's just fine, sitting on the margins, where it can be adopted or not. Monotheism doesn't need to be shoe-horned into everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T15:49:40-08:00","id":43766,"title":"","content":"\u201cshow courtesy and respect when dealing with\u2026\u201d is not the same thing as \u201cbow down before\u2026\u201d. And yes, in a <b>Scion</b> setting, I\u2019m willing to go with a version of the Abrahamic faiths who accept that other Pantheons are real (though they may disagree about what they really are), but that their own god is superior to the others and is to be worshipped exclusive to the worship of other gods. That\u2019s part and parcel to Piety, and is no different from any other Pantheon that favors Piety. <br /> <br /> And yeah, I know you\u2019ve said that you\u2019re fine with it as long as it\u2019s safely locked away in a supplement that you\u2019re free to ignore. I don\u2019t disagree with that, and didn\u2019t see any point in addressing it until you made it clear that you think I somehow missed that point. I would point out that <i>any</i> material that doesn\u2019t appear in one of the core books (e.g., the Yazata) could be given the same \u201cignore it if you don\u2019t like it\u201d treatment \u2014 though I sometimes get the impression that people who would be \u201cOK\u201d with Abrahamic mythology being addressed in a supplement rather than the core book would prefer it to come with a bold disclaimer up front to the effect of \u201cif you\u2019re a reasonable person and you get what <b>Scion</b> is all about, by all means disregard this supplement; it\u2019s meant only as a sop for those nuts who don\u2019t really Get It and keep on making irrational demands!\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T15:52:15-08:00","id":43767,"title":"","content":"No, it's because it represents a dramatic shift from the premise of Scion as we understand it and hope that it continues to be viewed by the developers and writers. It would be just as jarring to see Starjammers material dropped into D&amp;D 5th Edition as to see monotheism and playable elves in Scion. New, different and totally awesome interpretations of existing rules and material are the <i>express purpose</i> of spin-offs and supplements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T16:19:58-08:00","id":43782,"title":"","content":"\u201cPlayable elves\u201d is a whole different debate. As for monotheism, I\u2019ve already said that for the purpose of <b>Scion</b>, I\u2019d prefer a henotheistic model to a monotheistic one. <br /> <br /> And yeah, I certainly <i>do</i> hope that 2e takes a more open-minded approach as to what is and isn\u2019t acceptable than 1e took. As I\u2019ve said before, the tools that would make a playable Abrahamic faction doable would also address many of the difficulties <b>Scion</b> tends to have as it moves away from Eurocentric Pantheons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T16:31:05-08:00","id":43785,"title":"","content":"Difficult to see the Abrahamic religions as playable, unless there was only a game session that involved only those pantheons, since their very doctrine is so very against recognizing any other religion, much less deity, as worthy of respect. ....and then there's that annoying idea of a scion of an Abrahamic god...oh man, I can hear the fundamentalists (funny mentals?) now...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T16:37:07-08:00","id":43789,"title":"","content":"Yeah... the very idea of a &quot;Scion of Jesus&quot; would just be terribly offensive to many people. A &quot;Scion of Gabriel&quot; isn't much better and a &quot;Scion of St. Patrick&quot; is just weird since there were Saints that <i>had kids</i> and their kids weren't magical at all. The Abrahamic religions not only don't play well with others, they don't play well with the very <i>concept</i> of &quot;Scions&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T17:09:30-08:00","id":43802,"title":"","content":"After some research, isn't most early abrahamic religions actually founded on the in the Levantine religions that are largely polytheistic (with the exceptions of the split off cults that focused on one god to the exclusion of others)? The Caananite, Hittite, and Israelite religions that paved the way for the formation of sect of Yahweh that would eventually become very early Judaism. These religions that were the religions that Abraham was born in and Patriach of?<br /> <br /> After some research, I really don't see a difference from the very early Levantine Pantheons (which would be partially evolved into the monotheistic abrahamic religions in text (El Elohim, Yahweh, Ba'al all come from the Canaanite pantheon)) to that of say the Greek pantheon or the Egyptian pantheon.<br /> <br /> Seeing as the pantheons of Scion are not like the pantheons of real world pantheons (but they are based on), I don't see how making the Abrahamic pantheon be any different from the others. So there for I don't understand the argument that making this would be the odd duckling out for OOP. <br /> <br /> Thematically they could take gods from the Levantine Pantheons (in fact they could call it the Levantine Pantheon) and then mix in a bit of the religious figures of later evolution such as Ezekial and Mary the Virgin and maybe a bit of the figures that were added in due to books like Paradise Lost and other extra pieces that name the angels like The Divine Comedy and such and you have yourself a fictional but very function Scion Pantheon that represents a Very large portion of a Religious line (large enough that players can adapt their own gods based on the mythology, it's really no different from how the voodoo god's are. They are basically just a conglomeration of voodoo gods and others from the many many MANY religions of Africa allowing players to make their own and fit it in nicely.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly, I don't see why this is such a contentious issue when it is basically no different than any of the others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T17:52:53-08:00","id":43829,"title":"","content":"Because the ancient henotheistic and polytheistic roots of Abrahamic religions are <i>not</i> what most people seem to want out of the idea. The most common idea is saints and angels which distinctly <i>post-date</i> the henotheistic period of history. Basically anything from the Talmud, Bible or Quaran is monotheism straight up, and does not fit. A Caananite Pantheon would fit Scion just fine, but that isn't &quot;Abrahamic&quot; in the modern sense of the term.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T18:06:45-08:00","id":43843,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=43785#post43785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Difficult to see the Abrahamic religions as playable, unless there was only a game session that involved only those pantheons, since their very doctrine is so very against recognizing any other religion, much less deity, as worthy of respect. ....and then there's that annoying idea of a scion of an Abrahamic god...oh man, I can hear the fundamentalists (funny mentals?) now...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Minor bone of contention? As a practicing Christian, I really hate hearing people refer to the crazy Christians who bomb abortion clinics and picket soldier's funerals as &quot;Fundamentalists.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> The &quot;fundamentals&quot; of Christianity are love, compassion and tolerance. Any Christian you see who isn't practicing these concepts is about as far away from the fundamentals of Christianity as you can get.<br /> <br /> The highest command Christ had for us was &quot;Love God and love your neighbor as yourself.&quot; That's the fundamenals of Christianity. Crazy people who read one passage in the Old Testament and take THAT to mean what Christianity is all about are not &quot;Fundamentalists.&quot; Any Christian who practices mercy and compassion and tolerance toward others is more of a &quot;Fundamentalist&quot; than those nutjobs. They should be called something more like Christian Radical Fringe Groups, or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T18:25:09-08:00","id":43859,"title":"","content":"Oh, man; here we go\u2026<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll agree with unnatural1\u2019s position this far, at least: <b>Scion</b> isn\u2019t a game for dyed-in-the-wool \u201cFundamentalists\u201d, as the term is generally understood. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-06-2014, 09:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T18:43:33-08:00","id":43874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=43843#post43843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Minor bone of contention? As a practicing Christian, I really hate hearing people refer to the crazy Christians who bomb abortion clinics and picket soldier's funerals as &quot;Fundamentalists.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Would &quot;radical fundamentalists&quot; be a more appropriate term?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=43829#post43829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the ancient henotheistic and polytheistic roots of Abrahamic religions are <i>not</i> what most people seem to want out of the idea. The most common idea is saints and angels which distinctly <i>post-date</i> the henotheistic period of history. Basically anything from the Talmud, Bible or Quaran is monotheism straight up, and does not fit. A Caananite Pantheon would fit Scion just fine, but that isn't &quot;Abrahamic&quot; in the modern sense of the term.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's it. In a nutshell.<br /> <br /> I have zero problem with the early Levantine and Canaanite pantheons. How it might be explained how they hold up with current pantheons (and how a particular deity or two might have been confused with certain religions today) might need a lot of &quot;fast talk&quot; to get through however. But exploring them to see how they could fit in, along with Mesopotamian deities, I'd buy that game book.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T18:46:59-08:00","id":43877,"title":"","content":"IMHO, there\u2019s room for both; and there\u2019s potential for interesting interactions between Abrahamic and Canaanite factions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T19:12:28-08:00","id":43891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=43877#post43877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMHO, there\u2019s room for both; and there\u2019s potential for interesting interactions between Abrahamic and Canaanite factions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. One thing to ask then; what would bringing Christianity with all it's relatively modern incompatibilities even bring to the table of Scion that going back to ancient roots can't?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T19:18:43-08:00","id":43892,"title":"","content":"That's probably a better question than I realize...hmm...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T19:32:31-08:00","id":43898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=43874#post43874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would &quot;radical fundamentalists&quot; be a more appropriate term?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, because they're still &quot;radical&quot; about a set of beliefs that are NOT the &quot;fundamentals&quot; of Christianity. It's a semantics thing.<br /> <br /> I should point out that calling extreme Muslims &quot;fundamentalists&quot; is also incorrect. Islam has a lot more to say about tolerance and mercy than it does about killing infidels and shoving Islam down people's throats. These people read like two passages of the Koran and choose to believe that those statements are the entirety of the Koran. Same problem.<br /> <br /> As far as the topic at hand? Here are my thoughts.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I would LIKE a means to bring the Abrahamic faiths into Scion in a way that is respectful to both the Abrahamic faiths AND the other religions represented. That said? This thread, and many others like it, do a lot to prove that that's a very tall order. I have considered ways to bring the Abrahamic faiths into Scion and I haven't been able to come up with anything that works real well either. And if I, and the rest of the very intelligent people in this forum, haven't been able to come up with anything we can all agree on, then I have a hard time faulting the devs of the game if they can't either.<br /> <br /> And I definitely agree with Telgar and Samudra that letting the Abrahamic faiths be represented in an alternate setting kind of thing is probably for the best. People who aren't interested in bringing in the Abrahamic faiths can simply ignore them and those who are get their wish. Everyone wins. Now, it would be nice if the core books at least give some ideas about how to deal with the Abrahamic faiths in the core setting if one is so inclined, but I really don't need a full pantheon write-up in the core books. I don't think the issue should be completely ignored, but I don't think it needs the full deluxe treatment right out of the box.<br /> <br /> So my stance is that it would be nice to have, but I can survive if it never shows up. Letting it be an alternate setting is probably the safest way, and as long as everything is handled with respect, I can be happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T22:43:36-08:00","id":43967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">With regard to &quot;A follower of God does not bow before any other deity&quot; I have to ask if you read my post on that matter on the previous page?</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not, actually <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I'm very sorry for missing it, it was four in the morning for me so I was not at my most perceptive. I have read it now.<br /> <br /> First of, I'm totally in agreement with the henotheistic interpretation of the First Commandment. No problems there.<br /> <br /> My disagreement, and, I feel, the disagreement of everyone else that feels the Abrahamic Pantheon does not play well with Scion's setting, is with the interpretation of 'before me'. You are fine with treating it as 'defer to the other Gods as needed for PR' while I feel that goes counter to the essence of the religion. I especially feel that your suggestion that God might be fine with 'a quick prayer' to a foreign goddess is akin to saying that Ares has suddenly decided to become a pacifist. Sure both things <i>might</i> have happened, but it would make it an alternate setting and a matter for a supplement (which is a point I note everyone is in agreement with anyway, so Yay!).<br /> <br /> Now, don't get me wrong, there are a lot of problems the Pantheons have interacting with each other. The Maya with their dislike of anything death related probably feel the Egyptians need their collective animal heads examined. The Deva and Yazata, as noted above, probably cannot stand to be in the same room together. The Roman and Canaanite Gods still probably haven't gotten over the Rome-Carthage fiasco. But the Abrahamic Pantheon is the only one with the potential to rub <i>all</i> the other Pantheons off the wrong way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I\u2019ve said before, the tools that would make a playable Abrahamic faction doable would also address many of the difficulties <b>Scion</b> tends to have as it moves away from Eurocentric Pantheons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am having some trouble seeing how this is. There are certain Mythologies, like the Chinese with it's random people getting upgraded to Gods every other week, that don't fit well into Scion's framework, true. But they are equally incompatible with the Abrahamic faith's guidelines. The only Pantheons I can think of that are similar somewhat are the Yazata and the Loa, the former having influenced the Abrahamic religions to a degree and the latter having been influenced by them. In the case of the former, the Yazata are still treated as powers worthy of worship in their own right. They just also happen to be subservient to a God more powerful than any of them. The Loa are getting a revamp to bring them closer to the Orisha, who very much <i>are</i> divinities in their own right, though also paying respects to Oludumare. The presence of nigh-omnipotent Creator deities is not unusual in mythology. Oludomare, Nana Buluku, Itzamna and Viracocha prove that amply. What <i>is</i> unusual is the contention that they are the <i>only</i> Gods in that mythology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 01-07-2014, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T07:30:38-08:00","id":44154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=43967#post43967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did not, actually <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I'm very sorry for missing it, it was four in the morning for me so I was not at my most perceptive. I have read it now.<br /> <br /> First of, I'm totally in agreement with the henotheistic interpretation of the First Commandment. No problems there.<br /> <br /> My disagreement, and, I feel, the disagreement of everyone else that feels the Abrahamic Pantheon does not play well with Scion's setting, is with the interpretation of 'before me'. You are fine with treating it as 'defer to the other Gods as needed for PR' while I feel that goes counter to the essence of the religion. I especially feel that your suggestion that God might be fine with 'a quick prayer' to a foreign goddess is akin to saying that Ares has suddenly decided to become a pacifist. Sure both things <i>might</i> have happened, but it would make it an alternate setting and a matter for a supplement (which is a point I note everyone is in agreement with anyway, so Yay!).<br /> <br /> Now, don't get me wrong, there are a lot of problems the Pantheons have interacting with each other. The Maya with their dislike of anything death related probably feel the Egyptians need their collective animal heads examined. The Deva and Yazata, as noted above, probably cannot stand to be in the same room together. The Roman and Canaanite Gods still probably haven't gotten over the Rome-Carthage fiasco. But the Abrahamic Pantheon is the only one with the potential to rub <i>all</i> the other Pantheons off the wrong way.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem. Happens to all of us.<br /> <br /> Yeah, you'll notice that when I typed the &quot;offer a quick prayer&quot; part, I capitalized the word &quot;maybe.&quot; That's my way of emphasizing the importance of that word in the sentence. Yeah, God being okay with an actual act of worship to a foreign goddess is a BIG stretch. Showing respect and even deference to other gods in the interest of cooperation is probably acceptable to Him. But actively participating in the religion may not be. Now attending a festival or two in Amaterasu's honor would probably be okay. I'm not an expert, but I'm pretty sure most Shinto celebrations are relatively tame affairs that don't involve anything God would find truly offensive. Now, that may not be a standing rule, of course. I can imagine God would NOT want an Abrahamic Scion to even show up to a celebration in honor of, say, Dionysus? Big rolling orgy and &quot;sex, drugs, and rock 'n roll?&quot; Yeah, THAT may be going too far.<br /> <br /> The Abrahamic faiths, as others have pointed out, started out with a decidedly henotheistic world view. The whole &quot;There IS no God but ours&quot; attitude didn't really come into play until Christianity managed to take over Europe. The Tanakh (the official name of the &quot;Old Testament&quot;) specifically makes mention of many of the gods worshipped by Israel's pagan neighbors and mentions numerous times when the people of Israel turned at least part of their worship to these other gods. Islam specifically mentions the Djinn of previous Arab religions as being very real, and just as capable of converting to Islam and achieving salvation. So the henotheistic core of the Abrahamic faiths is a very real thing and was part of the original world view. Within Scion's setting, it would be very easy to say that henotheism is STILL the appropriate viewpoint for the Abrahamic Pantheon. The fact that most of their worshippers have become hardcore monotheists doesn't really have to be an issue. Those people are simply mistaken. Thus? The Abrahamic Pantheon COULD fit into the core setting without too much trouble. Christians, like myself, who play the game will simply have to accept that the setting doesn't work if the Abrahamic faiths really are the only game in town. Seeing as how that wasn't the real, original attitude of the religion anyway? I personally don't have any trouble accepting this. I don't think too many others would either.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I stand by what I said in my last post: bringing the Abrahamic faiths into the core setting should NOT be attempted unless the devs are supremely confident that they've figured out a way to do it in a way that shows respect to all the religions represented. It probably does work best as an alternate setting, as you and others say. But it COULD be made to work even in the core if properly handled. That's the key phrase: &quot;IF PROPERLY HANDLED.&quot; If the devs don't think they can do it right, then they definitely should not do it.<br /> <br /> And I'm not so sure that the Abrahamic Pantheon would rub EVERYONE the wrong way, if the Scion setting forces the henotheistic viewpoint. Yeah, the Abrahamic Pantheon is snooty and superior toward everyone else, but Companion tells us that the Devas can also irritate the other Pantheons just by pointing out the whole &quot;Ha, ha! Our religion is HUGE!&quot; thing. Oh, there's going to be friction, to be sure. But as you say, a LOT of the Pantheons have friction with each other. And honestly, that friction is exactly what makes inter-Pantheon interaction so interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T08:03:54-08:00","id":44170,"title":"","content":"What would the titan for the &quot;Pantheon&quot; be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T10:54:02-08:00","id":44283,"title":"","content":"You really have to ask?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.conspirazzi.com/wp-content/uploads/2012/09/tenacious-d/tenacious-d15.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T10:59:16-08:00","id":44286,"title":"","content":"So the Scion of Gabriel has to be recruiting a daughter of Anubis and a son of Zeus to form a band to stop the hellaishly nasty licks of the Abrahamic Titan and his metal band","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T11:02:44-08:00","id":44292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=43843#post43843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Minor bone of contention? As a practicing Christian, I really hate hearing people refer to the crazy Christians who bomb abortion clinics and picket soldier's funerals as &quot;Fundamentalists.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem confused about the Fundamentalist Christian movement's core beliefs. They are: the infallible nature of the Bible as God's own work (this being the one that tends to be &quot;to blame&quot; for their actions), the virgin birth of Jesus, the historical reality of Jesus and his miracles, his death being atonement for his sins, and his bodily resurrection.<br /> <br /> By and large the appellation &quot;Fundamentalist&quot; applies to a large majority of practicing Protestant Christians in the United States.<br /> <br /> With that said, I would prefer we deviate no further into discussing fundamentalist-modernist Christian schism within the Protestant movement because it tends to get people really, really worked up (for the record, unnatural1, your outlook is the modernist view). You'll note I encourage the polytheists from letting their personal practice and beliefs from getting in the way of arguing their points logically and rationally. It's not in the least constructive for people to get caught up in reactive sniping because <i>their</i> thing is being torn apart on the forums.<br /> <br /> You're also wrong about fundamentalist Islam. When people say fundamentalist muslims it's a misappellation. They mean fundamentalist Sufi muslims, who really do believe that Muhammad's primary lesson is that Islam must be spread by the sword if necessary and that muslims have lost their way and are not in <i>fitra</i> with Allah's intentions. But Sufism isn't the only sect that teaches similar tenets, and thus there are non-Sufist muslims who get involved in violent jihad against &quot;crusaders,&quot; and the West. Which is why the misappellation is so widespread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":889,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","user":"Dayen","date":". 01-07-2014, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T11:02:50-08:00","id":44293,"title":"","content":"But...but...virgin birth?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T11:39:11-08:00","id":44319,"title":"","content":"God has a screwy sense of humor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T11:43:23-08:00","id":44321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44286#post44286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Scion of Gabriel has to be recruiting a daughter of Anubis and a son of Zeus to form a band to stop the hellaishly nasty licks of the Abrahamic Titan and his metal band</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd include either a Scion of a Deva or Aesir in there somewhere but, yes. Precisely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T12:02:43-08:00","id":44340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44292#post44292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem confused about the Fundamentalist Christian movement's core beliefs. They are: the infallible nature of the Bible as God's own work (this being the one that tends to be &quot;to blame&quot; for their actions), the virgin birth of Jesus, the historical reality of Jesus and his miracles, his death being atonement for his sins, and his bodily resurrection.<br /> <br /> By and large the appellation &quot;Fundamentalist&quot; applies to a large majority of practicing Protestant Christians in the United States.<br /> <br /> With that said, I would prefer we deviate no further into discussing fundamentalist-modernist Christian schism within the Protestant movement because it tends to get people really, really worked up (for the record, unnatural1, your outlook is the modernist view). You'll note I encourage the polytheists from letting their personal practice and beliefs from getting in the way of arguing their points logically and rationally. It's not in the least constructive for people to get caught up in reactive sniping because <i>their</i> thing is being torn apart on the forums.<br /> <br /> You're also wrong about fundamentalist Islam. When people say fundamentalist muslims it's a misappellation. They mean fundamentalist Sufi muslims, who really do believe that Muhammad's primary lesson is that Islam must be spread by the sword if necessary and that muslims have lost their way and are not in <i>fitra</i> with Allah's intentions. But Sufism isn't the only sect that teaches similar tenets, and thus there are non-Sufist muslims who get involved in violent jihad against &quot;crusaders,&quot; and the West. Which is why the misappellation is so widespread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. I learned a lot today. Thanks!<br /> <br /> I agree with you, of course. I was a little worried when I chose to start this discussion, and I'm glad that so far I haven't started a flame war.<br /> <br /> Which means, yes, let's not push our luck and just move on to other topics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T12:17:08-08:00","id":44356,"title":"","content":"*shrugs* It's all about how one defines the word; <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fundamentalism\" target=\"_blank\">fundamentalism</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T12:51:49-08:00","id":44371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44292#post44292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With that said, I would prefer we deviate no further into discussing fundamentalist-modernist Christian schism within the Protestant movement because it tends to get people really, really worked up (for the record, unnatural1, your outlook is the modernist view). You'll note I encourage the polytheists from letting their personal practice and beliefs from getting in the way of arguing their points logically and rationally. It's not in the least constructive for people to get caught up in reactive sniping because <i>their</i> thing is being torn apart on the forums.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. I personally identify with the Fundamentalist position as outlined by Dayen to the point that I take offense when it\u2019s characterized as a bunch of crazies who bomb abortion clinics and picket soldiers\u2019 funerals (such people certainly exist, but are opposed by the average Fundamentalist as much as they are by everyone else); but it doesn\u2019t do anyone any good to get into a fight about it (and is almost certain to derail the topic, which isn\u2019t about what Christian beliefs are so much as it\u2019s about how best to represent Abrahamic faiths in the context of <b>Scion</b>), so I\u2019ve been holding my tongue.<br /> <br /> I think it was Samudra who commented earlier that it\u2019s possible that trying to do one Abrahamic faction may very well be tantamount to doing a Manitou Pantheon that mishmashes all native North American tribal beliefs into one undifferentiated whole. I tend to agree with this, as I tend to see drastic differences between Judeo-Christian mythology and Islamic mythology. Heck, the Loa could be considered to be something of an Abrahamic faction, to the extent that Carribean religions syncretized African beliefs and various forms of Christianity.<br /> <br /> Were it me, I\u2019d have one faction that arose out of the Levant region and had some early animosities with the Egyptian and Canaanite Pantheons; and I\u2019d have a separate faction that arose much later in the Arabian region and all but wiped out the Pantheon that used to dominate that region (the reason I\u2019d have said Pantheon all but wiped out is because there\u2019s so little information left about them that piecing together a functioning pre-Islam Arabian Pantheon is largely an exercise in guesswork and invention rather than research).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T13:01:52-08:00","id":44377,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure that makes a lot of sense. If you have the Arabian Pantheon, why are they wiped out by the rising Abrahamic Pantheon (which they coexisted with for thousands of years)? The Greek, Norse, Irish, Slavic and Gaulish Gods weren't wiped out by the Christanization of their people.<br /> <br /> And I'm still having trouble seeing Gabriel coming down and banging a mortal woman to create a Scion. Sure, the <i>entire Pantheon</i> could do nothing but adopt, but then they're adopting the literal spawn of demons (non-Abrahamic gods) to be their own warriors... and plus you have that issue with Apotheosis where mortals are becoming Archangels? Or whatever else you use to stand-in for the &quot;Gods&quot; of a one-God religion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T13:02:08-08:00","id":44378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44340#post44340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow. I learned a lot today. Thanks!<br /> <br /> I agree with you, of course. I was a little worried when I chose to start this discussion, and I'm glad that so far I haven't started a flame war.<br /> <br /> Which means, yes, let's not push our luck and just move on to other topics.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44356#post44356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*shrugs* It's all about how one defines the word; <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fundamentalism\" target=\"_blank\">fundamentalism</a></div> </div> </div> </div>It actually doesn't. The word &quot;fundamentalism&quot; and the actual capital-F &quot;Fundamentalist&quot; religious groups are not the same thing. This is like libertarianism and capital-L American Libertarianism.<br /> <br /> I suppose it's only fair to point out that there is an Fundamenlist Sufi sub-sect that eschews the Hadith for the teachings of Abu Bakr. Spoiler alert: Abu Bakr also encourages the spread of Islam at the point of a sword. So the short version is: it's complicated, but violence is the answer. But so is peace. The long version is that Muhammad's Hadith are contradictory to what is professed in the Qu'ran, which is the core conflict within Islam and honestly I could write a book about this and I would be the 10,000th person to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T13:07:13-08:00","id":44380,"title":"","content":"Never ceases to amaze me how a word can have entirely different meanings based on whether it's capitalized or not. I wonder, is that a flaw of english or does every language have to put up with such nonsense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T13:28:42-08:00","id":44401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heck, the Loa could be considered to be something of an Abrahamic faction, to the extent that Carribean religions syncretized African beliefs and various forms of Christianity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence why I welcome the revamping of the Loa to the Orishas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Were it me, I\u2019d have one faction that arose out of the Levant region and had some early animosities with the Egyptian and Canaanite Pantheons; and I\u2019d have a separate faction that arose much later in the Arabian region and all but wiped out the Pantheon that used to dominate that region (the reason I\u2019d have said Pantheon all but wiped out is because there\u2019s so little information left about them that piecing together a functioning pre-Islam Arabian Pantheon is largely an exercise in guesswork and invention rather than research).</div> </div> </div> </div>This does bring up the question of why Gabriel is holding down two dayjobs under two bosses who intensely dislike the idea of sharing followers.<br /> <br /> The good folks over at GBN did exactly that actually, creating a write-up of the Alihah using what little we know and a heavy dose of creative interpretation. It is one of my favourite fan supplements and makes me very sad that we don't know more about these fascinating Gods.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never ceases to amaze me how a word can have entirely different meanings based on whether it's capitalized or not. I wonder, is that a flaw of english or does every language have to put up with such nonsense?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of us got off easy. Indian scripts don't have capitalization. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T13:30:08-08:00","id":44402,"title":"","content":"On a personal level, if I were to bring the Abrahamic faiths into Scion, I would probably say that the God of the Abrahamic religions is the briefly-referenced Titan of Order who sided with the gods against the other Titans.<br /> <br /> The Angels of that Titan claim that it was the first and greatest Titan, and stands above the others. Whether this is a true fact, or merely a desire, is really moot. What matters is that YHVH is a very powerful being, who stands for order and a properly functioning world, and who is a potential ally against the other Titans, but who is also kind of a strange incarnation of reality rather than a human-like figure and thus is not wholly knowable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Remember - popcorn can feel pain.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1195-frivyeti","name":"FrivYeti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T14:07:00-08:00","id":44425,"title":"","content":"Y'know...it does seem that we do live in this real world of a titan of order...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T14:13:34-08:00","id":44430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44377#post44377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure that makes a lot of sense. If you have the Arabian Pantheon, why are they wiped out by the rising Abrahamic Pantheon (which they coexisted with for thousands of years)? The Greek, Norse, Irish, Slavic and Gaulish Gods weren't wiped out by the Christanization of their people.<br /> <br /> And I'm still having trouble seeing Gabriel coming down and banging a mortal woman to create a Scion. Sure, the <i>entire Pantheon</i> could do nothing but adopt, but then they're adopting the literal spawn of demons (non-Abrahamic gods) to be their own warriors... and plus you have that issue with Apotheosis where mortals are becoming Archangels? Or whatever else you use to stand-in for the &quot;Gods&quot; of a one-God religion.</div> </div> </div> </div>A few points:<br /> <br /> First, I\u2019m not necessarily positing a Pantheon, either in the singular or <i>as</i> a \u201cpantheon\u201d in the same sense that Egyptians, Greeks, etc. have pantheons; the jury\u2019s still out on that.<br /> <br /> Second: according to the \u201cGaulish Pantheon\u201d <b>Scion</b> supplement published in France, the Gaulish Pantheon <i>was</i> all but destroyed (by the Greek Pantheon\u2019s Roman Empire rather than by the Christianization of its people; but the precedent is there). I\u2019m personally of the opinion that Pantheons of religions for which real-world research material is sparse should be treated as either devastated or missing in the context of <b>Scion</b>. As well, the posited devastation of the Arabian Pantheon isn\u2019t the result of the mortal population being converted to Islam; it\u2019s the result of the Islamic \u201cOverworld faction\u201d going to war with the Arabian Pantheon directly.<br /> <br /> Third: if we posit that the Abrahamic \u201cPantheon\u201d(s) is/are composed of angels who rival the power of the gods, then the scions of said Pantheon(s) would be <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nephilim\" target=\"_blank\">nephilim</a>. Obviously, it\u2019s not a practice that the Pantheon condones under normal circumstances; but with the siege of the Titans, they may be willing to do things for the sake of survival that they wouldn\u2019t otherwise even consider.<br /> <br /> Fourth: this is another place where the notion of Champions (mortals who can achieve Hero status without actually being descended from any known gods) could prove useful, especially if the PSP includes some means of identifying and empowering potential Champions. And if we go with the Catholic notion of Saints as the end result of what happens when and if an Abrahamic Champion achieves Legend 9 (assuming they can even go beyond Legend 4), you have the potential for a \u201cPantheon\u201d composed of a mixture of angels and saints.<br /> <br /> Again, I don\u2019t have a fully fleshed out and rigorously playtested concept here; just some rough ideas of how it might be made to work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FrivYeti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44402#post44402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a personal level, if I were to bring the Abrahamic faiths into Scion, I would probably say that the God of the Abrahamic religions is the briefly-referenced Titan of Order who sided with the gods against the other Titans. The Angels of that Titan claim that it was the first and greatest Titan, and stands above the others. Whether this is a true fact, or merely a desire, is really moot. What matters is that YHVH is a very powerful being, who stands for order and a properly functioning world, and who is a potential ally against the other Titans, but who is also kind of a strange incarnation of reality rather than a human-like figure and thus is not wholly knowable.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is another notion I\u2019ve been contemplating. My concern about treating the Abrahamic God as a Titan comes mainly from the way that 1e treats all Titans as being subject to the Dark Virtues, and always presented as antagonists; but a <i>benevolent</i> Titan, subject to regular Virtues akin to the ones that the Pantheons have and working as an ally of the Pantheons against the other Titans, would be a reasonable compromise IMHO.<br /> <br /> (I\u2019m not sure I\u2019d go with the Titan of Order; my own admittedly biased inclination would be to take the Christian concept of \u201cGod is Love\u201d as the basis for such a Titan, with the emphasis being the Greek notion of <i>agape</i>.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-07-2014, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T14:34:22-08:00","id":44442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44377#post44377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure that makes a lot of sense. If you have the Arabian Pantheon, why are they wiped out by the rising Abrahamic Pantheon (which they coexisted with for thousands of years)? The Greek, Norse, Irish, Slavic and Gaulish Gods weren't wiped out by the Christanization of their people.<br /> <br /> And I'm still having trouble seeing Gabriel coming down and banging a mortal woman to create a Scion. Sure, the <i>entire Pantheon</i> could do nothing but adopt, but then they're adopting the literal spawn of demons (non-Abrahamic gods) to be their own warriors... and plus you have that issue with Apotheosis where mortals are becoming Archangels? Or whatever else you use to stand-in for the &quot;Gods&quot; of a one-God religion.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the whole &quot;Arch-Angel flying down and banging a woman&quot; thing, the whole Pantheon could do immaculate conception, or start siring Scions out of necessity for the war, or all adopt as you said---but the way I see it if they were to be all adopting it would be less adopting spawn of demons and more of converting them to their cause and enlightening them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44377#post44377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you have that issue with Apotheosis where mortals are becoming Archangels?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how that's an issue since that's an accepted occurrence in Scion, the children might become Gods of their own one day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T15:18:08-08:00","id":44474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44430#post44430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is another notion I\u2019ve been contemplating. My concern about treating the Abrahamic God as a Titan comes mainly from the way that 1e treats all Titans as being subject to the Dark Virtues, and always presented as antagonists; but a <i>benevolent</i> Titan, subject to regular Virtues akin to the ones that the Pantheons have and working as an ally of the Pantheons against the other Titans, would be a reasonable compromise IMHO.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea I'm currently kicking around is that (at the very least) the Angels of El are generally benevolent, at least towards humans (I'd probably only give them the Dark Virtue of Zealotry, and maybe Ambition for certain special ones. The rest would probably get Duty, Harmony, and Order). In general, they would do what angels are depicted as doing: helping people, delivering messages, and waging war with demons. The little tricky bit is that of course the demons are actually the Gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/93-xegek","name":"Xegek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar93_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T16:00:24-08:00","id":44499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egg</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how that's an issue since that's an accepted occurrence in Scion, the children might become Gods of their own one day.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hard to believe that an Abrahamic deity would be friendly to the idea of an archangel becoming a god. Since, as I recall, he is a &quot;jealous god...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T16:14:38-08:00","id":44515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44499#post44499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hard to believe that an Abrahamic deity would be friendly to the idea of an archangel becoming a god. Since, as I recall, he is a &quot;jealous god...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> You misunderstand; in this complete hypothetical the scions of the Abrahamic Pantheon go into Archangels instead of Gods. Mechanically identical, just a different label. Besides, I'm sure a little leeway would be fine. Scion 2e version of the jealous god will get over it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T16:34:52-08:00","id":44529,"title":"","content":"Well, if there's any accuracy in it, Metatron was once Enoch, and Sandalphon was once Elijah...so there are precedents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T16:41:49-08:00","id":44536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44529#post44529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if there's any accuracy in it, Metatron was once Enoch, and Sandalphon was once Elijah...so there are precedents.</div> </div> </div> </div>yep, this is accurate (at least, according to some kabbalists I know and the apocryphal book of Enoch)<br /> <br /> Edit- also, there is a story about Metatoron being punished by God because some rabbi has seen him and thought he was a god by itself, so there are &quot;two gods in heaven&quot; and by that explaining why there are good and evil. That person was named as heretic so even his name wasn't to be said (he is named as &quot;Other&quot;, I think), and Metatoron was punished. I think this is a good example to all of the &quot;jealous God&quot; thing","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 01-07-2014, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T17:30:20-08:00","id":44563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xegek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44474#post44474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The idea I'm currently kicking around is that (at the very least) the Angels of El are generally benevolent, at least towards humans (I'd probably only give them the Dark Virtue of Zealotry, and maybe Ambition for certain special ones. The rest would probably get Duty, Harmony, and Order). In general, they would do what angels are depicted as doing: helping people, delivering messages, and waging war with demons. The little tricky bit is that of course the demons are actually the Gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I hope that 2e dispenses with the Dark Virtues altogether. What\u2019s the difference between Zealotry and Piety, other than degree? That is, how does someone with Zealotry differ from someone whose Piety has pushed him into Self-Righteousness? I\u2019d rather \u201cantagonist\u201d be defined by Virtue extremes (to the extent that it\u2019s hardwired into the Virtues system at all) rather than separate Dark Virtues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T17:37:51-08:00","id":44571,"title":"","content":"o..I dunno...I think piety allows for questions...doubts, which encourage strengthening faith. Zealotry doesn't...at all. As I see it anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T17:54:51-08:00","id":44580,"title":"","content":"And Self-Righteousness, Piety\u2019s Virtue extreme? Does that leave room for questions?<br /> <br /> EDIT: actually, Zealotry is a near-perfect fit to Conviction\u2019s Virtue extremity; it\u2019s even in the name.<br /> <br /> But going with your point, I\u2019d say that Piety would <i>still</i> be a better choice for an Abrahamic faction than Zealotry.<br /> <br /> More generally, I don\u2019t think that <b>Scion</b>\u2019s Virtue set from the core book is sufficient to handle an Abrahamic faction. Going to <b>Exalted</b>, there are four Virtues, only two of which appear in <b>Scion</b> (Conviction and Valor). Interestingly, the other two (Compassion and Temperence) are Virtues that I\u2019d use for an Abrahamic faction; I\u2019d use Order and Piety as the other two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-07-2014, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T19:25:10-08:00","id":44611,"title":"","content":"Hmm...I should think that there are differences from a historical perspective. I don't think Compassion, Temperance, or even Piety existed much in the beginning of any of those religions.. whereas today, may be different depending on sect. Naturally, zealotry gets a lot of press.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T19:44:42-08:00","id":44619,"title":"","content":"Compassion is a founding principle of Christianity. Piety is what the First Commandment is all about<b></b>: \u201cScions who espouse this Virtue exalt and respect their God, their ancestors and the traditions of their forebears, taking strength from the wisdom of the ancients. There is no situation that can't be addressed by heeding the commandments of the Gods and the deeds of one's ancestors. Those who break with tradition insult the hard work and sacrifice of their predecessors and show a reckless arrogance that can only lead to misfortune.\u201d Not so much the ancestors bit; but the rest fits quite well. Temperence is a bit more of a stretch, but can be seen in the reflection of the Seven Daedly Sins: Greed, Gluttony, and Lust can all be seen as violations of Temperence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T20:12:18-08:00","id":44628,"title":"","content":"We're going to have to disagree here. Without Roman Catholicism and it's willingness to do anything and everything to be the top power, including committing the worst atrocities, Christianity would have been little better than a not-so-well-known Judaic sect that died almost as soon as it began. When I was an altar boy (unmolested thank you very much), I once thought of becoming a priest. Until I really read the Bible and studied the Church's history...and realized that I could never be a priest. Indeed, I turned my back upon the whole of Christianity. Of course, that's in the history. What it has become in the past half century or so...well, I can only look at today's pope and feel a measure of admiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T20:54:15-08:00","id":44644,"title":"","content":"If I had a choice between someone with your hostility doing an Abrahamic faction and no Abrahamic faction at all, I\u2019d prefer the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T21:17:34-08:00","id":44649,"title":"","content":"Seriously-I don't think it should happen, but if it were to, I'd want someone who actually respects the mythology.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, how the flying fuck did we get to 17 pages on this subject?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-08-2014, 12:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T21:31:29-08:00","id":44661,"title":"","content":"Don't call it mythology. Seriously, that's a big deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T21:42:58-08:00","id":44666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44661#post44661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't call it mythology. Seriously, that's a big deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that big of a deal. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44649#post44649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously-I don't think it should happen, but if it were to, I'd want someone who actually respects the mythology.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, how the flying fuck did we get to 17 pages on this subject?</div> </div> </div> </div>40 posts per page is the way to go~<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T21:59:25-08:00","id":44679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44661#post44661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't call it mythology. Seriously, that's a big deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd appreciate it if the leeway given in one direction is returned in the other. One man's myth is another man's legend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T22:00:38-08:00","id":44680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44644#post44644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I had a choice between someone with your hostility doing an Abrahamic faction and no Abrahamic faction at all, I\u2019d prefer the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I see pretty much two options for this:<br /> <br /> 1. The Abrahamic Pantheon would consist of Angels and use the mythology associated with as gods with El or Jehovah or Yahweh or Alla or whatever as the head of it similar to the All-Father is to the Aesir.<br /> <br /> 2. The Abrahamic Pantheon would pull from the mythologies of its roots and would actually pull from the Levantine Pantheons for the gods.<br /> <br /> <br /> Personally I would be fine with either options because I can see some good stories from both and that's all I really care about. However I see the Latter actually being both doable and popular for the following reasons:<br /> <br /> A. The Former seems to be quite contentious. As an athiest I don't quite understand but I assume it hits straight towards home and it would prolly be harder to remain impartial than most others that pull from a lot of the ancient religions.<br /> <br /> B. The latter is the root of the Abrahamic religions and so have some things in common. <br /> <br /> C. The latter is less contentious and is less close to home for practitioners of those religions and so easier to stay impartial to the deities. <br /> <br /> Personally I could do both... but I see the Latter much more believable and much less of an argument maker. It already has Pantheons so they don't have to make things gods that weren't gods already, the religions had relationships with with the Egyptian religions so there are already relations to build off. I don't know... it sees to write itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T22:01:28-08:00","id":44681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44666#post44666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not that big of a deal.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking from personal experience, yes, it is. I've been yelled at for doing that by people I was otherwise on great terms with. I've had teachers reject papers for doing that. It's <i>not mythology</i> to Christians. It's <i>their religion</i>. Do not tell someone their religion is made up, or is not the truth. They do not ever appreciate it. That issue Dayen mentioned earlier, about Fundamentalist Christians believing in the inerrancy of the Bible? It's serious. The Bible is the Word of God. Don't question it, don't compare it to other religions and don't suggest it isn't His Word.<br /> <br /> It is a very big deal. It is an extremely volatile subject. Maybe not to you, personally, but I imagine you know at least one person that would be deeply offended if you told them the Bible was mythology, or compared the Bible to the Eddas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T22:06:11-08:00","id":44684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44679#post44679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd appreciate it if the leeway given in one direction is returned in the other. One man's myth is another man's legend.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but the polytheists I've met don't <i>tend</i> to be as touchy about the subject as the monotheists I've met. I never had a problem talking with the voodoo practitioner I knew. She was happy to answer questions, help me with research, provide an insider opinion, etc. She engaged in class discussions about the evolution of her religion from the Yoruba sources. My interactions with Christians have been much less forgiving regarding how their religion is treated.<br /> <br /> But, yes, generally if you call it Christian theology, you should probably call it Norse theology, too. That just isn't common parlance as far as I've encountered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T22:08:08-08:00","id":44685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44681#post44681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking from personal experience, yes, it is. I've been yelled at for doing that by people I was otherwise on great terms with. I've had teachers reject papers for doing that. It's <i>not mythology</i> to Christians. It's <i>their religion</i>. Do not tell someone their religion is made up, or is not the truth. They do not ever appreciate it. That issue Dayen mentioned earlier, about Fundamentalist Christians believing in the inerrancy of the Bible? It's serious. The Bible is the Word of God. Don't question it, don't compare it to other religions and don't suggest it isn't His Word.<br /> <br /> It is a very big deal. It is an extremely volatile subject. Maybe not to you, personally, but I imagine you know at least one person that would be deeply offended if you told them the Bible was mythology, or compared the Bible to the Eddas.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's anecdotal. I'm Christian, I know I don't speak for every single member, but it's not something I or any of the others that I know would care about. Besides, it goes both ways. I'm 99% sure on these forums there's one person that's a member Norse religion (sorry dude, I don't remember the name) and even though he's a minority it's still fair if we call his mythology to call mine (yours, ours, whatever) mythology too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T22:31:06-08:00","id":44692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44661#post44661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't call it mythology. Seriously, that's a big deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve been using the term to refer to the stories and characters featured in the Abrahamic faiths without reference to any truth value. But yeah; I wouldn\u2019t expect <b>Scion</b> to talk about the \u201cAbrahamic mythologies\u201d any more than it talks about the \u201cNordic mythologies\u201d: it talks about the Aesir; it talks about the Creatures, Guides, and Relics associated with the Aesir; it talks about the stories related to the Aesir; but it talks about all of these things as if they were <i>true</i> \u2014 because, in the context of the game, they <i>are</i> true. It doesn\u2019t refer to them as myths, except in the sense of being epic stories influenced by Fate: <i>certainly</i> not in the sense of \u201cthese are just make-believe.\u201d<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T22:32:07-08:00","id":44693,"title":"","content":"On this matter? I generally use the word &quot;Mythology&quot; only when I'm talking about the actual stories of the religions in question. For simplicity's sake. I try very hard to show respect to all religious beliefs, whether I share them or not. Thus, I try to approach all religious views with the same respect that I approach my own. And if I ever slip up on that front, don't hesitate to call me on it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T22:41:03-08:00","id":44698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=42580#post42580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not understanding your logic. How would adding the Orisha cheapen the Loa when they ARE the Loa (except for Damballah)? And they're hardly the only religion that's done a total 180 in the course of its history.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> I think you have the story slightly confused. The God Marduk created the World from the body of Tiamat. And while Tiamat is definitely the original Mother of Dragons, I don't think she herself is ever described as a dragon, though someone better acquainted with Mesopotamian iconography could give you a more conclusive answer. Also, Tiamat is prime Titan material, so being her Scion is a remote possibility at best.</span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, first I thought some people wanted the Orisha as a SECOND African pantheon, and I thought that it made Africa seem better than the rest of the world.<br /> <br /> As with the dragon thing, I saw a special on either the History channel or Discovery about Dragons in general. The special said that the first instance of a dragon in Western folklore was a Sumerian tale of how (Bell?) the dragon goddess defeated an evil dragon (I forgot the name) and made the world from his body. Later on, there was a Jewish story about this one Jew who came to the Sumerians (I forget his name) and denounced the Sumerians dragon goddess saying that the dragon wasn't a god. According to the tale, he was thrown into a stadium to be eaten by lions, and by the grace of God, wasn't eaten by said lions.<br /> <br /> Am I wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T22:57:36-08:00","id":44710,"title":"","content":"It would be interesting if there were Scions of Angels, but I remember that it was talked about before as Nephilim. Also, the books didn't think of them kindly. According to them, Nephilim were the by-product of humans and FALLEN angels. Most of them were wiped out by God, a few were left as a reminder. So...more Titanspawn than Scion. Still I think that if you want Abrahamic, writing about the Caannite pantheon is the way to go, because zealous Christians and Muslims realizing the existence of the Gods and not reacting to them is on a superhero comic book level of ignorance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T23:00:30-08:00","id":44713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44698#post44698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, first I thought some people wanted the Orisha as a SECOND African pantheon, and I thought that it made Africa seem better than the rest of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>They <i>would</i> be the second African Pantheon, the first being the Pesedjet. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44698#post44698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As with the dragon thing, I saw a special on either the History channel or Discovery about Dragons in general. The special said that the first instance of a dragon in Western folklore was a Sumerian tale of how (Bell?) the dragon goddess defeated an evil dragon (I forgot the name) and made the world from his body. Later on, there was a Jewish story about this one Jew who came to the Sumerians (I forget his name) and denounced the Sumerians dragon goddess saying that the dragon wasn't a god. According to the tale, he was thrown into a stadium to be eaten by lions, and by the grace of God, wasn't eaten by said lions.<br /> <br /> Am I wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019re probably thinking of Daniel, who was taken captive by the Babylonians when they conquered Israel and who refused to worship their gods on the grounds that his God didn\u2019t want him to. Very different from the impression you describe of someone showing up uninvited and sticking his nose where it didn\u2019t belong. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T01:01:46-08:00","id":44759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44685#post44685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's anecdotal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as someone who has been threatened with very real physical violence regarding the subject, and knowing a decent number of people who share similar stories, it is a widespread anecdotal experience that should not be dismissed. But there are extremists and paragons in every organization regardless of what that organization happens to be.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think it is a problem of definition. Somewhere along the line people began to confuse the term 'myth' with something that is 'false', instead of the older definition which did not make any judgement about the potential veracity of the subject. Of course there is nothing much to be done about that, since the newer definition has made its way into our dictionaries at this point. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T05:50:31-08:00","id":44840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44759#post44759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking as someone who has been threatened with very real physical violence regarding the subject, and knowing a decent number of people who share similar stories, it is a widespread anecdotal experience that should not be dismissed. But there are extremists and paragons in every organization regardless of what that organization happens to be.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think it is a problem of definition. Somewhere along the line people began to confuse the term 'myth' with something that is 'false', instead of the older definition which did not make any judgement about the potential veracity of the subject. Of course there is nothing much to be done about that, since the newer definition has made its way into our dictionaries at this point. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I understand that there are people who get seriously offended by even the slightest notion that their beliefs may be false. I do, My father is one of them. But 'mythology' is a pretty widely used word to describe or group up the stories and myths of a culture. The Abrahamic faiths are a culture (or several) and they do have stories (their amount of truth depends on the person you ask but they are still stories). I think the very nature of this forum topic (discussing how one would or if one should convert the Abrahamic religions into that of the world of Scion) means that we don't have tip toe or avoid words that slightly <i>might</i> offend some one.<br /> <br /> Lore could work too but I could see someone having a problem with that too. They both work in conveying our ideas so I don't see any point in avoiding a word just because some people (probably those who wouldn't like this topic any way, they might think it blasphemous) might get offended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T06:04:44-08:00","id":44847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44619#post44619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Compassion is a founding principle of Christianity. Piety is what the First Commandment is all about<b></b>: \u201cScions who espouse this Virtue exalt and respect their God, their ancestors and the traditions of their forebears, taking strength from the wisdom of the ancients. There is no situation that can't be addressed by heeding the commandments of the Gods and the deeds of one's ancestors. Those who break with tradition insult the hard work and sacrifice of their predecessors and show a reckless arrogance that can only lead to misfortune.\u201d Not so much the ancestors bit; but the rest fits quite well. Temperence is a bit more of a stretch, but can be seen in the reflection of the Seven Daedly Sins: Greed, Gluttony, and Lust can all be seen as violations of Temperence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would suggest Conviction and Endurance in place of Compassion and Temperance. This Pantheon is already bending over backwards to try and fit in Scion; introducing two random new Virtues that no one else has (and honestly, those two Virtues don't really gel with any other Pantheon) will not help its case. Endurance resonates with the martyrs of the religion and is equally symbolic of the rejection of the seven deadly sins, and Conviction is the belief in their own rightness that helped them conquer most of the world. You might not agree with the latter (especially if you want to put that down to Piety), but as you yourself said, Compassion is the founding principle of <i>Christianity</i>. It does not gel well with the picture of Islam's more demanding deity. Or are you now set on splitting the Abrahamic Pantheon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T06:27:37-08:00","id":44857,"title":"","content":"The problem with using Abrahamic beliefs (as opposed to Levantine and Canaanite) is the desire for some historical accuracy. And how can anyone wanting any level of accuracy go without delving into the history of the Bible, Tanakh, and Quran or their respective faiths without going indepth in that first bunch of books called the Old Testament? (The first 17 or so books are supposedly historical, the middle five are poetic and philosophical, while the last 17 are prophetic.) Skipping the OT is forgetting the patriarch and founder Abraham...and if that were to happen, then it kinda loses the reason of having an &quot;Abraham&quot;-ic belief to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T07:21:34-08:00","id":44894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44847#post44847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would suggest Conviction and Endurance in place of Compassion and Temperance. This Pantheon is already bending over backwards to try and fit in Scion; introducing two random new Virtues that no one else has (and honestly, those two Virtues don't really gel with any other Pantheon) will not help its case. Endurance resonates with the martyrs of the religion and is equally symbolic of the rejection of the seven deadly sins, and Conviction is the belief in their own rightness that helped them conquer most of the world. You might not agree with the latter (especially if you want to put that down to Piety), but as you yourself said, Compassion is the founding principle of <i>Christianity</i>. It does not gel well with the picture of Islam's more demanding deity. Or are you now set on splitting the Abrahamic Pantheon?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not set on anything; but yeah, I\u2019m open to a split. I could be convinced that Conviction is more appropriate than Piety, perhaps; but to me, Piety and Conviction are like Courage and Valor: while they\u2019re different things, they\u2019re similar enough that including both in the same faction is problematic: they\u2019re essentially different spins on a common theme.<br /> <br /> As for Compassion being unique to Christianity: is it? Leaving aside for the moment the claims that Christians don\u2019t do Compassion, surely it isn\u2019t the only religion in the history of mankind to have something like \u201clove thy neighbor as thyself\u201d as a core teaching. Surely there\u2019s a Pantheon out there that prizes Compassion. Right?<br /> <br /> And if Compassion <i>is</i> unique to Christianity, why <i>not</i> include it? Virtues are rules-light enough that it wouldn\u2019t take a lot of space to put it in. Or are you saying that there\u2019s no room for Compassion in <b>Scion</b>?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44857#post44857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with using Abrahamic beliefs (as opposed to Levantine and Canaanite) is the desire for some historical accuracy. And how can anyone wanting any level of accuracy go without delving into the history of the Bible, Tanakh, and Quran or their respective faiths without going indepth in that first bunch of books called the Old Testament? (The first 17 or so books are supposedly historical, the middle five are poetic and philosophical, while the last 17 are prophetic.) Skipping the OT is forgetting the patriarch and founder Abraham...and if that were to happen, then it kinda loses the reason of having an &quot;Abraham&quot;-ic belief to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, <b>Scion</b> is a game about myths made real, not a treatise on the factuality of myths; so what\u2019s the problem with saying that most of the Old Testament\u2019s history is accurate in at least the broad outlines? Surely you\u2019re not saying that stories such as Gilgamesh, Beowulf, or the Illiad should be accepted or rejected in the world of <b>Scion</b> based on how much or little historical support there is for them in the real world?<br /> <br /> We\u2019re not seeking <i>historical</i> accuracy; we\u2019re seeking <i>mythological</i> accuracy. The former is useful when it provides a framework for the latter; but it shouldn\u2019t be used to <i>strangle</i> the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T07:22:03-08:00","id":44895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44698#post44698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, first I thought some people wanted the Orisha as a SECOND African pantheon, and I thought that it made Africa seem better than the rest of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would a second African pantheon make Africa seem better than the rest of the world?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Remember - popcorn can feel pain.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1195-frivyeti","name":"FrivYeti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T07:40:24-08:00","id":44897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FrivYeti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44895#post44895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would a second African pantheon make Africa seem better than the rest of the world?</div> </div> </div> </div>Europe: Aesir, Dodekatheon, Tuatha.<br /> Asia: Amatsukami, Celestial Bureaucracy, Devas, Yazatas? <br /> Africa: Pesedjet<br /> Carribean: Loa<br /> America: Aztlanti<br /> <br /> Yeah; I don\u2019t see a problem with there being a second African Pantheon, or even a third. The setting could stand to have a few Middle Eastern Pantheons, four or five American Pantheons (say, three or four north of the Aztlanti and another one or two south of them), a couple in the Pacific (say, an Australian one and a Polynesian one), and maybe even a few more in Asia (it\u2019s a big continent, and official material hasn\u2019t covered Russia, Mongolia, the Caucasus region, etc.); so adding one more to Africa is potentially not going far <i>enough</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T07:53:33-08:00","id":44904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Egg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44685#post44685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's anecdotal. I'm Christian, I know I don't speak for every single member, but it's not something I or any of the others that I know would care about. Besides, it goes both ways. I'm 99% sure on these forums there's one person that's a member Norse religion (sorry dude, I don't remember the name) and even though he's a minority it's still fair if we call his mythology to call mine (yours, ours, whatever) mythology too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am Asatru. I'm fairly certain there's another lurking around here. Trust me, I am far beyond caring about the general perceptions of my faith. I spent a large part of my career home-based in &quot;God's country,&quot; which is everywhere except New England and California from what I can discern. I worked closely with predominantly Christian gentlemen. I understand that there are some who take grave offense to the imaginary slighting of their deeply held beliefs. I am not in the habit of coddling them; if they are going to insist my religion is pure mythology, then they need to be prepared to accept that I feel the same way about theirs. I don't (I can clearly discern extant themes ripped whole-cloth from other religions and thus am not into questioning the historicity of the events, merely which window dressing is applied to them), but they need to be prepared for the eventuality of it.<br /> <br /> If we are going to discuss these subjects like the adults we are, we have to allow that people are going to have differing opinions about our respective faiths. Even if that faith is Abrahamic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T07:55:37-08:00","id":44906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44894#post44894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not set on anything; but yeah, I\u2019m open to a split. I could be convinced that Conviction is more appropriate than Piety, perhaps; but to me, Piety and Conviction are like Courage and Valor: while they\u2019re different things, they\u2019re similar enough that including both in the same faction is problematic: they\u2019re essentially different spins on a common theme.<br /> <br /> As for Compassion being unique to Christianity: is it? Leaving aside for the moment the claims that Christians don\u2019t do Compassion, surely it isn\u2019t the only religion in the history of mankind to have something like \u201clove thy neighbor as thyself\u201d as a core teaching. Surely there\u2019s a Pantheon out there that prizes Compassion. Right?<br /> <br /> And if Compassion <i>is</i> unique to Christianity, why <i>not</i> include it? Virtues are rules-light enough that it wouldn\u2019t take a lot of space to put it in. Or are you saying that there\u2019s no room for Compassion in <b>Scion</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you do decide to split it, then I must ask again, why is Gabriel doing double duty for two Gods who are known to be reluctant to share followers?<br /> <br /> I would suggest both Conviction and Piety. Conviction is the belief in the rightness of your cause, and Piety is the belief in the rightness of your Pantheon. The Pesedjet possess both, I see no problem in their inclusion. Also, Courage and Valour are different things. One propels you to fight, the other propels you to act honourably. Valour has out of combat applications, such as helping an old lady cross the street or help a cat out of a tree. It is the general 'friendly neighbourhood superhero' Virtue, and thus quite compatible with Courage.<br /> <br /> There are many religions that hold 'loving thy neighbour' as an ideal. There are no mythologies that do so. I will echo the feelings of Dean Shomshak on another thread. While deciding the Virtue set of the Shen, he realized that, while the culture and religion strongly favoured Order, none of the great heroes of Chinese Myth ever give a shit about laws. So Order is not a fit Virtue even if the religion came up with Legalism. Similarly, Compassion is an ideal for many religions. For their Gods? Not so much. Even the Pantheons that are heavily invested in, and deeply care about, protecting their peoples, like the Aztec and Hindu, this is best represented by other Virtues. In both these cases, the Gods have a Duty to protect their worshippers (and yes, I know that the Deva in Companion don't have Duty. That is but one part of that chapter that needs serious revamping).<br /> <br /> There is room for compassion (small c) in Scion. Very much so. But to create a new Virtue that has only one Pantheon as an adherent? That smacks of Special Snowflake Syndrome. Of course, if we're still discussing the Abrahamic Pantheon as an optional 'shard' like supplement, then go for it. Introducing one-off Virtues is just one of the things that optional supplements are there for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 01-08-2014, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T08:07:51-08:00","id":44915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44894#post44894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not set on anything; but yeah, I\u2019m open to a split. I could be convinced that Conviction is more appropriate than Piety, perhaps; but to me, Piety and Conviction are like Courage and Valor: while they\u2019re different things, they\u2019re similar enough that including both in the same faction is problematic: they\u2019re essentially different spins on a common theme.<br /> <br /> As for Compassion being unique to Christianity: is it? Leaving aside for the moment the claims that Christians don\u2019t do Compassion, surely it isn\u2019t the only religion in the history of mankind to have something like \u201clove thy neighbor as thyself\u201d as a core teaching. Surely there\u2019s a Pantheon out there that prizes Compassion. Right?<br /> <br /> And if Compassion <i>is</i> unique to Christianity, why <i>not</i> include it? Virtues are rules-light enough that it wouldn\u2019t take a lot of space to put it in. Or are you saying that there\u2019s no room for Compassion in <b>Scion</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the very real sense that most of the religions we're including in Scion were codified in the light of harsh realities that brooked very little room for mercy or compassion, Christianity stands apart. Although not very far from the Loa/Orisha, which is also a religion steeped in the idea of charity, togetherness in struggle, and compassion. It also manages to not need Compassion being a specific virtue to express itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44894#post44894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, <b>Scion</b> is a game about myths made real, not a treatise on the factuality of myths; so what\u2019s the problem with saying that most of the Old Testament\u2019s history is accurate in at least the broad outlines? Surely you\u2019re not saying that stories such as Gilgamesh, Beowulf, or the Illiad should be accepted or rejected in the world of <b>Scion</b> based on how much or little historical support there is for them in the real world?<br /> <br /> We\u2019re not seeking <i>historical</i> accuracy; we\u2019re seeking <i>mythological</i> accuracy. The former is useful when it provides a framework for the latter; but it shouldn\u2019t be used to <i>strangle</i> the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are some points within the Abrahamic tradition that would need specific refuting for Scion to continue to make sense. For instance, Yahweh supposedly banished the Abrahamic equivalent of Titans from the mortal plane in exchange for a promise to keep his angels out. Which both sides have sort of broken quite a lot. So much in fact that the idea of the Fatebindings that kept the other pantheons out of the world until now falls apart in light of the shenanigans of Abraham's sons, literal and spiritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T08:13:58-08:00","id":44917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44915#post44915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although not very far from the Loa/Orisha, which is also a religion steeped in the idea of charity, togetherness in struggle, and compassion. It also manages to not need Compassion being a specific virtue to express itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd just like to point out that while the Loa might be ideals of compassion, the Orisha are very emphatically not. Oh <i>Gods</i> are they not! Rampant slavery, wife-beatings, mutilation of an entire country, getting two lifelong friends to kill each other for the heck of it, tricking your co-wife into serving her ear to your hot-headed husband, anally violating an elephant with one's entire body...you get the picture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 01-08-2014, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T08:23:39-08:00","id":44924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44917#post44917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd just like to point out that while the Loa might be ideals of compassion, the Orisha are very emphatically not. Oh <i>Gods</i> are they not! Rampant slavery, wife-beatings, mutilation of an entire country, getting two lifelong friends to kill each other for the heck of it, tricking your co-wife into serving her ear to your hot-headed husband, anally violating an elephant with one's entire body...you get the picture.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't strictly agree, but you're right that it's not quite so important. That's the dichotomy between the religion of slaves and of freemen, I suppose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T09:34:43-08:00","id":44947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44894#post44894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Compassion being unique to Christianity: is it? Leaving aside for the moment the claims that Christians don\u2019t do Compassion, surely it isn\u2019t the only religion in the history of mankind to have something like \u201clove thy neighbor as thyself\u201d as a core teaching. Surely there\u2019s a Pantheon out there that prizes Compassion. Right?</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm pretty sure Buddha had that compassion schtick down earlier. But earlier than that? I think I read that Dionysus might have said a few things. But the prime virtue historically speaking has ever been Order. More to the point, the order imposed by the gods. The gods pretty much did what they wanted to as long as they followed that order. Can't have slavery, a caste system, sacrifices, etc., if compassion is a prime virtue in that order.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44894#post44894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, <b>Scion</b> is a game about myths made real, not a treatise on the factuality of myths; so what\u2019s the problem with saying that most of the Old Testament\u2019s history is accurate in at least the broad outlines? Surely you\u2019re not saying that stories such as Gilgamesh, Beowulf, or the Illiad should be accepted or rejected in the world of <b>Scion</b> based on how much or little historical support there is for them in the real world?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on how you define the broad outlines. You can't deny the very actions that made them what they are, or how and why they became so lodged in history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T10:49:47-08:00","id":44986,"title":"","content":"Oy vey.<br /> <br /> For clarity's sake, I am a Christian(member of the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter Day Saints, if it matters). I did not intend the use of the word mythology to be offensive, but rather to keep it in context of the game in question as well as (failingly, apparently) a neutral assessment of it's value. I apologize for the problems this has caused.<br /> <br /> Still don't think they should come anywhere close to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T11:33:14-08:00","id":45019,"title":"","content":"You (and everyone else on this board especially) should know, one man's myth is another man's religion. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T12:26:48-08:00","id":45059,"title":"","content":"I do, which is why I had no problem referring to my religion and it's roots as mythology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T13:50:56-08:00","id":45107,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s interesting that the only posters here who complained about the use of \u201cmyth\u201d to describe Abrahamic stories and the like were not themselves offended by the term AFAICT, but rather were speaking of the offense that was taken by other people that they knew. I\u2019ve counted four different self-identified Christian posters of wildly different flavors of Christianity here who have said that they\u2019re fine using the term \u201cAbrahamic myth\u201d because they <i>don\u2019t</i> take it to be a statement refuting the truth of their beliefs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T14:08:14-08:00","id":45114,"title":"","content":"Ummm I'm not sure if I'm among those counted yet, but I guess I will go on record and say that the word &quot;Mythology&quot; doesn't really bother me when used in relation to my religious beliefs. It's a word, like any other. And as has already been pointed out, the word &quot;myth&quot; is not technically synonymous with &quot;false&quot; or &quot;untrue&quot; anyway. So, no, I can't say I'm bothered by it.<br /> <br /> I was offended by the use of the word &quot;Fundamentalist&quot; to describe the nutjob Christians who give the rest of us a bad name because I wasn't aware that capitalizing the word gives it a whole new meaning. Now that I know that, the word also doesn't bother me anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T14:17:22-08:00","id":45120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44915#post44915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are some points within the Abrahamic tradition that would need specific refuting for Scion to continue to make sense. For instance, Yahweh supposedly banished the Abrahamic equivalent of Titans from the mortal plane in exchange for a promise to keep his angels out. Which both sides have sort of broken quite a lot. So much in fact that the idea of the Fatebindings that kept the other pantheons out of the world until now falls apart in light of the shenanigans of Abraham's sons, literal and spiritual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two questions here:<br /> <br /> First, where are you getting the bit about \u201cyou are banished from the mortal plane; in exchange, I will keep my angels out\u201d? <br /> <br /> Second, what\u2019s this business about Fatebindings that have kept other Pantheons out of the world until now? No, wait; never mind. That should be addressed in another topic. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44947#post44947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on how you define the broad outlines. You can't deny the very actions that made them what they are, or how and why they became so lodged in history.</div> </div> </div> </div>The broad outlines I\u2019m thinking of are the stories of Abraham, Joseph, Moses, Joshua, David, and Solomon. They\u2019re not the only ones (e.g., I skipped Isaac and Jacob; but they\u2019re implied), but they provide the basic outline of what the early history of the Abrahamic faction should look like in the context of <b>Scion</b>, whether or not you consider them to be true in the real world. Again, mythological accuracy is what the goal should be. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T14:21:30-08:00","id":45121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=45107#post45107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s interesting that the only posters here who complained about the use of \u201cmyth\u201d to describe Abrahamic stories and the like were not themselves offended by the term AFAICT, but rather were speaking of the offense that was taken by other people that they knew. I\u2019ve counted four different self-identified Christian posters of wildly different flavors of Christianity here who have said that they\u2019re fine using the term \u201cAbrahamic myth\u201d because they <i>don\u2019t</i> take it to be a statement refuting the truth of their beliefs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. While I continue to preach that this distinction should be taken seriously because there are very serious consequences, I personally think it is unfortunate that we cannot refer to all religion as mythology because of the assumed negative connotation. I am more than happy with its use here on these forums, and wish it was once again acceptable to use everywhere. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T03:13:44-08:00","id":45473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44661#post44661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't call it mythology. Seriously, that's a big deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fine. We'll call it Bob.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T03:23:03-08:00","id":45477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44906#post44906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are many religions that hold 'loving thy neighbour' as an ideal. There are no mythologies that do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Semantics.<br /> <br /> Whether you consider Buddhism and Christian to be Religions or Mythol- I mean Bobs, compassion is a central tenant to the belief system and the stories that come of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","user":"The Revenge of TV Head","date":". 01-09-2014, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T06:22:31-08:00","id":45540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=44698#post44698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As with the dragon thing, I saw a special on either the History channel or Discovery about Dragons in general. The special said that the first instance of a dragon in Western folklore was a Sumerian tale of how (Bell?) the dragon goddess defeated an evil dragon (I forgot the name) and made the world from his body. Later on, there was a Jewish story about this one Jew who came to the Sumerians (I forget his name) and denounced the Sumerians dragon goddess saying that the dragon wasn't a god. According to the tale, he was thrown into a stadium to be eaten by lions, and by the grace of God, wasn't eaten by said lions.<br /> <br /> Am I wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to be referring to the apocryphal story of <a href=\"http://www.earlyjewishwritings.com/text/bel.html\" target=\"_blank\">Bel and the Dragon</a>, in which the &quot;dragon&quot; seems actually to have been a large mundane reptile the Babylonians viewed as the manifestation of a god, and which Daniel killed. Bel is a separate deity Daniel trys to discredit earlier in the text by proving the his image doesn't actually consume the food offering left in front of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T06:58:08-08:00","id":45552,"title":"","content":"Babylonians worshiped a Crocodile?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T08:08:33-08:00","id":45600,"title":"","content":"The account was written from the point of view of Daniel rather than of the Babylonians (and probably significantly later), so it's hard to tell what the actual beliefs behind the story may have been. The &quot;dragon&quot; isn't very thoroughly described either. It could be a crocodile or a large snake. My guess is that it might have been an animal kept in the temple of some god which it represented, similar to cult surrounding the Egyptian Apis bull. On the other hand, the whole story may have some source other than Babylonian practices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not the <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/Daimon/Alastor.html\" target=\"_blank\">daimon</a>, just a namesake.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/858-alastor","name":"Alastor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T08:10:26-08:00","id":45602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=45473#post45473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fine. We'll call it Bob.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;And I will call him George and I will love him and squeeze him and stroke his soft fur and......&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T09:19:00-08:00","id":45654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=45552#post45552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Babylonians worshiped a Crocodile?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, you dig hard enough, probably every animal on the planet has had a cult at one time or another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T09:29:31-08:00","id":45660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=45120#post45120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, where are you getting the bit about \u201cyou are banished from the mortal plane; in exchange, I will keep my angels out\u201d?</div> </div> </div> </div>The apocryphal books (which, to my constant consternation, is a gross misappellation). I'll take a look in my books this weekend and see if I can't grab you chapter and verse.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T22:47:08-08:00","id":46757,"title":"","content":"I finally looked in the Scion God book at I noticed that the whole hierarchy of angels were considered titanspawn of Aten. If they continue on with this story in the Second Edition, perhaps Aten could have created the Abrahamic religions to undermine the power of the World Pantheons of Scion, and to cover his tracks, he masquerades as a god in each pantheon to keep tabs. It'll be kind of like how Io in the Discworld series poses as a god of many religions on the Disc by using disguises.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T08:03:49-08:00","id":46907,"title":"","content":"You do realize how problematic making various belief systems into a titan's con is in a game where &quot;All myths are true&quot; is, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","user":"The Revenge of TV Head","date":". 01-11-2014, 11:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T10:51:41-08:00","id":46971,"title":"","content":"That says there's a problem with Scion God when it comes to presentation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T22:15:03-08:00","id":47256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=46757#post46757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I finally looked in the Scion God book at I noticed that the whole hierarchy of angels were considered titanspawn of Aten. If they continue on with this story in the Second Edition, perhaps Aten could have created the Abrahamic religions to undermine the power of the World Pantheons of Scion, and to cover his tracks, he masquerades as a god in each pantheon to keep tabs. It'll be kind of like how Io in the Discworld series poses as a god of many religions on the Disc by using disguises.</div> </div> </div> </div>The gods Borrowed the angel naming and hierarchy to label Aten's servants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T00:22:06-08:00","id":47280,"title":"","content":"I'm just saying that if the term is put on Aten's servants and mortals who see those servants believe so, then in First Edition, Aten might have gone under the names of God, Yahweh, and Allah in his future dealings with mortals. That would explain a lot, if they do the same thing in Second Edition. Then again, OP may surprise me and do a completely different explanation to the existence of the angels in Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T01:23:05-08:00","id":47293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=47280#post47280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just saying that if the term is put on Aten's servants and mortals who see those servants believe so, then in First Edition, Aten might have gone under the names of God, Yahweh, and Allah in his future dealings with mortals. That would explain a lot, if they do the same thing in Second Edition. Then again, OP may surprise me and do a completely different explanation to the existence of the angels in Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aten and the origins existed separately before the names were applied. So God/Yhwh/Allah already existed, at least as a concept, to mortals before Thoth decided to use the naming scheme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T08:11:24-08:00","id":47393,"title":"","content":"\u201cAten = El = Yahweh = Allah\u201d is a different flavor of the same issue as \u201call North American Coyote Tricksters are the same entity\u201d: you\u2019re trying to conflate different mythologies on the basis of a shared feature. In <b>Scion</b>, Thor didn\u2019t go under the name \u201cZeus\u201d when dealing with the Greek people (or vice versa); Thor and Zeus were separate entities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T08:14:25-08:00","id":47395,"title":"","content":"\u201cAten = El = Yahweh = Allah\u201d is the same sort of mythological conflation as saying that there\u2019s only one Coyote in North America, or that Zeus, Thor, and Raiden are different guises for the same god.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T10:41:04-08:00","id":47474,"title":"","content":"On a similar note (and forgive me if it's been mentioned I don't really feel like perusing the 20 pages thread) what about the Zoroastrian gods Ahura Mazda and Angra Mainyu? I'd love to play a Zoroastrian scion because it's probably my favorite religion from a mythology standpoint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1646-finch181","name":"finch181","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T11:03:10-08:00","id":47487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>finch181</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=47474#post47474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a similar note (and forgive me if it's been mentioned I don't really feel like perusing the 20 pages thread) what about the Zoroastrian gods Ahura Mazda and Angra Mainyu? I'd love to play a Zoroastrian scion because it's probably my favorite religion from a mythology standpoint.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both of them would probably be Titans. In fact, Ahriman is a Titan in the Yazata supplement. Ahura Mazda has, iirc, conveniently disappeared.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T11:07:33-08:00","id":47490,"title":"","content":"how unfortunate. But aren't titans evil? I don't remember because I haven't read anything about scion in ages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1646-finch181","name":"finch181","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T11:11:49-08:00","id":47492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>finch181</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=47490#post47490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how unfortunate. But aren't titans evil? I don't remember because I haven't read anything about scion in ages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Evil is an appropriate label from the perspective of Scions who don't know much about the Titans, certainly.<br /> <br /> &quot;Axiomatically opposed to the pantheons&quot; is probably a better descriptor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T11:17:35-08:00","id":47495,"title":"","content":"Umm....Zoroastrian? Sounds Persian to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T11:20:47-08:00","id":47497,"title":"","content":"It is an ancient Persian religion that apparently heavily influenced early Judaism<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=47492#post47492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Evil is an appropriate label from the perspective of Scions who don't know much about the Titans, certainly.<br /> <br /> &quot;Axiomatically opposed to the pantheons&quot; is probably a better descriptor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno Ahura Mazda is pretty much portrayed as the ultimate good and anti-evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1646-finch181","name":"finch181","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T11:40:08-08:00","id":47509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>finch181</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=47490#post47490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how unfortunate. But aren't titans evil? I don't remember because I haven't read anything about scion in ages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Scion 1e does make it look like all Titans are evil (the fact that every last one of them has all four Dark Virtues does NOT help), but I sincerely hope that 2e takes a step away from this approach. What Titans ultimately are, is powerful. They are embodiments of aspects of the fundamental building blocks of the World. All the Water Titans in the book, for eg. are evil, but the Greater Titan of Water is supposed to be the underlying principle of the element of water in the World, so it stands to reason that somewhere in there is a Titan Avatar that represents water's helpful qualities...Mizuhame, the direct counterpart to her brother Kagutsuchi, could be one.<br /> Similarly, you could play Ahura Mazda as an Avatar of an Order Titan, representing rightful Law, and give him just Zealotry (to represent his somewhat less than flexible view towards morality). Given his general nature, he might even have volunteered to be bound to Tartarus so that the rest of the more dangerous Order Titans can be contained (and honestly, 1e does paint Order as the one Titan on the side of the Gods, but that is equally as uninspired an approach as 'all other Titans are evil'. There are plenty of less savoury sides to Order as well).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T16:01:41-08:00","id":47664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>finch181</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=47497#post47497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is an ancient Persian religion that apparently heavily influenced early Judaism<br /> <br /> I dunno Ahura Mazda is pretty much portrayed as the ultimate good and anti-evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware of Zoroastrian dogma. Ahura Mazda isn't present in the setting any more likely for the very reason of his insurmountable goodness.<br /> <br /> Titans are generally axiomatically opposed to the pantheons they're engaging with, which of course means there's wiggle room for them not to be axiomatically opposed with the pantheons they're not actively combative with.<br /> <br /> 1e did a very poor job of demonstrating instances where this might be true, to the extent that they went out of their way to avoid pointing out that many pantheons rely on Titans to fulfill vital functions for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T16:03:49-08:00","id":47667,"title":"","content":"There are also Pantheons that don't have &quot;Titans&quot; like the Greeks do. The Greeks don't even really fit the game's Titan archetype because a lot of their Titans are perfectly friendly to both humanity and the Gods. Hecate &amp; Helios for example. Again, Scion is trying to force <i>all of mythology</i> into a single, cohesive cosmology and mythology doesn't work that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T16:29:02-08:00","id":47685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=47667#post47667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are also Pantheons that don't have &quot;Titans&quot; like the Greeks do. The Greeks don't even really fit the game's Titan archetype because a lot of their Titans are perfectly friendly to both humanity and the Gods. Hecate &amp; Helios for example. Again, Scion is trying to force <i>all of mythology</i> into a single, cohesive cosmology and mythology doesn't work that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would you solve that problem for 2e? All the &quot;pantheons&quot; existing in the same setting is pretty important to Scion but I'd be lying if I said all of it in one cohesive cosmology wasn't awkward and uncomfortable at best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T16:40:37-08:00","id":47693,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s only awkward and uncomfortable to the extent that it\u2019s restrictive. A few small expansions to Scion 1e\u2019s metaphysics and cosmology could <i>drastically</i> expand the amount of real-world mythology that the setting can handle. The trick is in keeping the expansions minor enough that you don\u2019t lose cohesion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T17:25:17-08:00","id":47735,"title":"","content":"I would suggest in taking things..and titans...and the &quot;evil&quot; element, on a pantheon-by-pantheon basis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T17:35:01-08:00","id":47747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=47693#post47693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s only awkward and uncomfortable to the extent that it\u2019s restrictive. A few small expansions to Scion 1e\u2019s metaphysics and cosmology could <i>drastically</i> expand the amount of real-world mythology that the setting can handle. The trick is in keeping the expansions minor enough that you don\u2019t lose cohesion.</div> </div> </div> </div>What would you propose?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T19:52:38-08:00","id":47817,"title":"","content":"At a minimum? An alternative to playing literal human/god half-breeds, so that all of the pantheons that <i>don\u2019t</i> feature promiscuous gods can still join in the fun without having to shoehorn themselves into that model. Also useful would be to ditch the \u201cTitans are EVIL!\u201d schtick; you could get a lot of mileage out of having the Titans pick from the same set of Virtues that the Gods do. <br /> <br /> Another option would be to blur the distinction between Gods and Titans: e.g., allow (but do not require) a Pantheon to have a \u201cGreater God\u201d that is analogous to a Greater Titan, which manifests godlike Avatars within the Pantheon\u2019s Godrealm. In effect, that Pantheon\u2019s \u201cGodrealm\u201d would <i>be</i> a Greater Titan. This would allow for more henotheistic models for Pantheons, with the option of a Titan-like \u201cGreater God\u201d presiding over the rest of the Pantheon. <br /> <br /> Likewise, play up Lesser Immortals as potential denizens of Godrealms, possibly with the option to achieve full-on God status; this would allow for various \u201cLittle Gods\u201d options such as kami. The main line I wouldn\u2019t cross would be the notion that Gods are somehow created by human beliefs: I\u2019d save that for a Legendary Beings \u201cShard\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T19:19:27-08:00","id":50335,"title":"","content":"I'm going to have to convert my Grigori to 2nd Edition. I'm looking forward to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1976-tashiro","name":"Tashiro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1976_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T00:18:51-08:00","id":54514,"title":"","content":"As this topic actually came up in a quasi-ST brainstorming session between Watcher, Iry, and myself, we had a sitdown for thinking how you could put monotheistic Christianity into Scion RAW.<br /> <br /> It could work as Yahweh being a god who splintered from the originial Caanite pantheon; (or his own entirely) but instead of taking the Israelite people into their own nation, he created them from Adam and Eve (since all Creation Myths are true) maybe created them in his own Terra Incognitae/personal sanctum. Bible actually happens. Adam and Eve break His own laws and are kicked out into the real world, have their own children, yadda yadda.<br /> <br /> Since Yahweh formed his own new pantheon, he makes a new PSP and this PSP allows him to adopt (or even a new power/relic, or a condition worked into the mix when he created Adam and Eve) but either way, he can take anyone born of Adam's lineage into a Scion which would explain Saints; and Jesus himself is an actual born Scion through Divine intervention and sacrificing himself did something (maybe banishing away the Titanic stain that happened when Adam and Eve got cast out of Yahweh's paradise)<br /> <br /> Because Angels are not humans, and they're not Gods; they're Legendary Creatures (Legendary Beings) with their own ranking hierarchies and whatnot. They themselves cannot sire Scions, but they have the power to Visit scions on Yahweh's behalf (because that's also RAW scion).<br /> <br /> At least, this is a way that works for me to make both sides have their own respectful histories, mythologies, and understandings side-by-side. It is soooo not perfect, but I dunno; it's better than flat out &quot;nos&quot; like I have been doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T02:45:51-08:00","id":54551,"title":"","content":"Very mental gymnastics. So wow.<br /> <br /> But I don't think I'd want that sort of obvious hack as part of the game's canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T04:25:00-08:00","id":54596,"title":"","content":"Well, we know that the plans for 2e include allowances for non-Scions to transition from Origins-tier to Hero-tier, provided they meet appropriate criteria; so in 2e terms, the single biggest hack in Aynie\u2019s suggestion isn\u2019t much of a hack at all. <br /> <br /> Also, \u201canyone descended from Adam and Eve\u201d could easily be synonymous with \u201canyone alive\u201d by now \u2014 or not, as the Storyteller determines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T06:13:25-08:00","id":54625,"title":"","content":"Well I mean &quot;all creation myths are true&quot; so everyone would technically be descended from Adam/Eve","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><i>!</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/245-egg","name":"Egg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar245_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-21T09:43:25-08:00","id":54729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=54596#post54596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, we know that the plans for 2e include allowances for non-Scions to transition from Origins-tier to Hero-tier, provided they meet appropriate criteria; so in 2e terms, the single biggest hack in Aynie\u2019s suggestion isn\u2019t much of a hack at all.<br /> <br /> Also, \u201canyone descended from Adam and Eve\u201d could easily be synonymous with \u201canyone alive\u201d by now \u2014 or not, as the Storyteller determines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that came up in discussion too. It depends on if all of humanity is now one race or still seperated depending on their point of origin, so to speak. As for all Creation Myths are true... not everyone would be descended from Adam and Eve. Every single &quot;we created humans from X, Y, or Z&quot; would be true so you'd have your Israelites from Adam, your Mexica from Queztacoatl stealing bones, your Navajo from the Fifth World, your Norse from Ymir's body, and so on and so forth.<br /> <br /> Or maybe that's how it was then, and by now humans have interbred and mingled beyond the point that no one Creation Myth can rule them all, so to speak. *shrug*<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T05:02:31-08:00","id":56048,"title":"","content":"If Onyx Path ever decides to do a real world religions splat book then Buddhism is obviously the best choice since we are the best at being &quot;whatever.....~&quot;, no more pages upon pages of arguing in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T13:09:34-08:00","id":56309,"title":"","content":"Buddhism seems as though it'd be one of the more difficult religions to fit into Scion, not least because it combines regional differences with local entanglement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T15:34:15-07:00","id":91141,"title":"","content":"Heres my 2 cents.<br /> In my Scion game this how I did it. I borrowed the Innomine write up on Angels and Devils and used them. In my cosmology I have God as the super powerfully God from the Judeo-Christian-Muslim. But HE/She/It is so distant from the game. God created the Titans and they created gods. God created the Angels to help the Titans run the Universe (Since Titans are embodiments of nature and concepts), while god went off to &quot;Work in mysterious ways.&quot; Man makes his appearance in world. gods are created by Titans. Angels have internal conflict (whole Lucifier fall) and can't restrain the Titans from giving there nature and wreaking the world. The gods rise up and imprison the Titans. Angels defeat rebels and cast them in their own prison (Hell) Titans get looses, devils never left. So angels and gods have to fight them.<br /> <br /> So what the God in my game represent. The GM. He ultimate authority, but is so distance that his role in daly affairs is near nill. Even his own guys the angels (who I treat just like another pantheon) are not in the loop what HE/SHE/It is up to. <br /> <br /> Of course that how I did it. My group is not very religious so they don't really care. But for any other GM, like it been said before, know you players and work with their sensibilities on the subject.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2512-cavalier1645","name":"Cavalier1645","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2512_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T22:35:21-07:00","id":92659,"title":"","content":"Ok I read until page 19 and at that point I just gave up. There are so many options on this subject why wouldn't it be a supplement? It makes perfect sense from a marketing standpoint which in all honesty is the final decider on what will go into print and what wont. Now lets look at what would go into core 2e: a side bar saying you could hand wave it away like 1e does or you can be a good ST and A) know your group and what they want B) do what makes the story better.<br /> As for the supplement I would say that it would be much less difficult then you all are making it. Firstly you need to appeal to multiple audiences with different possibilities on how to build a pantheon (That is like a third of the book right there) then the rest would offer examples of the several options. All the options would be simplified for modern people. I was raised roman catholic and did what I thought was a lot of research to finally settle on my view of religion but you all are really beating a dead horse. If it was me I would offer four examples, number one being don't include it fully as a pantheon. IN MY VERSION of scion I explain away Christianity with the fact that prayers to &quot;GOD&quot; can be answered by any god in the vicinity. If you specify a named god then the prayer finds its real recipient. Most people I know (and when I say this I allude to the greater majority not the minorities which is what the writers aim will be) don't ask a named god for special treatment unless they are not one of the monotheistic religions. Now on to the simplified versions. God is a single deity pantheon with a army of angels as low level gods or demi gods who enforce his will and specialize in certain previews so he can have Sundays off. Next choice, God is a titan of order who sleeps eternally so as not to distub his creation and dreams of his followers prayers. In this angels are GOD LEVEL creatures of myth, saints are demi gods, and the prophets of the one true god are scions of various legend level. In these scenarios several things can hold true. There is no evil titan, there are only the equivalents of titan spawn where Lucifer and Lilith take head positions and various demons and fallen angels underneath them. (it is also feasible that they my have scions as well since they are GOD LEVEL creatures). Finally we cover the whole scions of god or scions of angels coming to ...um... fruition for lack of a better term by creating a new stamina knack OR fertility boon called &quot;Immaculate Conception&quot; where any willing subject can receive the divine grace of carrying a scion of God (as all angels are only messengers of god carrying out his will).<br /> This is of course assuming that 2e follows 1e's set path which we all know it wont rendering this entire thread mostly conjecture and wishful thinking. By the way it was for the most part a very entertaining and informative thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Every normal man must be tempted at times to spit upon his hands, hoist the black flag, and begin slitting throats.&quot;<br /> -H.L. Mencken","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2486-irisheathen","name":"Irisheathen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2486_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T02:59:47-07:00","id":92713,"title":"","content":"For the record I have no interest in playing a Scion of the Abrahamic Faith but it is not for the same reason as others. First and foremost the game is based on earlier beliefs so we can toss out the notion that the Abrahamic Faith is a monotheistic faith, it was a Monolatry. In other words they didn't believe in just the one god, they just believe that only their one god should be worshiped as only he aided his people and therefore only he should receive their prayer. For more information on this, this is the quick and dirty of it <a href=\"http://booksnthoughts.com/ancient-jews-believed-in-the-existence-of-many-gods/\" target=\"_blank\">http://booksnthoughts.com/ancient-je...-of-many-gods/</a> since some folks don't much care to go into in depth reading for a game. <br /> <br /> The above statement and relation of information relating to an older (And fitting more closely to the era in which the other pantheons came from) version of the faith, it would not cause conflict with existing Pantheons as Yahweh's existence does not contradict their own existence nor does it identify him as hostile towards the other gods, only that he is a jealous god (And really...aren't they all?) who is equally on par as a Legend 12 god, just like the other gods.<br /> <br /> My objection to it is that without giving a huge overhaul to the Abrahamic Faith, making angles into gods and what not, you have only a singular god for which you can be the scion of and this can be very boring without having variety. <br /> <br /> The other issue is that of Aten (And the much longer name associated that I can't remember how to spell) and the fact that in every single aspect he is essentially the same being, and to introduce the Abrahamic God, is to negate a Titan and Titan Avatar of another Pantheon, and that doesn't really sit all to kosher with me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T08:38:47-07:00","id":92806,"title":"","content":"Aten's connection with the God of the Abrahamic religions is tenuous. El, Father of the Canaanite pantheon, is a much better candidate for the God of the Abrahamic religions, though he has his share of problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T09:42:28-07:00","id":92841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Creticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=92806#post92806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aten's connection with the God of the Abrahamic religions is tenuous. El, Father of the Canaanite pantheon, is a much better candidate for the God of the Abrahamic religions, though he has his share of problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>El just doesn't seem angry enough. Yaweh does things like destroy cities, counsel genocide, lay waste to nations, torture people for the fun of it, etc. El just seems to get pushed around a lot (by Yamm, by Anat, by Ba'al, even, more gently, by his wives).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T15:17:15-07:00","id":92999,"title":"","content":"Well Yahweh was originally in the Canaanite Pantheon: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yahweh_%28Canaanite_deity%29\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yahweh_...anite_deity%29</a><br /> <br /> It was until the Hebrews made a monotheistic following around him and the rest was history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1997-deathpathoes","user":"DeathPathoes","date":". 03-17-2014, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1997-deathpathoes","name":"DeathPathoes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T15:59:52-07:00","id":93026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=92841#post92841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> El just doesn't seem angry enough. Yaweh does things like destroy cities, counsel genocide, lay waste to nations, torture people for the fun of it, etc. El just seems to get pushed around a lot (by Yamm, by Anat, by Ba'al, even, more gently, by his wives).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, hence the part about his share of problems. El has his moments, but for the most part, he's more subtle than the God of the Abrahamic religions. Bit of a charmer too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T16:22:01-07:00","id":93048,"title":"","content":"Hmmm...Some of those old religions absolutely had to loathe certain religions. The Nabataeans (ancient Arabians) were forcefully converted to Judaism by the well-hated Alexander Jannaeus who was hated even by other Jews....hmm...thinking...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T16:22:06-07:00","id":93049,"title":"","content":"As, &quot;I give in to everyone around me&quot; kinda charm? Yamm scares him into doing what he/it wants. Ba'al just presumes away his authority and does what he wants. Anat actually beats him up until he gives in. Asherah and Astarte charm him, not the other way around. El seems to sit in his tent and want to be left alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T17:30:13-07:00","id":93090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=93049#post93049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As, &quot;I give in to everyone around me&quot; kinda charm? Yamm scares him into doing what he/it wants. Ba'al just presumes away his authority and does what he wants. Anat actually beats him up until he gives in. Asherah and Astarte charm him, not the other way around. El seems to sit in his tent and want to be left alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, I was thinking more of how El wooed Asherah and Rahmay rather than the Baal Cycle. However, I recall El naming Yam his favorite and then using him to fight Baal in the next breath. Furthermore, El remains the one who bestows kingship throughout the Baal Cycle, so much so that Mot surrenders because Shapash threatens him with El's censure. Sure, El loses his kingship to Baal in the Baal Cycle, but he's faring a lot better than most of his counterparts.<br /> <br /> That said, please feel encouraged to correct me if I'm mistaken, since I don't have access to a copy of the Baal Cycle at the moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T19:19:43-07:00","id":93140,"title":"","content":"Hmmm.... I'm looking over my copy of the Cycle. Looks like it could be a translation/matter of perspective thing. Spin, even. <br /> <br /> Outside the cycle, it seems so low key, but it looks like Asherah and Rahmay seduce El rather than the other way around. <br /> <br /> Yamm is pretty much a monster (a sea monster) that extorted the kingship from El. He definitely reads as a Titan. (Though there is one weird reference that might indicate Yamm is supposed to be Yahweh. Which might explain why El is so scared of him.)<br /> <br /> Ba'al pretty much just self-declares and El panics because he is scared of Yamm. <br /> <br /> Then, after Yamm bites it, El is being pissy because Ba'al undermined him so he won't give the kingship to Ba'al (e.g. giving him permission to build a palace, which is apparently THE big deal). Astarte/Aserah can't woo him out of it. Then Anat comes and beats the crap out of him until he capitulates. That part is pretty definite and not subject to spin. He is so afraid of Anat that he sends out his flying monkey posse of gods and demons to keep her away (who all, of course, die, this is Anat after all). It almost seems like he's secretly happy that Mot is coming for Ba'al as a consequence. <br /> <br /> That's why I think of El as being something of a pushover. <br /> <br /> All that aside, Canaanite mythology is fricking awesome, which is the reason I don't like brushing it all aside to try to construct something from the post-hinotheist, post-monolatrist, fully monotheistic Judeo-Christian mythology and shoehorn into the pantheistic architecture of Scion's rules. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T19:40:39-07:00","id":93150,"title":"","content":"Couple of those deities practiced child sacrifice. It's fascinating, but lets get real. I mean, a lot of people frown down at the Aztecs...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T20:33:15-07:00","id":93179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=93140#post93140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All that aside, Canaanite mythology is fricking awesome, which is the reason I don't like brushing it all aside to try to construct something from the post-hinotheist, post-monolatrist, fully monotheistic Judeo-Christian mythology and shoehorn into the pantheistic architecture of Scion's rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks like I'm going to have to pick up a copy of the Baal Cycle before I can continue this argument. That said, I'm in agreement that I'd rather see a Canaanite pantheon than something chopped up to accommodate the Abrahamic religions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=93150#post93150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couple of those deities practiced child sacrifice. It's fascinating, but lets get real. I mean, a lot of people frown down at the Aztecs...</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the cultures in Scions performed human sacrifice at one point or another.<br /> <br /> Livius recorded a rare incidence of Roman human sacrifice in the Punic Wars, though a number of Roman practices are kind of suspicious in that regard. We know that the Germans practiced human sacrifice, while there is evidence that at least some of the Celts had rituals involving the same. Retainer sacrifice seems to have been practiced in both Egypt and Mesopotamia, while similar practices had to be banned in <i>Ming</i> China. Furthermore, there are famous Chinese stories about human sacrifices made to river deities, while the Japanese used human pillars as late as the Sengoku period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T05:36:08-07:00","id":93402,"title":"","content":"I think most have worked around the occasional human sacrifice that involved other deities. (Otherwise...Aztecs...come on. We've worked past that idea long ago)<br /> But the literal thousands of children that were murdered? I recall reading that Moloch's foul worship involved little ones from newborn to the age of six. Now I can see that many accusations were from rival/enemy tribes or city-states and this can be easily seen as propaganda, but it so obviously wasn't just propaganda. We know what a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tophet\" target=\"_blank\">Tophet</a> is. *shrugs* If this is what some people want in their game, well...Which side is the bad guy on again?<br /> I've read JSR's article for Moloch and the sample character. If there's a titanspawn in the fray, I would be skeptical that it was the &quot;bad guy.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T06:40:12-07:00","id":93443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If this is what some people want in their game, well...Which side is the bad guy on again? </div> </div> </div> That would be the side with the people who want to take the whole World and turn it into a flaming wasteland...or an endless ocean with no shore or sky...or a featureless desert...or a gibbering senseless thing that has no definition. You know, the guys for whom the extinction of all of humanity and/or human life as we know it would be a mere footnote, a side-effect of their grand scheme to flood the Universe with the overwhelming essence of their native elements. You know, the guys so bad that all the child-sacrificers, serial-rapists, mass-murderers and general all-around assholes that we all know and love as the Gods are terrified of them and are doing everything in their power to stop them. Those guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T06:42:47-07:00","id":93446,"title":"","content":"Pardon the poor formatting. My net has slowed to a crawl and my browser seems unable to handle the rich text editor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T07:06:13-07:00","id":93466,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=93443#post93443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That would be the side with the people who want to take the whole World and turn it into a flaming wasteland...or an endless ocean with no shore or sky...or a featureless desert...or a gibbering senseless thing that has no definition. You know, the guys for whom the extinction of all of humanity and/or human life as we know it would be a mere footnote, a side-effect of their grand scheme to flood the Universe with the overwhelming essence of their native elements. You know, the guys so bad that all the child-sacrificers, serial-rapists, mass-murderers and general all-around assholes that we all know and love as the Gods are terrified of them and are doing everything in their power to stop them. Those guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>O...well, that puts some of the Titans on the side of the white hats. Because my scion of Hecate (what with the whole guardian of childbirth thing) isn't going to tolerate a scion of Moloch for long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T07:16:47-07:00","id":93477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=93402#post93402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think most have worked around the occasional human sacrifice that involved other deities. (Otherwise...Aztecs...come on. We've worked past that idea long ago)<br /> But the literal thousands of children that were murdered? I recall reading that Moloch's foul worship involved little ones from newborn to the age of six. Now I can see that many accusations were from rival/enemy tribes or city-states and this can be easily seen as propaganda, but it so obviously wasn't just propaganda. We know what a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tophet\" target=\"_blank\">Tophet</a> is. *shrugs* If this is what some people want in their game, well...Which side is the bad guy on again?<br /> I've read JSR's article for Moloch and the sample character. If there's a titanspawn in the fray, I would be skeptical that it was the &quot;bad guy.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=93443#post93443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That would be the side with the people who want to take the whole World and turn it into a flaming wasteland...or an endless ocean with no shore or sky...or a featureless desert...or a gibbering senseless thing that has no definition. You know, the guys for whom the extinction of all of humanity and/or human life as we know it would be a mere footnote, a side-effect of their grand scheme to flood the Universe with the overwhelming essence of their native elements. You know, the guys so bad that all the child-sacrificers, serial-rapists, mass-murderers and general all-around assholes that we all know and love as the Gods are terrified of them and are doing everything in their power to stop them. Those guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I'm hoping that 2nd Edition will present the Titans with more nuance than 1st Edition's omni-cidal kill-bots. Some of the Titans should be cosmos-ending monstrosities with whom there can be no compromise, but others shouldn't be any worse than the pantheons.<br /> <br /> In main, I'm somewhat uncomfortable with the fact that 1st Edition focused so much on re-fighting the Titanomachia. It squeezes out room for questioning the gods, calling them to account, and even overthrowing them. As it stands, however, scrutinizing the gods while the Titans are loose is comparable to screaming about high taxation while there are literal cannibal rape hordes about to smash through the gates. You can either buy into the system of the gods, or you are a horrible monster out to kill everyone and everything that you've ever loved.<br /> <br /> Sure, you can stand aside and refuse to fight for either the gods or the Titans, but considering how much the threat of the Titans has been played up, that's pretty much handing the win to the Titans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T09:05:40-07:00","id":93512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=93150#post93150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couple of those deities practiced child sacrifice. It's fascinating, but lets get real. I mean, a lot of people frown down at the Aztecs...</div> </div> </div> </div>So did Yahweh. Oh wait! No that was a joke! Haha! What a funny guy! Almost as much fun as that bet about Job!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T09:27:02-07:00","id":93526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Creticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=93179#post93179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most of the cultures in Scions performed human sacrifice at one point or another.<br /> <br /> Livius recorded a rare incidence of Roman human sacrifice in the Punic Wars, though a number of Roman practices are kind of suspicious in that regard. We know that the Germans practiced human sacrifice, while there is evidence that at least some of the Celts had rituals involving the same. Retainer sacrifice seems to have been practiced in both Egypt and Mesopotamia, while similar practices had to be banned in <i>Ming</i> China. Furthermore, there are famous Chinese stories about human sacrifices made to river deities, while the Japanese used human pillars as late as the Sengoku period.</div> </div> </div> </div>We know the Romans did. And a lot of their sacrifices would definitely count as children by our lights. Greeks too. That's what they were doing to Oedipus that got his feet so swollen. Celts did the sacrifice thing a lot. Caesar dwelt on it, but he was justifying himself before an audience that thought he was exceeding his authority in a naked power/resource grab. Lots of archaeological evidence. Norse - blood eagles and gibbet trees. Aztecs sacrificed children too. Xipe Totec's fav. Egypt we know that retainer sacrifice was cool. Cannibalism was the no-no. It faded over time. Mesopotamia, retainer sacrifice big time, in the high double and low triple digits. (Including the poor girl who was late to the sacrifice and didn't have time to get her hair ready, so the ribbons and ornaments were still balled up in her pouch). China, agreed. How about sati? That's still going on in India and not getting seriously punished if you can make it look coincidental. So the Deva are culpable. Inca sacrifice was braining kids and leaving them to freeze to death too stunned to move. Some of the tribes worshiping the Orisha practice exposure. Sometimes a times of low resources but sometimes for specific children. Like always killing one twin (the bad one of course). <br /> <br /> I don't give Moloch a pass. In fact, I think the scholarship is good that there was never a god Moloch. It was more of a way of sacrificing - consumption by fire of a human sacrifice. But whether you hold to that or not, those child sacrifices were going to some god or gods in the Canaanite pantheon. There is pretty damning archaeological evidence all the way to Carthage and I don't remember seeing the Romans being upset about a god names Moloch or even the practice of child sacrifice. I could have missed it. Roman rhetoric was thoroughly anti-Carthage. <br /> <br /> But back to Abrahamic mythology... <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T09:39:52-07:00","id":93537,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Creticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=93477#post93477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, I'm hoping that 2nd Edition will present the Titans with more nuance than 1st Edition's omni-cidal kill-bots. Some of the Titans should be cosmos-ending monstrosities with whom there can be no compromise, but others shouldn't be any worse than the pantheons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree there.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Creticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=93477#post93477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In main, I'm somewhat uncomfortable with the fact that 1st Edition focused so much on re-fighting the Titanomachia. It squeezes out room for questioning the gods, calling them to account, and even overthrowing them.</div> </div> </div> </div>k...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Creticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=93477#post93477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As it stands, however, scrutinizing the gods while the Titans are loose is comparable to screaming about high taxation while there are literal cannibal rape hordes about to smash through the gates.</div> </div> </div> </div>But if your god is about eating babies, especially <i>your scion's</i> baby, one can easily see a defection to Titan Mother Earth.<br /> <br /> Some gods are monsters. Certain titans? Just the opposite. And that's how I would present <b>my</b> game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T09:48:38-07:00","id":93541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=93537#post93537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if your god is about eating babies, especially <i>your scion's</i> baby, one can easily see a defection to Titan Mother Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the 1st Edition Titans are set on either killing all humans or reshaping the cosmos into something so hostile to human interests that current civilization cannot survive. Switching teams because some of the gods are horrible, horrible people is akin to cutting off your nose to spite your face.<br /> <br /> Regardless, I'll drop it here since it's off-topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T10:29:57-07:00","id":93569,"title":"","content":"*shrugs* Ragnarok we could have Fenris redeemed, and Odin a major villain. (and I admit I favored Fenris as an ancient deity in his own right anyway that was demonized by the Aesir later)<br /> <br /> But, yeah, I'm reading too much of JSR's stuff and using that to create deity level villains. So...off-topic it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T12:19:59-07:00","id":93688,"title":"","content":"Just an FYI, when your referring to Titans as &quot;The Good Guys&quot; for the most part your making a mistake. A Titan is not his Avatars, his Avatars are only a piece of his soul such as Prometheus. He is not a Titan, just an Avatar of a Titan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T12:46:00-07:00","id":93719,"title":"","content":"IMO, one more thing that needs to be changed.<br /> <br /> At the moment, Titan can refer to a Titan-realm, an Avatar of a Titan-realm, or even one of the Titanes and Titanides, each of whom may or may not be an Avatar of a Titan-realm. It's an useful term, but it still reminds me of the Malfeas/Malfean problem back in Exalted 1st Edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T16:45:07-07:00","id":93915,"title":"","content":"Hmm..looks like my post got eaten...try again...I just look at the supposed &quot;bad guys in a pantheon and see if they are the villains that they're supposed to be, or simply demonized to support the pantheon's takeover and structured order. Then I look over the pantheon and see if they're are truly the paragons of good or just as bad if not worse than their predecessors. I try to qualify this all by looking at the timeframe and try to view what was &quot;acceptable&quot; then as to what we see as acceptable today. It's like trying to figure out whether slavery is better than death in some cases. Or to tie this in the thread topic...Abram was ordered to slay his firstborn. And despite protesting he was going to do just that. Today, if a scion was ordered to do the same, I suppose it would depend on the scion and the deity involved, but...I think we can all see where this would lead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T17:44:08-07:00","id":93954,"title":"","content":"How will it end? It's going to hinge on the Virtues. If the Scion has Conviction or Duty (or possibly Piety or Order) and resists and the deity is persistent, I guess there's a dead child on the altar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T18:08:46-07:00","id":93972,"title":"","content":"Hmm...In my game when obedience isn't a virtue, defiance is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T20:09:49-07:00","id":94041,"title":"","content":"Generally there's no God, anywhere, ever, who likes it when mortals get uppity with them. They're all pretty big on being obeyed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T20:49:25-07:00","id":94057,"title":"","content":"A scion isn't exactly mortal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T22:37:27-07:00","id":94110,"title":"","content":"They pretty much are till they hit Godhood. Being uppity at the Gods rarely ends well. Look what happened to Heracles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-18T23:39:31-07:00","id":94143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=94110#post94110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They pretty much are till they hit Godhood. Being uppity at the Gods rarely ends well. Look what happened to Heracles.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Odysseus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T05:42:42-07:00","id":94217,"title":"","content":"And neither are considered for any fight against titans.<br /> <br /> To clarify; <i>&quot;You're worthless to me if you aren't on your feet looking me in the eye. On your knees with your face to the ground is the position of the defeated, and I won't have that in my son! Go out there and remind them who you are and make me proud!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> If the gods want a child's obedience then that's what they'll receive. Heracles in 1e (as well as those others) seems a bit justified to me.<br /> Or maybe they should want a soldier prepped for the burdens of responsibility. (Blind obedience has never been a virtue in our nice little real world. I don't believe It should ever be seen as one in a virtual world either)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","user":"Shadowflame","date":".  I just need more coffee. I'll be fine. 03-19-2014, 09:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T08:21:04-07:00","id":94268,"title":"","content":"That God needs that kid dead, he will ask. Assuming we are in a situation where there are Virtues in play. The Scion will defy (spend WP or fail roll). He will either end up dead or worse, he will prevail or he will be asked again. If he is asked again, same thing. Only less WP. And there are some WP depleting powers. How about a Scathing Retort when the uppity liitle duffer is giving his big defiant speech? Then ordering him to do it again. If Virtues are in play, the Scion will do it eventually. If they aren't I guess it's POSSIBLE that the Scion will prevail... BUT I think &quot;prevail&quot; against the ego of a full God is unlikely. Myths are full of those who try. They don't end with &quot;and the God, his/her parent, said, &quot;Whoops! I was being a total dick! Thanks for standing up to me and setting my right, oh my son/daughter! Whatever have I done without you since I created the world, sitting on my shoulder like Jiminy Cricket to be my conscience.&quot;<br /> <br /> Not incidentally that includes pretty much ALL the myths this thread is supposed to be about. Think Job (admittedly not a Scion, but, hey, Yahweh didn't treat his one Scion much better there at the end). He starts to complain and then he gets a big speech about how he didn't create the world, fight dragons, etc. and told to shut up and suffer in silence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T09:25:05-07:00","id":94295,"title":"","content":"Hmm...Job was the most upright dude on the world but the devil didn't think he'd be so decent a person if he didn't have it so good. Apparently God doesn't like a smug devil so..he decides to test Job's faith by getting rid of his happy life, killing his children, taking away his herds, covering him with sores...which leads Job to say some of the most bitter damning statements in the Bible against God. And apparently it was a bit too much because God comes down to make his case personally to Job, of which can be boiled down to; &quot;I've a big fist so shut it.&quot; Of which Job then says &quot;Fear of the Lord, that is wisdom.&quot; (Job 28:28) A mollified God then gives him ten more children, more animals for his herds, and 140 more years of life.<br /> <br /> Not certain if this is applicable to the ideas being thrown in this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T09:42:57-07:00","id":94308,"title":"","content":"Citing an example from the primary source text about which we are discussing to support a point? Can we use the Iliad or the Homeric hymns to talk about Greek myths? The Popul Vuh to talk about Mayan religion? The Tain to talk about Irish myths? <br /> <br /> I really don't like being told that I am not legitimately discussing the topic of the thread, especially as I have been working pretty hard to bend the topic back to the core issues from an aside.<br /> <br /> Why is my viewpoint that the best way to handle the Abrahamite religion question in Scion is to look past it to polytheistic material that it heavily utilized is not a valid idea to throw around in this thread?<br /> <br /> If Yahweh treats a mere mortal (perhaps Legendary Mortal) follower that way, how is he going to treat a disobedient child? Wasn't that what we were talking about? Did I get lost in the conversation somewhere? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T10:39:50-07:00","id":94329,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=94308#post94308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't like being told that I am not legitimately discussing the topic of the thread, especially as I have been working pretty hard to bend the topic back to the core issues from an aside.</div> </div> </div> </div>And someone told you this?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=94308#post94308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Yahweh treats a mere mortal (perhaps Legendary Mortal) follower that way, how is he going to treat a disobedient child?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm...killing his children and taking away everything in his life may be the thing to do back then, but I would think that such beliefs have evolved. Were he to treat a scion like this (or worse) I would wonder how dysfunctional (and likely destructive) this relationship really is. Job spent like 28 chapters on vilifying God. Just because God told him to shut up or else, and then he spends the rest of that book singing praises about him sounds altogether rather insincere. If Job were a scion in todays society, he'd be looking for another pantheon to join. And failing that...Hello Titans!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T10:56:42-07:00","id":94335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And failing that...Hello Titans! </div> </div> </div> At which point his entire Pantheon will murder him. Most (by which I mean all) Pantheons would prefer a dead Scion over one on the side of the Titans. And if they don't manage to murder him, he can happily sit back and watch all of existence die when his Patron Greater Titan makes the World inhospitable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T12:43:09-07:00","id":94391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=94335#post94335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> At which point his entire Pantheon will murder him. Most (by which I mean all) Pantheons would prefer a dead Scion over one on the side of the Titans. And if they don't manage to murder him, he can happily sit back and watch all of existence die when his Patron Greater Titan makes the World inhospitable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but you push someone far enough, that's just exactly what they'll be happy to see. If the choices are to live in a world where that kind cruelty is to be accepted from the individuals who are supposed to be the &quot;Good Guys&quot;, than perhaps the world is just better off having the reset button hit on it. After all, they may be part god but Scions still have a mortal mind, a fragile fragile mortal mind that is easily broken by even normal mundane life, yet alone by abuse you KNOW is being heaped upon you by a being you are certain that you cannot defeat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T14:02:31-07:00","id":94450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=93466#post93466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> O...well, that puts some of the Titans on the side of the white hats. Because my scion of Hecate (what with the whole guardian of childbirth thing) isn't going to tolerate a scion of Moloch for long.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Not all the Titans are good or bad. The greater Titans in my game are just embodiment of concepts and ideas. Their 100% devoted to them to the detriment of everything else. Thats why their in the &quot;bad guy&quot; camp. Most Titans don't have a concept of human like feelings and those that do, seldom care about the mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2512-cavalier1645","name":"Cavalier1645","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2512_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T14:04:37-07:00","id":94453,"title":"","content":"We obviously have a different view of how to play this game. That's fine. The &quot;Hero&quot; in the name doesn't necessarily mean &quot;good guy&quot; to me. It means what it meant to the Greeks who coined it. <br /> <br /> I don't want to reject out of hand pantheons that have beliefs radically different to those held up as &quot;good&quot; in our current society. I will take the baby-sacrificing Canaanite gods on their terms, the Mesopotamian gods who perpetrate genocide for the pettiest of reasons on theirs, the homicidally jealous and petty Greek gods on theirs. If I'm talking Abrahamic, I'll even take the Old Testament guy on his terms, which are not very nice ones.<br /> <br /> At the same time, I don't buy into the Titan War very much at all. I have run games where the Aztec gods were the vanguard of the bad guys and there were no Titans at all. I've run them where it was exactly &quot;Wake up kid! I'm your deadbeat dad! I know your life was miserable, but it's going to get worse. You're going to war, son!&quot; I've split the difference and made their Titans into gods and chopped up the different ways they use that word for so many different things (like Avatar) to create different echelons of being/creation/etc.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, the only time I've used the Abrahamic stuff explicitly, it was with Yaweh as a the primary Avatar of the Greater Titan of Truth. Not subjective truth, but Absolute Truth, which is a very scary thing. His minions started out as the bad guys, but as things progressed they met other minions of other Greater Titans and found out that what they thought was simple, wasn't. Some of the gods were bad guys. Some of the Titan (Avatars) were good guys. It was a complicated, messed up world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T12:31:23-07:00","id":95854,"title":"","content":"One interesting idea is to do it like the WitchCraft RPG. The Gods and Angels were both created by a Supreme Being. The Gods are the ones that stuck around Earth and helped humans while the angels spent time carrying God's messages and eventually fighting a huge civil war. So this lets the Gods have their thematic space and the angels have their space too. So I guess you have Nephilim running around that are more like cousins to Scions, and the Angels and Gods are related but not the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T14:40:24-07:00","id":97760,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth - not saying this is the &quot;best&quot; way, or saying it should be in the core book, but here's how I plan to handle it if I can ever get a Scion game running: <br /> <br /> Aten really is the Judeo-Christian God. No coy flirting with the idea. In the book, Aten was really, really blatantly meant to be the Judeo-Christian God, so just come right out and embrace it. <br /> <br /> The thing is, you don't really need to tweak the idea very much to actually resolve a lot of the problems discussed in this thread! Aten actually canonically *is* an over-god more powerful than all the other gods. Aten actually *is* canonically the first being in existence in the game universe. Aten arguably *did* make Creation, with all other Titans (and then gods) following after his Light at the dawn of time. <br /> <br /> Aten is also an antagonist to the player characters. But... well, wouldn't the Judeo-Christian God be expected to be an antagonist to a bunch of pagan deities? Just because he's an antagonist doesn't mean he's evil. Not all Titans are evil, so you could play it however you want. My personal preference would be to play Aten as a full, to the hilt, fire and brimstone Old Testament God, but that's just my game. <br /> <br /> I think the only thing I'd be likely to change is that in my campaign, Aten was never cast down in the Titanomachy.<br /> <br /> Although if you want to throw in a bit of Milton, I rather like the idea that some of his Titanspawn actually *did* break free once upon a time, same as with the other Titans and Pantheons. In this case, though, it was Aten who won and cast that Pantheon down into the underworld. Now we know them as Lucifer and the fallen angels, and when the other Titans smashed their way out of the underworld, guess who else got loose?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2076-mrapophenia","name":"MrApophenia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T07:44:51-07:00","id":98341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrApophenia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=97760#post97760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth - not saying this is the &quot;best&quot; way, or saying it should be in the core book, but here's how I plan to handle it if I can ever get a Scion game running:<br /> <br /> Aten really is the Judeo-Christian God. No coy flirting with the idea. In the book, Aten was really, really blatantly meant to be the Judeo-Christian God, so just come right out and embrace it.<br /> <br /> The thing is, you don't really need to tweak the idea very much to actually resolve a lot of the problems discussed in this thread! Aten actually canonically *is* an over-god more powerful than all the other gods. Aten actually *is* canonically the first being in existence in the game universe. Aten arguably *did* make Creation, with all other Titans (and then gods) following after his Light at the dawn of time.<br /> <br /> Aten is also an antagonist to the player characters. But... well, wouldn't the Judeo-Christian God be expected to be an antagonist to a bunch of pagan deities? Just because he's an antagonist doesn't mean he's evil. Not all Titans are evil, so you could play it however you want. My personal preference would be to play Aten as a full, to the hilt, fire and brimstone Old Testament God, but that's just my game.<br /> <br /> I think the only thing I'd be likely to change is that in my campaign, Aten was never cast down in the Titanomachy.<br /> <br /> Although if you want to throw in a bit of Milton, I rather like the idea that some of his Titanspawn actually *did* break free once upon a time, same as with the other Titans and Pantheons. In this case, though, it was Aten who won and cast that Pantheon down into the underworld. Now we know them as Lucifer and the fallen angels, and when the other Titans smashed their way out of the underworld, guess who else got loose?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ya know.....of all of the ideas mentioned I can't say I hate this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T10:41:20-07:00","id":100792,"title":"","content":"And now we're back on the subject of Good Titans, which a good amount of people would believe considering the current religious landscape of Christianity, Judaism, and Islam. Hell, after reading the Titan Avatars in the God book of 1e, the only avatar that, seemed to me, filled the role of &quot;white-hat&quot; the best was Prometheous, though his plans seem to be half-assed at times. Aten, in 1e, was a total dick who believed completely in his monotheistic dogma. To make him a &quot;Good Titan&quot; would mean that he'll have to get a total psychological redo on his personality. The reason why I had my two cents on this thread was that I was concerned that the Scions weren't harassed (to the point of bodily harm) by the &quot;God hates fags&quot; minority of Christians and the &quot;Preach with the sword&quot; mentality that some Muslims have, just like they do in our real world. To me, Scion is a what if scenario where the gods of old still existed. Not having that very visual and vocal part of our world makes me break the immersiveness that I would expect in a Scion game. <br /> <br /> Throughout this thead, two solutions came out that I do approve:<br /> <br /> 1. A Canaanite pantheon that includes Yahweh. Adding the henotheistic side of ancient religions will give more diversity, plus it would explain the omnipresence of our current religions and the opinions on that.<br /> <br /> 2. Good Titans. This was hinted before as a possible character creation point with the incluison of Chronos and Nyx as divine parents. I think this is because we now realize that the Titans were really the pantheon that precluded the Olympians and that the Theol pantheon just is a result of a couple of timely coups (Chronos pulling a coup on Uranus, then Zeus pulling a coup on Chronos, which then, would allegedly result of Athena pulling a coup on Zeus (if the prophecy was correct), and so on. Because of the Angels minions, and with a little tweaking, Aten could be a Good Titan which orchestrated the Abrahamic Three.<br /> <br /> Hopefully when the game finally ships, then we can see where Christianity, Judaism, and Islam fall in the Scion universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T13:38:44-07:00","id":100854,"title":"","content":"The prophecy said &quot;son&quot; so Athena and her daddy are all good. Now if Metis is raising Athena's twin brother in Zeus's head, he might have a problem.<br /> <br /> Yahweh is tricky to insert into the Canaanite pantheon. Since he conflated with El so much, you can use it as an alias of El. But El definitely gave up the mantle of king. A bunch of times, but lastly to Ba'al. So he's not going to be the big kahuna unless you want to postulate a post-myth shift in power. Which they did for the Celestial Bureaucracy, so maybe not out of line. <br /> <br /> Also, there is some VERY recent archaeology to back this up. Yahweh is depicted as being alongside but subservient to Ba'al in a wall painting with a Hebrew inscription in a Jewish fort in the Sinai from 9th century BC. (Which is AFTER the time it became a big no no to depict Yahweh in any way. Bad travelers! Bad!). BTW, Asherah is playing harp in the background. So you can just go with that and manufacture a story where Yahweh does to Ba'al what Ba'al sorta did to El, Yamm and Mot. (And Zeus did to Chronos who did it to Ouranous, what Tarhun did to his pa, etc.)<br /> <br /> I just go with it and have had Yahweh give up the &quot;being part of the pantheon&quot; for ULTIMATE COSMIC POWER and become the Primary Avatar of a Greater Titan. In my case the Titan of Truth (associated with the Justice Purview). Good Titan is a relative word to me. Yahweh hasn't come across as good. Other aspects of Truth have had more traction, though, like Ma'at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T21:16:14-07:00","id":101060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=100792#post100792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aten, in 1e, was a total dick who believed completely in his monotheistic dogma. To make him a &quot;Good Titan&quot; would mean that he'll have to get a total psychological redo on his personality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. But then, I figure how to handle the character - good or evil, antagonist or not - is best left to the individual GM and their judgement of what their players are up for. Personally, and for the purposes of my own hypothetical game if I ever get to run it, I'd plan to leave Aten entirely as written in 1E. He's a fairly decent representation of the God of the Old Testament, and when you get right down to it, the White Wolf writers essentially wrote a campaign where the End Boss is the Judeo-Christian-Islamic God. Which my group would totally eat up, but I can see how that maybe wouldn't play so well at every table. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2076-mrapophenia","name":"MrApophenia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T09:57:10-07:00","id":116557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrApophenia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=101060#post101060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the White Wolf writers essentially wrote a campaign where the End Boss is the Judeo-Christian-Islamic God. Which my group would totally eat up, but I can see how that maybe wouldn't play so well at every table.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're talking about a game where ancient myths are like the good guys and the titans the bad guys. While I disagree with inserting Aten in the Titan category, Abrahamic religion replaced the ancient Gods. So, a game where ancient Gods are the good guys, it's only obvious to make the one God their issues. Titans and Gods should fight against the one God before trying to &quot;kill&quot; each other...<br /> If one's belief is too strong to accept a game like that, then one should not play. It's like any other games that might deal with any kind of discrimination. You only play when you feel comfortable.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T10:04:11-07:00","id":116562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=116557#post116557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abrahamic religion replaced the ancient Gods. So, a game where ancient Gods are the good guys, it's only obvious to make the one God their issues. Titans and Gods should fight against the one God before trying to &quot;kill&quot; each other...</div> </div> </div> </div>This brings up a slight problem: It will lead to a clear divide between Pantheons like the Tuatha and Dodekatheon who have been affected by the Abrahamic God and those like the Deva, Kami and Shen that could not care less. What would the latter be doing in this cosmology?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T10:12:35-07:00","id":116565,"title":"","content":"I don't think they could care less. Because Chinese people start becoming Christians which surely happen in the other two religions. So, they would just fight against Aten not to be forgotten as the other pantheons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T10:52:32-07:00","id":116579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=116565#post116565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think they could care less. Because Chinese people start becoming Christians which surely happen in the other two religions. So, they would just fight against Aten not to be forgotten as the other pantheons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not making any kind of statement about whether or not Christians are good or bad. But they have made many attempts to establish a presence in eastern cultures, and predominantly failed. I agree with Samudra. Most eastern religions do not care any more than they would care about any other Pantheon attempting to encroach on their territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T11:12:33-07:00","id":116592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=116565#post116565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think they could care less. Because Chinese people start becoming Christians which surely happen in the other two religions. So, they would just fight against Aten not to be forgotten as the other pantheons.</div> </div> </div> </div>In between the Boxer Rebellion and Tokugawa Shogunate, the Shen and Kami probably aren't too worried, and even after nearly two centuries of colonization India has a less than 3 % Christian population, so I don't think the Deva are losing any sleep over it either.<br /> <br /> There is also the matter of traditional arrogance that the Big Three of Asia have towards foreigners in general. The whole 'Barbarians Gaijin Firangi' thing. They most likely believe the Abrahamic God to be a fairly unimportant individual compared to the shining glory of Amaterasu or the divine presence of the Jade Emperor or the all encompassing majesty of the Trimurti. Suffice to say these three Pantheons have fairly healthy egos.<br /> <br /> You could rule that in their arrogance they don't even notice until the Abrahamic God turns up and takes over their domains, but short of that actually happening they will consider Him a minor nuisance at best them, no matter how nice they are about it.<br /> <br /> Also, am I the only one who finds the date of the resurrection of this thread a striking coincidence? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 04-20-2014, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T14:47:03-07:00","id":116687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=116592#post116592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could rule that in their arrogance they don't even notice until the Abrahamic God turns up and takes over their domains, but short of that actually happening they will consider Him a minor nuisance at best them, no matter how nice they are about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=116592#post116592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, am I the only one who finds the date of the resurrection of this thread a striking coincidence? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Haha, it wasn't on purpose. I just thought about it when I read what 2e will be about.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T11:54:11-07:00","id":121888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=116579#post116579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not making any kind of statement about whether or not Christians are good or bad. But they have made many attempts to establish a presence in eastern cultures, and predominantly <b>failed</b>. I agree with Samudra. Most eastern religions do not care any more than they would care about any other Pantheon attempting to encroach on their territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Philippines is the third largest Catholic countries in the world so those Christian don't fail so bad IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T17:45:55-07:00","id":124158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=116592#post116592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In between the Boxer Rebellion and Tokugawa Shogunate, the Shen and Kami probably aren't too worried, and even after nearly two centuries of colonization India has a less than 3 % Christian population, so I don't think the Deva are losing any sleep over it either.<br /> <br /> There is also the matter of traditional arrogance that the Big Three of Asia have towards foreigners in general. The whole 'Barbarians Gaijin Firangi' thing. They most likely believe the Abrahamic God to be a fairly unimportant individual compared to the shining glory of Amaterasu or the divine presence of the Jade Emperor or the all encompassing majesty of the Trimurti. Suffice to say these three Pantheons have fairly healthy egos.<br /> <br /> You could rule that in their arrogance they don't even notice until the Abrahamic God turns up and takes over their domains, but short of that actually happening they will consider Him a minor nuisance at best them, no matter how nice they are about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Christianity is even less than 3% of India's total population, though it is the overwhelming majority in some states (Nagaland is about 90% Christian, and Mizoram is about 86%). Nonetheless, you are forgetting about a much bigger, more important group here: Islam. The Delhi Sultanate was established in 1206, and for centuries onward Muslims ruled much of the Indian subcontinent. At their height, the Mughals controlled almost all of India except a few Hindu kingdoms in the far south, as well as most of modern day Bangladesh, Nepal, Bhutan, Pakistan, Afghanistan and even Tajikistan (stopping only at the borders of Safavid Persia and the Khanate of Bukhara). Entire stretches of the Indian subcontinent are overwhelmingly Muslim majority, including the parts that were broken off to form Pakistan and Bangladesh, and modern India still has a huge Muslim minority (only about 15% of the total population, but still accounting for some 180 million+ people, making it the world's largest Muslim minority and one of the largest Muslim populations overall; again it varies by state so about 25% of West Bengal is Muslim, 37% of Punjab is Muslim, and nearly 30% of Assam is Muslim).<br /> <br /> I think its safe to say that the Deva would have had plenty of encounters with the Abrahamic Pantheon. Far more so than the Chinese or Japanese gods. Also, bear in mind that China, India and Japan don't account for all of Asia either. Certainly the Deva may have been represented in parts of Central and Southeast Asia thanks to the spread of Hinduism and later Buddhism, but many smaller, local Pantheons could just as easily have been swallowed up by the Abrahamic Pantheon. I'm thinking of the Philippines and East Timor, which are both overwhelmingly Catholic, but also in Indonesia (the world's largest Muslim nation, though the eastern half of Indonesia is mostly Catholic too), Malaysia, Brunei, Singapore, southern Thailand (Pattani), western Burma (Rakhine state) and even possibly in the Mekong delta (the Cham Kingdom) and the former South Vietnam. South Korea too has a large Christian minority, and indeed Christians have been well placed in the political and business communities; I believe their current President is Christian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1449-zakariya-ali-sher","name":"Zakariya Ali Sher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T02:35:11-07:00","id":124375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zakariya Ali Sher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=124158#post124158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think Christianity is even less than 3% of India's total population, though it is the overwhelming majority in some states (Nagaland is about 90% Christian, and Mizoram is about 86%). Nonetheless, you are forgetting about a much bigger, more important group here: Islam. The Delhi Sultanate was established in 1206, and for centuries onward Muslims ruled much of the Indian subcontinent. At their height, the Mughals controlled almost all of India except a few Hindu kingdoms in the far south, as well as most of modern day Bangladesh, Nepal, Bhutan, Pakistan, Afghanistan and even Tajikistan (stopping only at the borders of Safavid Persia and the Khanate of Bukhara). Entire stretches of the Indian subcontinent are overwhelmingly Muslim majority, including the parts that were broken off to form Pakistan and Bangladesh, and modern India still has a huge Muslim minority (only about 15% of the total population, but still accounting for some 180 million+ people, making it the world's largest Muslim minority and one of the largest Muslim populations overall; again it varies by state so about 25% of West Bengal is Muslim, 37% of Punjab is Muslim, and nearly 30% of Assam is Muslim).<br /> <br /> I think its safe to say that the Deva would have had plenty of encounters with the Abrahamic Pantheon. Far more so than the Chinese or Japanese gods. Also, bear in mind that China, India and Japan don't account for all of Asia either. Certainly the Deva may have been represented in parts of Central and Southeast Asia thanks to the spread of Hinduism and later Buddhism, but many smaller, local Pantheons could just as easily have been swallowed up by the Abrahamic Pantheon. I'm thinking of the Philippines and East Timor, which are both overwhelmingly Catholic, but also in Indonesia (the world's largest Muslim nation, though the eastern half of Indonesia is mostly Catholic too), Malaysia, Brunei, Singapore, southern Thailand (Pattani), western Burma (Rakhine state) and even possibly in the Mekong delta (the Cham Kingdom) and the former South Vietnam. South Korea too has a large Christian minority, and indeed Christians have been well placed in the political and business communities; I believe their current President is Christian.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was 2.9% at the last census I believe, though I am not sure. And as for the Muslims, yes, the Delhi Sultanate and then the Mughals ruled India for a long, prosperous time. The Taj Mahal is proof of that. My point was that despite being under Abrahamic rule for some eight centuries, the population is still 80% Hindu. Less than one-fifth of the population has converted after nearly a millenium. I also agree that the Deva would have had far more interaction with the Abrahamic Pantheon than the other two, I just say that they do not consider them a threat to their own supremacy.<br /> <br /> Also, I apologize if I gave off the wrong impression. Those three definitely do not represent all of Asia, and I never meant to even imply this. I simply noted that their are certain Pantheons that would be good candidates for a Scion setting where the Abrahamics were the opposition, which is the suggestion that started this whole part of the thread, and that there are some Pantheons that would not really care about fighting the Abrahamics because they don't see them as a threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T08:07:04-07:00","id":124505,"title":"","content":"It seems like there are a lot of different ideas and sub-ideas getting folded into this discussion:<br /> <br /> &quot;Abrahamite&quot; as a playable option standing shoulder to shoulder with the other pantheons (the Abrahamite option)<br /> &quot;Abrahamite&quot; as a playable option by turning back the clock and making them not monotheistic (he Canaanite option)<br /> &quot;Abrahamite&quot; as a the opposition, either as another Titan per se or as the primary opposition, replacing the Titans &amp; Titanomachy (the Opposition option)<br /> <br /> Each of them lead to a completely different type of discussion. There is certainly some cross-over possible/probable between the two (all categorization is inexact, we want cores, we get peripheries) and there is definitely avenue to weigh the pros and cons of each side. It's all going to come down to personal preference in the end, but it certainly isn't necessarily a bad idea to keep discussing the obvious &quot;elephant in the room&quot; that Scion decided to avoid.<br /> <br /> Personally, I've used all but the Abrahamite option and variously combined them. In the current game, I'm going with the Canaanites as a pantheon in their own right and have left open the question of how/if/why Abrahamite monotheism is factored in. I definitely don't plan it as being the primary opposition and it's likely to be a non-issue unless the PCs choose to go that way or it makes dramatic sense to address it. (I can see where I could use it for Opposition, but I'm not sure I need or want to go there).<br /> <br /> In previous iterations, I've definitely taken the &quot;Abrahamite&quot; religions are Titan-inspired and they have definitely been a part of the Opposition. Never replacing the other Titans, but definitely on camera. Once as the primary opposition (a re-write of the Order of Divine Glory that was getting orders from two different Titans unknowingly - Aten and Yahweh/Logos, the Titan of (Absolute) Truth). Once as tangential opposition (same sort of thing, but the story was directed at dealing with the annunciation of another Titan altogether... sorta a reminder that &quot;this war is bigger than merely the crap you are dealing with&quot; and a few stern warnings to mind their own business from both their parents and the monotheists - the pantheons had other champions to deal with this issue in those games... compartmentalization of mission parameters). <br /> <br /> In both games, I made sure the Abrahamite-Titan-worshiper weren't completely unsympathetic. Sure most were intolerant assholes, but there were good guys and/or understandable guys and/or &quot;there but for the grace of [the] god[s] go I&quot; guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-03T18:37:47-07:00","id":124902,"title":"","content":"I can definitely get behind the Titan-based Abrahamics, so long as the notion of sympathetic Titans (possibly to the extent of being potential protagonists) gets more play.<br /> <br /> (Really, my core point here is that Abrahamics become much more viable protagonist fodder once <b>Scion</b> breaks away from its one-note \u201call player-characters are scions; all Titans and Titan-spawn are antagonists; and everyone else are Birthrights\u201d stance. Yes, that mode of play should still be available and probably even presented as the default chronicle framework; but it shouldn\u2019t be the <i>only</i> playstyle supported by the game.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-10-2014, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T09:53:53-07:00","id":128331,"title":"","content":"I remember a friend of mine had a pretty interesting idea, or at least I thought it was. <br /> <br /> His idea was that 'God' was the Greater Titan of Spirit. The 'gods' of the Titan consisted of Angels both in Paradise (their Overworld) and the Inferno (their underworld).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T13:53:58-07:00","id":128496,"title":"","content":"Why \u201cSpirit\u201d?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T05:28:30-07:00","id":129813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=124902#post124902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can definitely get behind the Titan-based Abrahamics, so long as the notion of sympathetic Titans (possibly to the extent of being potential protagonists) gets more play.<br /> <br /> (Really, my core point here is that Abrahamics become much more viable protagonist fodder once <b>Scion</b> breaks away from its one-note \u201call player-characters are scions; all Titans and Titan-spawn are antagonists; and everyone else are Borthrights\u201d stance. Yes, that mode of play should still be available and probably even presented as the default chronicle framework; but it shouldn\u2019t be the <i>only</i> playstyle supported by the game.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I mostly agree with that. The problem is only Scion is enough intelligent to work on her own. Titanspawn may be restricted by the Titan's power, no free will because Titanspawns are not part human part Titan. Even if it were possible, they would be definitely stronger than Scion that come from God. Still, don't know why Titanspawn, which are Titan's creation, can be weaker than Scions since they are totally magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T19:05:32-07:00","id":131176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197-abrahamic-pantheon-necro?p=128496#post128496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why \u201cSpirit\u201d?</div> </div> </div> </div> His idea was so that it could take a whole slew of things into account. For one, most Abrahamic-inspired religions (Christianity, Islam, Judaism, and even a few New Age philosophies) put a special emphasis on spiritual matters (a certain angel for a certain virtue, a countering demon in charge of a countering vice). Secondly, he used it to explain why there were so many extremely different religions despite originating with the Abrahamic myth--as the greater Titan of spirit, its form was abstract; it literally appeared differently to different groups of people since its form and character took to reflecting the inherent spiritual outlook of the people it spoke to, despite communicating a similar message to all. Thirdly, considering all the other elements the Titans stood for (time, light, etc.) Spirit seemed as good an element as the rest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T11:11:03-07:00","id":132452,"title":"","content":"What is germain, my conclusion:<br /> <br /> The real question I would bring in the midst of this environment is, how are they formed? For if man is formed out of the body of a god (Kingu) or the remnants of a goddess (Tiamat), or otherwise created out of a divine source that is complete, would the scion not be innately more powerful than the titan spawn who is the conjuration of an aspect, a mere refraction and not a descendant of the divine being?<br /> <br /> What I thought about getting there:<br /> <br /> Between 4016 and 2008 BCE the sun rose in Taurus, set in Scorpio/Aquila, and held its solstice in Leo. During that time a people practiced a naturalistic religion where they dedicated themselves to preserving the purity and integrity of the creation. Their sons became embroiled as hired militias by city states in the Fertile Crescent who preferred watching &quot;savage nomads&quot; die in the opening salvos of their wars over spilling the blood of their own. These young warriors returned to become despots over their homes using the bronze technology of their city state neighbors. In that day one of the gods, Varuna - a god of light in the high Persian Plateau, vanishes and the Lord of Light, Truth, and Wisdom is revealed to the only priest in human history ever to found a religion: Zarathustra. The new prophet proclaimed the Devas and the Asuras/Aesir to be false gods, servants of the Lie. The Lord of Light was served by 7 archangels, lesser angels, and other spirits of ancestors and nature. The Lie was served by greater demons, lesser demons, and all manner of poisonous and corrupting things that bring about unhappiness, disharmony, and death. The son of the Lie was Azi Dahaka the wyrm which is the enemy of the Lord of Light. If we step back and look at this wyrm as it is written about from Ireland to India, per <u>How to Kill a Dragon: Aspects of Indo-European Poetics</u>, by Calvert Watkins and <u>Myth of Invariance: The Origin of the Gods, Mathematics and Music from the RG Veda to Plato</u>, by Ernest G. McClain, we see that the wyrm is the manifestation of cognitive dissonance against the weave of notes (the kosmos, kosmetic, kosmopolis) inspired from the discovery of the connection between all things in creation. During the Babylonian Captivity of Israel, elements of Hapiru ethical monotheism and Persian ethical monotheism fused to become the Pharisaic tradition leading to the Judaism of the Middle Ages, and influencing Christianity and Islam. This dragon cast down from heaven, this J\u00f6rmungandr of the Middle East, is but another face of Leviathan. Yet, the origins of man remain divided by the traditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T19:22:49-07:00","id":137543,"title":"","content":"I just got Scion: Companion, and I noticed something that I was surprised no one said anything about it. There's actually an antagonist group that has connections to the montheistic faith of the Abrahamic religions called The Order of Divine Glory. This group, who is endorsed by the Vatican itself, seeks to convert Scions, and eventually the Gods themselves into the belief of the One God.<br /> <br /> Why didn't someone tell me about this? I thought that White Wolf totally ignored the monotheistic response to Scions. This changes a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T20:44:08-07:00","id":137654,"title":"","content":"Not really. The Order of Divine Glory is essentially \u201cthe Abrahamic faiths are strictly a human invention with little basis in fact\u201d. For those of us who want the Abrahamic faiths to have a stronger basis in fact, the Order is inadequate; for those of us who want the option of Abrahamic protagonists, it\u2019s too inherently antagonistic. <br /> <br /> All that said, it <i>has</i> been mentioned numerous times in this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"